{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019rRMCjNH3N4B3u9UdQZEU1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion gameplay mechanics Healing Touch instruments GUILT operations design review\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion review\",\"url\":\"https://gamesradar.com/trauma-center-second-opinion-review\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion review\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamesradar.com/trauma-center-second-opinion-review/2/\"},{\"title\":\"gamespot.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamespot.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/user-reviews/2200-567980/\"},{\"title\":\"gamespot.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamespot.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/user-reviews/2200-235540/\"},{\"title\":\"Archives by Day\",\"url\":\"https://www.worthplaying.com/article/2006/11/27/reviews/38020-wii-review-trauma-center-second-opinion/\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/3030-7184/\"},{\"title\":\"Monday, August 22, 2022\",\"url\":\"https://ofswordsandjoysticks.blogspot.com/2022/08/game-1231-trauma-center-second-opinion.html\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Trauma_Center_Second_Opinion\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-7184/\"},{\"title\":\"Genre: Simulation\",\"url\":\"https://worthplaying.com/article/2006/11/27/reviews/38020/\"},{\"title\":\"www.giantbomb.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/wd/3030-7184\"},{\"title\":\"Your Account\",\"url\":\"https://www.supercheats.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/full-review/582-minigauntlet/\"},{\"title\":\"trauma center second opinion review preview for the nintendo wii wii\",\"url\":\"https://www.cheatcc.com/articles/trauma-center-second-opinion-review-preview-for-the-nintendo-wii-wii/\"},{\"title\":\"Jump to navigation\",\"url\":\"https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.mobygames.com/game/25357/-/adblurbs/\"},{\"title\":\"Recensione Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://www.everyeye.it/articoli/recensione-trauma-center-second-opinion-6379.html\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://archive.hitsave.org/ark:/78322/12351\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"url\":\"https://games.kikizo.com/reviews/wii/trauma_center_second_opinion.asp\"},{\"title\":\"Trauma Center%7E Second Opinion bc93\",\"url\":\"https://wikipedia.classicistranieri.com/en/articles/s/e/c/Trauma_Center%7E_Second_Opinion_bc93.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up solid coverage of the core mechanics, but little on GUILT or a formal design review.\n\n- **Core loop:** The game uses the features of the Wii Remote and Nunchuck in place of the stylus-based gameplay of the DS game. Its tools include scalpels, stitches, defibrillators, and lasers, among others (bandages, lasers, ultrasounds, hypodermic needles, defibrillators, scalpels, and even stitches). One reviewer found that the analog stick for tool selection speeds up the gameplay from the DS version.\n- **Healing Touch:** Players activate it by drawing a star on-screen using the Wii Remote. Its effect depends on the character. Dr. Stiles' Healing Touch allows him to slow down time, and the cleaner and larger the star, the longer the Healing Touch lasts, and a Touch can only be used once a stage.\n- **Design lineage:** The game is a remake of the game Trauma Center: Under the Knife for the Nintendo DS, although its graphics and mechanics were completely redone to take advantage of the Wii's motion-sensing controls. Additions include a new chapter, tools, and Dr. Nozomi Weaver.\n- **Credits:** Wikipedia lists Daisuke Kanada as director, Katsura Hashino as producer, Masayoshi Suto as designer, and Takaaki Ikeda as programmer (Director(s) | Daisuke Kanada | Producer(s) | Katsura Hashino | Designer(s) | Masayoshi Suto | Programmer(s) | Takaaki Ikeda).\n\n**Gaps:** None of the results describe GUILT in detail. The only mention is a Wikipedia stub heading that points to the Under the Knife article for it. I also found no dedicated design review; the material is mostly consumer reviews and wiki pages. A follow-up search on the GUILT system, or on Under the Knife's GUILT section, would be the next step.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"f7831da3-e78d-4f30-a9f2-e11b9b820639","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:24:08.432Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion gameplay mechanics Healing Touch instruments GUILT operations design review","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KEumQTGPCLcWun5ty7yvsd","content":[{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion review","url":"https://gamesradar.com/trauma-center-second-opinion-review"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion review","url":"https://www.gamesradar.com/trauma-center-second-opinion-review/2/"},{"title":"gamespot.com","url":"https://www.gamespot.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/user-reviews/2200-567980/"},{"title":"gamespot.com","url":"https://www.gamespot.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/user-reviews/2200-235540/"},{"title":"Archives by Day","url":"https://www.worthplaying.com/article/2006/11/27/reviews/38020-wii-review-trauma-center-second-opinion/"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://giantbomb.com/trauma-center-second-opinion/3030-7184/"},{"title":"Monday, August 22, 2022","url":"https://ofswordsandjoysticks.blogspot.com/2022/08/game-1231-trauma-center-second-opinion.html"},{"title":"Trauma Center: Second Opinion","url":"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Trauma_Center_Second_Opinion"},{