{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9KouSEUQwmxTsoNNmH8Dy","type":"tool_result","content":"# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when Michael explicitly asks,\n  for a major update: push with `deploymentEnabled` set to `true` (that push\n  deploys; check it reaches READY), then set it back to `false` in the next\n  commit, which does not deploy.\n- Work on `main`. If a branch is ever needed, merge it into main and delete\n  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\n  branch, an unpushed commit, a stash, or an open PR behind.\n- Before starting work, run `git fetch --prune` and look at\n  `gh pr list`. Anything open gets resolved first.\n\n## Pull requests from others\n\nDecide each one; do not let it sit. Accept it (merge to main, delete the\nbranch), reject it (close it with a one-line reason), or replace it (close\nit, and land a better version on main that says which PR it replaces).\n\n## Keep it simple and clean\n\n- No dependencies, no build step, no generated files committed\n  (`data/games.json` is gitignored and rebuilt by `scripts/scan.mjs`).\n- Run `pnpm test` (or `node --test \"scripts/**/*.test.mjs\"`) before\n  committing code.\n- Delete what is no longer used instead of leaving it around.\n\n## When something goes wrong\n\nRoll back rather than leave half-finished work. Revert the commit\n(`git revert`) or restore the last good state and push that, so main is\nalways a working wall. Say what was rolled back and why.\n------\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md:90:| Brick Bowl Turbo | `brick-bowl-turbo-standalone.html` | `original-Brick-Bowl-Turbo-2026-09-28-model-unknown.html` | 5.2 MB |\ncouch/index.html:11:    <title>Couch — AI Hub</title>\ncouch/index.html:27:    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/css/couch.css\" />\ncouch/index.html:28:    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/css/couch-page.css\" />\ncouch/index.html:29:    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/css/couch-find.css\" />\ncouch/index.html:34:    <div class=\"couch\" id=\"couch\">\ncouch/index.html:48:    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/assets/js/couch/app.js\"></script>\ncouch/index.html:51:        The Couch needs JavaScript. The games themselves are plain HTML files in\ndocs/session-hub.md:176:| game | `answer` | `answer`: `ready` or `more` | on its own card, after the welcome, until `start` |\ndocs/curation-2026-09-24.md:165:| Moonjunk Squadron — Crater City 9 | `moonjunk-squadron` | `moonjunk-squadron-standalone.html` |  |\nREADME.md:196:in the Couch, with its own screenshots and URL for comparison. Its genre and\nREADME.md:242:pnpm test         # parsers, layout rules, zip reading, search and filters, Couch and Catalogue logic\nREADME.md:267:If a game misbehaves in a frame, *Open on its own page* in its Details drawer\nREADME.md:315:(**Wall · Friends · Couch · Catalogue · Atlas · Timeline · Deck**) leads to six more, built over the same games\nREADME.md:326:record), on the Couch's hero and game page, and on the Deck's card. Each of\nREADME.md:344:  ghosts* (ghost), *Same start, side by side* (parallel) — and *Couch co-op*,\nREADME.md:353:  computer*, and *Practise alone* in the hub's player. A couch co-op game has\nREADME.md:356:### The Couch — `/couch`\nREADME.md:364:model that made three or more, *Originals*, *Couch co-op* (several players on\nREADME.md:386:While a game runs the Couch claims nothing, keys and buttons alike. With no\nREADME.md:422:record, **F** favourites, **O** opens a game on its own page, **/** writes a\nREADME.md:491:awards, and outside a session the game plays exactly as it always would. What\nREADME.md:518:each with a player leaving, then the game on its own. `--record` writes the\nREADME.md:564:  on its own compared with the original.\nREADME.md:800:couch/            the Couch: a page of its own, over the same library\nREADME.md:821:  couch/          rails, pad and keys, the game page, search (logic tested)\nREADME.md:903:ordinary wall, Couch and Catalogue search. Audio formats include voice and sound\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28.md:141:| City Companion — Standalone Three.js Career Sim | `original-City-Companion-Standalone-Three.js-Career-Sim-2026-08-21-model-unknown.html` | 2.1 MB |\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28.md:144:| Datecraft — Standalone | `original-Datecraft-Standalone-2026-08-21-model-unknown.html` | 22.8 MB |\ndocs/curation-2026-09-28.md:151:| Homefront Hearts — Standalone Beta | `original-Homefront-Hearts-Standalone-Beta-2026-08-22-model-unknown.html` | 4.8 MB |\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:154:| 5 Couch and remote couch | Couch co-op on one screen stays each game's own (up to four controllers), unchanged. Remote couch co-op is **pinned**: friends far away would need the host's screen streamed to them as video |\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:226:   progress and a seeded start expected; and the game on its own compared\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:398:  agent on its own copy of the game, spend capped, every failure put back);\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:479:  frames (the splash's pad buttons, Create + Options, the Couch's pad\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:504:- Remote couch co-op: friends far away playing a game made for one screen, on\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:507:  Couch co-op in one room is the game's own and is unaffected.\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:529:- **Up to four players locally, controller first**: welcome. Couch co-op in\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:530:  one room is the game's own; remote couch co-op is pinned.\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:542:| 1 | Decisions 3 and 4 | Decided Oct 29: state, not video, and no video 