nes load, by id: their text (Vite's `?raw` import), file and material swaps (the level\n113-   * entry's `materials`); registered unless already.\n114-   */\n115-  levels?: Readonly<Record<string, { text: string; file?: string; materials?: Readonly<Record<string, string>> }>>;\n116-  /** Replays the page offers by name (`?replay=<name>`): name → its text, loaded when asked for. */\n117-  replays?: Readonly<Record<string, () => Promise<string>>>;\n118-  /** The query to read (`location.search`). */\n119-  search?: string;\n120-  /** The hash to read (`location.hash`): a gallery deep link, `#gallery/<kind>/<id>` (engine/app/routes.ts). */\n121-  hash?: string;\n122-  /** Where scenes, levels, components, settings and materials are declared (the shared registry). */\n123-  registry?: Registry;\n124-  /** Where errors and advice go (the shared log). */\n125-  log?: Log;\n126-  /** The page's touch buttons, a `touchlayout` id (engine/ui/touch.ts); without it, only the touch stick shows. */\n127-  touchLayout?: string;\n128-  /**\n129-   * The action map the devices read (`actionMap:thirdPerson` by default): its actions are the intents' buttons. A\n130-   * function gives the map for the camera now (its code, `cam3=first,…`), so each camera mode has its own (WP 13.9).\n131-   */\n132-  actionMap?: string | ((camera: string) => string);\n133-  /** A view action of the map pressed (its `view`: a camera switch, a view's turn), as it happens (WP 13.9). */\n134-  onView?: (action: string) => void;\n135-  /** Opens the page's menu, called after the touch menu button has paused the game. */\n136-  onMenu?: () => void;\n137-  /** The page's own presentation (its sound): called once per drawn frame, after the draw, with the run to read. */\n138-  onFrame?: (frame: EngineFrame) => void;\n139-  /** Where the bindings are kept across sessions (`createStore`, engine/app/store.ts); in memory without it. */\n140-  store?: Store;\n141-  /** True while the page's front end holds the devic