{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9Zn7Di2cWPN5LfPgfS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LpjmQRebtAXMe1gv4thtXF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,100p engine/app/view.ts; echo ....; grep -n \"stage\\.\\|createStage\\|interface.*View\\b\\|scene\" engine/app/view.ts | head -50; echo ....; sed -n 1,70p engine/gfx/stage.ts; grep -n \"export \" engine/gfx/stage.ts | head -30","description":"Read how the view and stage build what gets drawn"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14988,"cache_read_input_tokens":208208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14988},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"ab4855bd-9b67-4266-84ff-482fcfd179bd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:27:19.877Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9Zmq61ZqguxqME6Tn4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LpjmQRebtAXMe1gv4thtXF":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/.scratch/engine && sed -n 1,100p engine/app/view.ts; echo ....; grep -n \"stage\\.\\|createStage\\|interface.*View\\b\\|scene\" engine/app/view.ts | head -50; echo ....; sed -n 1,70p engine/gfx/stage.ts; grep -n \"export \" engine/gfx/stage.ts | head -30","description":"Read how the view and stage build what gets drawn"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01LpjmQRebtAXMe1gv4thtXF":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/.scratch/engine"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpjmQRebtAXMe1gv4thtXF","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The view of a run (PLAN.md §6.4's `view.update`, §8.3, WP 2.7): what a running scene looks like, built\n * without a GPU, so a page draws it and `createHeadless({ view: true })` dumps it in Node. `createRunView` makes the\n * stage of the scene (engine/gfx/stage.ts: lights, the level's meshes, actors as puppets, a stand-in per other placed\n * entity) and its camera (engine/gfx/cameras: a camera code, `cam=iso` by default), and keeps both in step with the\n * run: `stepped()` after every sim step reads where the entities are, `frame({ alpha, dt, aspect })` puts every\n * puppet and stand-in `alpha` of the way between its last two steps and moves the camera by a rendered frame, then\n * draws the crowd bodies as that camera sees them (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts: its level of detail and culling; after\n * steps with no frame, `dump` draws them first), then moves the stage's effects on by the frame (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts:\n * the world's new events burst, its bolts, telegraphs and trails drawn, unless the view setting `gfx.effects` is off;\n * the page shakes its camera by them while it draws), returning what to draw (`{ scene, camera, alpha }`,\n * engine/gfx/renderer.ts's `FrameView`). A frame that finds `gfx.effects` switched since the last read reads the\n * entities again first, so a flying bolt is the effects' or its stand-in from that frame, with or without a step.\n *\n * The camera is a rig (engine/gfx/cameras/rig.ts: a code's camera, blends, the view effects, the settings `cam.*`) that\n * follows the player (WP 3.10): the first player actor's feet as the frame draws them, else the level's middle; so does\n * the stage's sky (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts, flickering at the frames' time, WP 7.8), and the level entry's looks (its\n * swaps, rooms' floors and recipes: `levelLooks`) reach the stage. The rig also gets the sim's read-only `QueryView` in\n * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n * head socket) and what he does each step (`cameraPlayer`); first person draws his arms by their own lens and hides his\n * body, its shadow kept (engine/gfx/viewmodel/, WP 13.12; `cameraInfo().culled`, `.arms`); hard landings shake the\n * screen. Following a player, the cutaways run (the stage's `frame`); `aim(rule, devices)` is his aim from the camera\n * drawn last (WP 13.9, engine/input/aim.ts: the centre's ray through the sim's queries, his body skipped, or the\n * pointer's onto his floor), which the page's input records. `restarted()` after the run starts again (a new seed, a\n * replay) or its world changes between steps (a restore, a dev action) reads the entities afresh: the stand-ins and\n * bolts snap to them, so no dump, shot or frame shows the places they had before. The effects forget what ran only for\n * a new world, read from its first event; the same world keeps its trace read, so no event plays twice.\n *\n * The level comes from the scene's `level` id (engine/world/level/level.ts), registered before the view starts\n * (`APP_NO_LEVEL`), the terrain from its `terrain` id (WP 10.5), the site from its `site` id (WP 13.15). Cameras are\n * view state: switching one (`setCamera(code)`, `__engine.camera.set`; `{ blend: true }` blends it in), moving it on\n * headless (`advance`) or at a replay's step drawing no frame (`carry`) never reaches the sim. Invariants: presentation\n * only: it reads the run, never writes it (its `QueryView` has no way in); one stage per view, a camera per projection.\n *\n * @example\n * // const view = createRunView({ run: () => session, registry, materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n * // view.stepped(); // after each sim step; then gfx.frame(view.frame({ alpha, dt, aspect }))\n * // view.setCamera('cam=topdown').describe; // what the camera now shows, in words\n * @see engine/app/view.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { BoostedOrthographicCamera, BoostedPerspectiveCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/boost';\nimport { cameraPlayer, type CameraPlayer } from '../gfx/cameras/effects';\nimport { createCameraPair, type AnyCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/place';\nimport type { CameraInput, CameraPose, Vec3 } from '../gfx/cameras/pose';\nimport { createCameraRig, rigOptions } from '../gfx/cameras/rig';\nimport type { MaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\nimport type { FrameView } from '../gfx/renderer';\nimport { aimPoint, type AimDevices, type AimRule } from '../input/aim';\nimport { dumpScene, type DumpOptions } from '../gfx/sceneDump';\nimport { levelLooks } from '../gfx/level/runs';\nimport { createStage, type Stage } from '../gfx/stage';\nimport type { FirstPersonParts } from '../gfx/viewmodel/body';\nimport { armsLens } from '../gfx/viewmodel/lens';\nimport { queryViewOf, type QueryView } from '../sim/queryView';\nimport { shutDoors } from '../sim/doors';\nimport { daytimeOf } from '../sim/lights';\nimport { CHEST } from '../sim/weapons';\nimport type { Session } from '../sim/session';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\nimport { getSite } from '../world/site';\nimport { getTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const VIEW_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n  APP_NO_LEVEL: {\n    template: 'the scene {scene} loads the level {level}, which is not registered, so its view cannot be built',\n    fix: \"register the level's text before the view starts: in a page, import text from './levels/<name>.txt?raw' and call defineLevel('{level}', { text, file }); in Node, read the file and do the same\",\n  },\n  APP_NO_VIEW: {\n    template: '{member} needs the scene drawn as a view, and this engine has none',\n    fix: 'start it with createHeadless({ scene, view: true }) in Node; a page always has one',\n  },\n});\n\n/** The camera code a view starts with when none is given. */\nexport const DEFAULT_CAMERA = 'cam=iso';\n\n/** The aspect a view frames for when nothing draws it (headless): 16:9, the e2e viewport's. */\nexport const HEADLESS_ASPECT = 16 / 9;\n\n/** A frame `advance` moves the camera on by, real seconds: a 60 Hz page's. */\nexport const ADVANCE_FRAME = 1 / 60;\n\n/** What `camera.get()` and `camera.set(code)` return: the camera as a code, in words, and its pose. */\nexport interface CameraInfo {\n  code: string;\n  describe: string;\n  type: string;\n  /** The heading it looks along, rad: the intents' `cam`. */\n  yaw: number;\n  pose: CameraPose;\n  /** First person: the player's joints whose body parts it hides from itself, and the ones his arms show. */\n  culled?: string[];\n  arms?: string[];\n}\n\n/** What a view is made from. */\n....\n2: * @file The view of a run (PLAN.md §6.4's `view.update`, §8.3, WP 2.7): what a running scene looks like, built\n4: * stage of the scene (engine/gfx/stage.ts: lights, the level's meshes, actors as puppets, a stand-in per other placed\n11: * the page shakes its camera by them while it draws), returning what to draw (`{ scene, camera, alpha }`,\n18: * swaps, rooms' floors and recipes: `levelLooks`) reach the stage. The rig also gets the sim's read-only `QueryView` in\n19: * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n29: * The level comes from the scene's `level` id (engine/world/level/level.ts), registered before the view starts\n51:import { dumpScene, type DumpOptions } from '../gfx/sceneDump';\n53:import { createStage, type Stage } from '../gfx/stage';\n69:    template: 'the scene {scene} loads the level {level}, which is not registered, so its view cannot be built',\n73:    template: '{member} needs the scene drawn as a view, and this engine has none',\n74:    fix: 'start it with createHeadless({ scene, view: true }) in Node; a page always has one',\n104:  /** Where the scene's level and the component kinds are declared. */\n123:export interface RunView {\n137:   * lit by the hour of the scene's clock (engine/sim/lights.ts) and lighting the props' lamps that are on (WP 13.23).\n153:  /** The stage as text (engine/gfx/sceneDump.ts). */\n157:  /** Frees the stage. */\n171:  const scene = options.run().scene;\n173:  if (scene.level !== undefined && !known(scene.level)) {\n174:    throw codeError('APP_NO_LEVEL', { scene: scene.id, level: scene.level });\n176:  const level = scene.level === undefined ? null : getLevel(scene.level, registry);\n177:  const looks = scene.level === undefined ? {} : levelLooks(registry, scene.level);\n178:  const terrain = scene.terrain === undefined ? null : getTerrain(scene.terrain, registry);\n179:  const site = scene.site === undefined ? null : getSite(scene.site, registry);\n181:  const stage = createStage({ level, terrain, site, materials: options.materials, registry, log: options.log, fxRng, ...looks }); // prettier-ignore\n190:    const changed = stage.fx.effects.enabled !== enabled;\n191:    stage.fx.effects.enabled = enabled;\n197:    stage.capture([]);\n198:    stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n213:    stage.crowd.draw(alpha, drawn);\n220:    if (!run.scene.physics) return undefined;\n240:    shut = run.scene.physics ? shutDoors(run.world, registry) : [];\n242:    if (entity) stage.actors.look(entity.id, look ? { yaw: look[0], pitch: look[1], aiming: doing?.aiming ?? aiming } : null); // prettier-ignore\n247:      stage.actors.look(other.id, along ? { yaw: along[0], pitch: along[1], aiming: false } : null);\n262:    const player = stage.actors.player();\n263:    const feet = player?.feet ?? stage.centre;\n273:    stage.fx.effects.shake.add(rig.shake());\n276:    parts = stage.actors.firstPerson(first);\n277:    const player = stage.actors.player();\n279:    if (player) stage.frame(pose, player.feet, { fade, view: rig.camera.type === 'view' });\n302:      stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n303:      stage.draw((alpha = 1)); // the latest state until a frame interpolates: what a headless dump shows\n312:        stage.fx.reset();\n317:      stage.draw((alpha = 1));\n326:      stage.draw((alpha = frame.alpha));\n329:      const [hour, lamps] = [daytimeOf(options.run().world), stage.props.lights()]; // WP 13.23\n330:      stage.sky.update({ camera: drawn, focus: stage.actors.player()?.feet ?? stage.centre, time, hour, lamps });\n332:      stage.fx.frame(frame.dt, drawn, options.run().world.events.trace());\n333:      return { scene: stage.scene, camera: drawn, alpha: frame.alpha, ...(stage.fx.gpuParticles ? { particles: stage.fx.gpuParticles } : {}) }; // prettier-ignore\n338:      if (!stage.actors.player()) return undefined;\n344:      const motion = (options.run().world.get(stage.actors.player()!.id) as { motion?: { stance?: string } } | undefined)?.motion; // prettier-ignore\n....\n/**\n * @file The stage (PLAN.md §6.4's view, §9.0, WP 2.7): a running scene's presentation graph, built from plain data with\n * no GPU, so a page draws it and a headless engine dumps it (`createHeadless({ view: true })`). `createStage` makes a\n * three.js `Scene` with a sky colour, the stage's ground (engine/gfx/stageGround.ts: a textured plane under the level\n * reaching well past it, or a frame round a terrain, `stage/ground`), its lights (`sky`, engine/gfx/stageSky.ts: a\n * hemisphere light and a sun fitted to the level, or the sky a look names), the level's meshes by runs\n * (engine/gfx/level/runs.ts: `level:room/wall@0,0-15,0`, each wall run on its own in the ID pass, with the level's\n * swaps), the terrain's chunks (engine/gfx/terrain.ts, WP 10.5: they stand for the ground, and the sun fits them when\n * there is no level) and one stand-in per placeable entity.\n *\n * Actors with an animator draw themselves as puppets (engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts, WP 3.10: `actors`), props standing\n * in the scene (`sceneProp`, engine/sim/props.ts) as their props (engine/gfx/stageProps.ts, WP 4.6: `props`), crowd\n * bodies (`crowdBody`) through a crowd (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts, WP 5.7: `crowd`), which the view draws once the\n * frame's camera is placed (`crowd.draw(alpha, camera)`), rides as themselves (engine/gfx/stageRides.ts, WP 13.7:\n * `rides`), and projectiles as bolts (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts, WP 6.7: `fx`, with telegraphs, trails and bursts, handed\n * each frame by the view), and the guns in the actors' hands as props (WP 13.20). Stand-ins: any other entity is drawn\n * as a box when one of its components declares `x` and `z` as numbers in metres (`placeableKinds`, asked of the\n * entries, never of a name: engine/gfx/standIns.ts). The first such component in registry order places it: `x`, `y` (the box's bottom, 0 by\n * default) and `z`, `yaw` (rad), `size` (the box's side, m; 0.5 by default) and `material` (a material library id;\n * `material:default` otherwise). A stand-in is named `<component>#<id>` with `userData.entity`, so the ID pass and the\n * inspector name its entity. `capture(entities, dt)` after each sim step keeps the last two places; `draw(alpha)` puts\n * every stand-in, puppet and prop `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last (§6.4's interpolation).\n *\n * The level's cutaway (engine/gfx/cutaway.ts, its fade taking the rides too) is made when a player first stands on\n * it, never without one; the view runs it as it follows the player (`frame`), with the cut by storey in a classic view\n * (storeyCut.ts) and a site's per structure (engine/gfx/stageSite.ts), the props on a storey it takes off with it.\n *\n * Warm-up: `register(warmup)` registers the ground, the level meshes, the terrain's every level of detail, the\n * cutaway's twins, the puppets, the props' and the crowd's batches and the stand-ins, and adds the stand-ins' looks\n * (side and material), the puppets' builds, the crowd's looks and whether there are a cutaway and props to the shader\n * key, so a new look makes the next frame warm up first instead of stalling.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads sim data and never writes it (doctrine: WebGPU only); every object it makes\n * is under `scene`; equal inputs make equal graphs; materials belong to the library and are never disposed here.\n * @example\n * // const stage = createStage({ level: getLevel('level:room'), materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n * // stage.capture(world.query('mover'));\n * // stage.draw(0.5); // halfway between the last two steps; then renderer.render(stage.scene, camera)\n * @see engine/gfx/stage.test.ts\n */\nimport { BufferGeometry, Color, Group, Mesh, Scene, type Material, type Object3D } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { Rng } from '../core/rng';\nimport type { QueryView } from '../sim/queryView';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport type { CompiledLevel } from '../world/level/types';\nimport type { Site } from '../world/site';\nimport type { Terrain } from '../world/terrain';\nimport type { CameraPose, Vec3 } from './cameras/pose';\nimport { createCutaway, type Cutaway } from './cutaway';\nimport { boxGeometry } from './geometry/box';\nimport type { LevelMeshes } from './level/meshes';\nimport type { LevelRecipe } from './level/recipes';\nimport type { DoorLeaf } from '../world/level/doorways';\nimport { runMeshes } from './level/runs';\nimport { createActorPuppets, type ActorPuppets } from './puppets/actors';\nimport { createStageCrowd, type StageCrowd } from './stageCrowd';\nimport { createStageFx, type StageFx } from './stageFx';\nimport { createStageProps, type StageProps } from './stageProps';\nimport { createStageRides, RIDE_KINDS, type StageRides } from './stageRides';\nimport { createStageShells, type StageShells } from './stageShells';\nimport { createStageSite, type StageSite } from './stageSite';\nimport { groundMesh } from './stageGround';\nimport type { FeatureReport } from './features';\nimport { createStageSky, type StageSky } from './stageSky';\nimport { placeableKinds, placeOf, type StandInPlace } from './standIns';\nimport { aboveStorey, createStoreyCut, cutPlace } from './storeyCut';\nimport { createTerrainMeshes, type TerrainMeshes } from './terrain';\nimport type { Warmup } from './warmup';\n73:export interface StageOptions {\n99:export interface Stage {\n166:export function createStage(options: StageOptions): Stage {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"cf7b62ed-9deb-4dd5-951a-444bca2681b1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:27:20.019Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The view of a run (PLAN.md §6.4's `view.update`, §8.3, WP 2.7): what a running scene looks like, built\n * without a GPU, so a page draws it and `createHeadless({ view: true })` dumps it in Node. `createRunView` makes the\n * stage of the scene (engine/gfx/stage.ts: lights, the level's meshes, actors as puppets, a stand-in per other placed\n * entity) and its camera (engine/gfx/cameras: a camera code, `cam=iso` by default), and keeps both in step with the\n * run: `stepped()` after every sim step reads where the entities are, `frame({ alpha, dt, aspect })` puts every\n * puppet and stand-in `alpha` of the way between its last two steps and moves the camera by a rendered frame, then\n * draws the crowd bodies as that camera sees them (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts: its level of detail and culling; after\n * steps with no frame, `dump` draws them first), then moves the stage's effects on by the frame (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts:\n * the world's new events burst, its bolts, telegraphs and trails drawn, unless the view setting `gfx.effects` is off;\n * the page shakes its camera by them while it draws), returning what to draw (`{ scene, camera, alpha }`,\n * engine/gfx/renderer.ts's `FrameView`). A frame that finds `gfx.effects` switched since the last read reads the\n * entities again first, so a flying bolt is the effects' or its stand-in from that frame, with or without a step.\n *\n * The camera is a rig (engine/gfx/cameras/rig.ts: a code's camera, blends, the view effects, the settings `cam.*`) that\n * follows the player (WP 3.10): the first player actor's feet as the frame draws them, else the level's middle; so does\n * the stage's sky (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts, flickering at the frames' time, WP 7.8), and the level entry's looks (its\n * swaps, rooms' floors and recipes: `levelLooks`) reach the stage. The rig also gets the sim's read-only `QueryView` in\n * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n * head socket) and what he does each step (`cameraPlayer`); first person draws his arms by their own lens and hides his\n * body, its shadow kept (engine/gfx/viewmodel/, WP 13.12; `cameraInfo().culled`, `.arms`); hard landings shake the\n * screen. Following a player, the cutaways run (the stage's `frame`); `aim(rule, devices)` is his aim from the camera\n * drawn last (WP 13.9, engine/input/aim.ts: the centre's ray through the sim's queries, his body skipped, or the\n * pointer's onto his floor), which the page's input records. `restarted()` after the run starts again (a new seed, a\n * replay) or its world changes between steps (a restore, a dev action) reads the entities afresh: the stand-ins and\n * bolts snap to them, so no dump, shot or frame shows the places they had before. The effects forget what ran only for\n * a new world, read from its first event; the same world keeps its trace read, so no event plays twice.\n *\n * The level comes from the scene's `level` id (engine/world/level/level.ts), registered before the view starts\n * (`APP_NO_LEVEL`), the terrain from its `terrain` id (WP 10.5), the site from its `site` id (WP 13.15). Cameras are\n * view state: switching one (`setCamera(code)`, `__engine.camera.set`; `{ blend: true }` blends it in), moving it on\n * headless (`advance`) or at a replay's step drawing no frame (`carry`) never reaches the sim. Invariants: presentation\n * only: it reads the run, never writes it (its `QueryView` has no way in); one stage per view, a camera per projection.\n *\n * @example\n * // const view = createRunView({ run: () => session, registry, materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n * // view.stepped(); // after each sim step; then gfx.frame(view.frame({ alpha, dt, aspect }))\n * // view.setCamera('cam=topdown').describe; // what the camera now shows, in words\n * @see engine/app/view.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { BoostedOrthographicCamera, BoostedPerspectiveCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/boost';\nimport { cameraPlayer, type CameraPlayer } from '../gfx/cameras/effects';\nimport { createCameraPair, type AnyCamera } from '../gfx/cameras/place';\nimport type { CameraInput, CameraPose, Vec3 } from '../gfx/cameras/pose';\nimport { createCameraRig, rigOptions } from '../gfx/cameras/rig';\nimport type { MaterialLibrary } from '../gfx/materials/library';\nimport type { FrameView } from '../gfx/renderer';\nimport { aimPoint, type AimDevices, type AimRule } from '../input/aim';\nimport { dumpScene, type DumpOptions } from '../gfx/sceneDump';\nimport { levelLooks } from '../gfx/level/runs';\nimport { createStage, type Stage } from '../gfx/stage';\nimport type { FirstPersonParts } from '../gfx/viewmodel/body';\nimport { armsLens } from '../gfx/viewmodel/lens';\nimport { queryViewOf, type QueryView } from '../sim/queryView';\nimport { shutDoors } from '../sim/doors';\nimport { daytimeOf } from '../sim/lights';\nimport { CHEST } from '../sim/weapons';\nimport type { Session } from '../sim/session';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\nimport { getSite } from '../world/site';\nimport { getTerrain } from '../world/terrain';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const VIEW_CODES = defineCodes('app', {\n  APP_NO_LEVEL: {\n    template: 'the scene {scene} loads the level {level}, which is not registered, so its view cannot be built',\n    fix: \"register the level's text before the view starts: in a page, import text from './levels/<name>.txt?raw' and call defineLevel('{level}', { text, file }); in Node, read the file and do the same\",\n  },\n  APP_NO_VIEW: {\n    template: '{member} needs the scene drawn as a view, and this engine has none',\n    fix: 'start it with createHeadless({ scene, view: true }) in Node; a page always has one',\n  },\n});\n\n/** The camera code a view starts with when none is given. */\nexport const DEFAULT_CAMERA = 'cam=iso';\n\n/** The aspect a view frames for when nothing draws it (headless): 16:9, the e2e viewport's. */\nexport const HEADLESS_ASPECT = 16 / 9;\n\n/** A frame `advance` moves the camera on by, real seconds: a 60 Hz page's. */\nexport const ADVANCE_FRAME = 1 / 60;\n\n/** What `camera.get()` and `camera.set(code)` return: the camera as a code, in words, and its pose. */\nexport interface CameraInfo {\n  code: string;\n  describe: string;\n  type: string;\n  /** The heading it looks along, rad: the intents' `cam`. */\n  yaw: number;\n  pose: CameraPose;\n  /** First person: the player's joints whose body parts it hides from itself, and the ones his arms show. */\n  culled?: string[];\n  arms?: string[];\n}\n\n/** What a view is made from. */\n....\n2: * @file The view of a run (PLAN.md §6.4's `view.update`, §8.3, WP 2.7): what a running scene looks like, built\n4: * stage of the scene (engine/gfx/stage.ts: lights, the level's meshes, actors as puppets, a stand-in per other placed\n11: * the page shakes its camera by them while it draws), returning what to draw (`{ scene, camera, alpha }`,\n18: * swaps, rooms' floors and recipes: `levelLooks`) reach the stage. The rig also gets the sim's read-only `QueryView` in\n19: * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n29: * The level comes from the scene's `level` id (engine/world/level/level.ts), registered before the view starts\n51:import { dumpScene, type DumpOptions } from '../gfx/sceneDump';\n53:import { createStage, type Stage } from '../gfx/stage';\n69:    template: 'the scene {scene} loads the level {level}, which is not registered, so its view cannot be built',\n73:    template: '{member} needs the scene drawn as a view, and this engine has none',\n74:    fix: 'start it with createHeadless({ scene, view: true }) in Node; a page always has one',\n104:  /** Where the scene's level and the component kinds are declared. */\n123:export interface RunView {\n137:   * lit by the hour of the scene's clock (engine/sim/lights.ts) and lighting the props' lamps that are on (WP 13.23).\n153:  /** The stage as text (engine/gfx/sceneDump.ts). */\n157:  /** Frees the stage. */\n171:  const scene = options.run().scene;\n173:  if (scene.level !== undefined && !known(scene.level)) {\n174:    throw codeError('APP_NO_LEVEL', { scene: scene.id, level: scene.level });\n176:  const level = scene.level === undefined ? null : getLevel(scene.level, registry);\n177:  const looks = scene.level === undefined ? {} : levelLooks(registry, scene.level);\n178:  const terrain = scene.terrain === undefined ? null : getTerrain(scene.terrain, registry);\n179:  const site = scene.site === undefined ? null : getSite(scene.site, registry);\n181:  const stage = createStage({ level, terrain, site, materials: options.materials, registry, log: options.log, fxRng, ...looks }); // prettier-ignore\n190:    const changed = stage.fx.effects.enabled !== enabled;\n191:    stage.fx.effects.enabled = enabled;\n197:    stage.capture([]);\n198:    stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n213:    stage.crowd.draw(alpha, drawn);\n220:    if (!run.scene.physics) return undefined;\n240:    shut = run.scene.physics ? shutDoors(run.world, registry) : [];\n242:    if (entity) stage.actors.look(entity.id, look ? { yaw: look[0], pitch: look[1], aiming: doing?.aiming ?? aiming } : null); // prettier-ignore\n247:      stage.actors.look(other.id, along ? { yaw: along[0], pitch: along[1], aiming: false } : null);\n262:    const player = stage.actors.player();\n263:    const feet = player?.feet ?? stage.centre;\n273:    stage.fx.effects.shake.add(rig.shake());\n276:    parts = stage.actors.firstPerson(first);\n277:    const player = stage.actors.player();\n279:    if (player) stage.frame(pose, player.feet, { fade, view: rig.camera.type === 'view' });\n302:      stage.capture(placed(run, stage.kinds), run.world.dt, queries());\n303:      stage.draw((alpha = 1)); // the latest state until a frame interpolates: what a headless dump shows\n312:        stage.fx.reset();\n317:      stage.draw((alpha = 1));\n326:      stage.draw((alpha = frame.alpha));\n329:      const [hour, lamps] = [daytimeOf(options.run().world), stage.props.lights()]; // WP 13.23\n330:      stage.sky.update({ camera: drawn, focus: stage.actors.player()?.feet ?? stage.centre, time, hour, lamps });\n332:      stage.fx.frame(frame.dt, drawn, options.run().world.events.trace());\n333:      return { scene: stage.scene, camera: drawn, alpha: frame.alpha, ...(stage.fx.gpuParticles ? { particles: stage.fx.gpuParticles } : {}) }; // prettier-ignore\n338:      if (!stage.actors.player()) return undefined;\n344:      const motion = (options.run().world.get(stage.actors.player()!.id) as { motion?: { stance?: string } } | undefined)?.motion; // prettier-ignore\n....\n/**\n * @file The stage (PLAN.md §6.4's view, §9.0, WP 2.7): a running scene's presentation graph, built from plain data with\n * no GPU, so a page draws it and a headless engine dumps it (`createHeadless({ view: true })`). `createStage` makes a\n * three.js `Scene` with a sky colour, the stage's ground (engine/gfx/stageGround.ts: a textured plane under the level\n * reaching well past it, or a frame round a terrain, `stage/ground`), its lights (`sky`, engine/gfx/stageSky.ts: a\n * hemisphere light and a sun fitted to the level, or the sky a look names), the level's meshes by runs\n * (engine/gfx/level/runs.ts: `level:room/wall@0,0-15,0`, each wall run on its own in the ID pass, with the level's\n * swaps), the terrain's chunks (engine/gfx/terrain.ts, WP 10.5: they stand for the ground, and the sun fits them when\n * there is no level) and one stand-in per placeable entity.\n *\n * Actors with an animator draw themselves as puppets (engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts, WP 3.10: `actors`), props standing\n * in the scene (`sceneProp`, engine/sim/props.ts) as their props (engine/gfx/stageProps.ts, WP 4.6: `props`), crowd\n * bodies (`crowdBody`) through a crowd (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts, WP 5.7: `crowd`), which the view draws once the\n * frame's camera is placed (`crowd.draw(alpha, camera)`), rides as themselves (engine/gfx/stageRides.ts, WP 13.7:\n * `rides`), and projectiles as bolts (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts, WP 6.7: `fx`, with telegraphs, trails and bursts, handed\n * each frame by the view), and the guns in the actors' hands as props (WP 13.20). Stand-ins: any other entity is drawn\n * as a box when one of its components declares `x` and `z` as numbers in metres (`placeableKinds`, asked of the\n * entries, never of a name: engine/gfx/standIns.ts). The first such component in registry order places it: `x`, `y` (the box's bottom, 0 by\n * default) and `z`, `yaw` (rad), `size` (the box's side, m; 0.5 by default) and `material` (a material library id;\n * `material:default` otherwise). A stand-in is named `<component>#<id>` with `userData.entity`, so the ID pass and the\n * inspector name its entity. `capture(entities, dt)` after each sim step keeps the last two places; `draw(alpha)` puts\n * every stand-in, puppet and prop `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last (§6.4's interpolation).\n *\n * The level's cutaway (engine/gfx/cutaway.ts, its fade taking the rides too) is made when a player first stands on\n * it, never without one; the view runs it as it follows the player (`frame`), with the cut by storey in a classic view\n * (storeyCut.ts) and a site's per structure (engine/gfx/stageSite.ts), the props on a storey it takes off with it.\n *\n * Warm-up: `register(warmup)` registers the ground, the level meshes, the terrain's every level of detail, the\n * cutaway's twins, the puppets, the props' and the crowd's batches and the stand-ins, and adds the stand-ins' looks\n * (side and material), the puppets' builds, the crowd's looks and whether there are a cutaway and props to the shader\n * key, so a new look makes the next frame warm up first instead of stalling.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads sim data and never writes it (doctrine: WebGPU only); every object it makes\n * is under `scene`; equal inputs make equal graphs; materials belong to the library and are never disposed here.\n * @example\n * // const stage = createStage({ level: getLevel('level:room'), materials: createMaterialLibrary() });\n * // stage.capture(world.query('mover'));\n * // stage.draw(0.5); // halfway between the last two steps; then renderer.render(stage.scene, camera)\n * @see engine/gfx/stage.test.ts\n */\nimport { BufferGeometry, Color, Group, Mesh, Scene, type Material, type Object3D } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { Rng } from '../core/rng';\nimport type { QueryView } from '../sim/queryView';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport type { CompiledLevel } from '../world/level/types';\nimport type { Site } from '../world/site';\nimport type { Terrain } from '../world/terrain';\nimport type { CameraPose, Vec3 } from './cameras/pose';\nimport { createCutaway, type Cutaway } from './cutaway';\nimport { boxGeometry } from './geometry/box';\nimport type { LevelMeshes } from './level/meshes';\nimport type { LevelRecipe } from './level/recipes';\nimport type { DoorLeaf } from '../world/level/doorways';\nimport { runMeshes } from './level/runs';\nimport { createActorPuppets, type ActorPuppets } from './puppets/actors';\nimport { createStageCrowd, type StageCrowd } from './stageCrowd';\nimport { createStageFx, type StageFx } from './stageFx';\nimport { createStageProps, type StageProps } from './stageProps';\nimport { createStageRides, RIDE_KINDS, type StageRides } from './stageRides';\nimport { createStageShells, type StageShells } from './stageShells';\nimport { createStageSite, type StageSite } from './stageSite';\nimport { groundMesh } from './stageGround';\nimport type { FeatureReport } from './features';\nimport { createStageSky, type StageSky } from './stageSky';\nimport { placeableKinds, placeOf, type StandInPlace } from './standIns';\nimport { aboveStorey, createStoreyCut, cutPlace } from './storeyCut';\nimport { createTerrainMeshes, type TerrainMeshes } from './terrain';\nimport type { Warmup } from './warmup';\n73:export interface StageOptions {\n99:export interface Stage {\n166:export function createStage(options: StageOptions): Stage {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LpjmQRebtAXMe1gv4thtXF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9Zn7Di2cWPN5LfPgfS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BJXutGbidwJJ9D34yfdERC","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"web-fetch","description":"Fetch source game reference pages","prompt":"Read these pages and answer the questions below factually and concisely, saying which page each fact came from, and saying \"not stated\" where a page doesn't say.\n\nPages:\n- https://cosimoquiche.github.io/tc-wiki/games/so/SO.html\n- https://cosimoquiche.github.io/tc-wiki/general/Healing_Touch.html\n- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion\n- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Under_the_Knife\n\nQuestions (about the Wii game Trauma Center: Second Opinion, and where needed its DS original):\n1. The complete instrument list, what each does, and how each is operated with Wii Remote + Nunchuk (tool select by stick, trigger, etc.).\n2. How Vitals, the operation timer, action ratings (Cool/Good/Bad/Miss or similar), mistakes, scoring, and end-of-operation ranks (including XS) work.\n3. How each character's Healing Touch works (how it is activated, the star gesture, duration, how many uses per operation, Derek's vs Naomi/Nozomi's differences).\n4. The structure of the story: chapters and how many operations, the story beats and tone, cast roles, what GUILT is, and the strains and how each behaves as a boss (a sentence each).\n5. What the game adds relative to the DS original (new chapter, new character, new tools, changed controls).\n6. Common criticisms in reviews (difficulty spikes, repetitive operations, control issues) — anything a designer should fix.\n\nReport the answer as compact bullet lists under each question number. Don't reproduce long passages.","run_in_background":false},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_