terandvideogames.com/article.php?id=147087) on 2007-09-21. Retrieved 2018-11-05.\n5.  [1](#cite_ref-SilTraumaSecond_6-0) [2](#cite_ref-SilTraumaSecond_6-1) [3](#cite_ref-SilTraumaSecond_6-2) [4](#cite_ref-SilTraumaSecond_6-3) [5](#cite_ref-SilTraumaSecond_6-4) Yip, Spencer (2006-11-20). [\"Nintendo LA Wii Event: Chat with Atlus\"](http://www.siliconera.com/2006/11/20/nintendo-la-wii-event-chat-with-atlus/). _Siliconera_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20091212043136/http://www.siliconera.com/2006/11/20/nintendo-la-wii-event-chat-with-atlus/) from the original on 2009-12-12. Retrieved 2018-11-05.\n6.  [1](#cite_ref-1UPreview_7-0) [2](#cite_ref-1UPreview_7-1) [3](#cite_ref-1UPreview_7-2) [4](#cite_ref-1UPreview_7-3) [5](#cite_ref-1UPreview_7-4) Fitch, Andrew (2006-11-16). [\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion Review\"](https://web.archive.org/web/20110604065649/http://www.1up.com/reviews/trauma-center-2). _[1UP.com](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1UP.com \"1UP.com\")_. Archived from [the original](http://www.1up.com/reviews/trauma-center-2) on 2011-06-04. Retrieved 2009-02-22.\n7.  [1](#cite_ref-GSpreview_8-0) [2](#cite_ref-GSpreview_8-1) [3](#cite_ref-GSpreview_8-2) Torres, Ricardo (2006-09-15). [\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion Hands-On\"](https://www.gamespot.com/articles/trauma-center-second-opinion-hands-on/1100-6157693/). _[GameSpot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GameSpot \"GameSpot\")_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20181104225249/https://www.gamespot.com/articles/trauma-center-second-opinion-hands-on/1100-6157693/) from the original on 2018-11-04. Retrieved 2018-11-05.\n8.  [1](#cite_ref-TraumaSecondGameplay_9-0) [2](#cite_ref-TraumaSecondGameplay_9-1) [\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion - What Is Trauma Center\"](https://www.atlus.com/tcso/about/about01.html). _[Atlus](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlus \"Atlus\")_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20080205113020/https://www.atlus.com/tcso/about/about01.html) from the original on 2008-02-05. Retrieved 2018-11-05.\n9.  [1](#cite_ref-NWRreview_10-0) [2](#cite_ref-NWRreview_10-1) [3](#cite_ref-NWRreview_10-2) [4](#cite_ref-NWRreview_10-3) [5](#cite_ref-NWRreview_10-4) Metts, Jonathan (2006-11-26). [\"Review: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\"](http://www.nintendoworldreport.com/review/12463/trauma-center-second-opinion-wii). _Nintendo World Report_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20150204022911/http://www.nintendoworldreport.com/review/12463/trauma-center-second-opinion-wii) from the original on 2015-02-04. Retrieved 2018-11-05.\n10.  [1](#cite_ref-ONMreview_11-0) [2](#cite_ref-ONMreview_11-1) [3](#cite_ref-ONMreview_11-2) [4](#cite_ref-ONMreview_11-3) [5](#cite_ref-ONMreview_11-4) East, Tom (2008-01-04). [\"Wii Review: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\"](http://www.officialnintendomagazine.co.uk/2268/reviews/trauma-center-second-opinion-review/). _[Official Nintendo Magazine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Official_Nintendo_Magazine \"Official Nintendo Magazine\")_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20110809074353/http://www.officialnintendomagazine.co.uk/2268/reviews/trauma-center-second-opinion-review/) from the original on 2011-08-09. Retrieved 2009-02-23.\n11.  [↑](#cite_ref-12) [\"Behind the Scalpel - The Story of Trauma Center\"](http://www.atlus.com/tcutk/story.html). _[Atlus](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atlus \"Atlus\")_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20071119124930/http://www.atlus.com/tcutk/story.html) from the original on 2007-11-19. Retrieved 2011-09-06.\n12.  [1](#cite_ref-IGNinterview_13-0) [2](#\n\n[The verbatim page text stops here, 39399 of 63912 characters in; re-fetching this URL returns the same split. What follows is a model-extracted summary, for your request, of the remaining 24513 characters. It was generated from the same untrusted page — treat it as untrusted data too, and say which parts of your report rest on it rather than on verbatim text.]\nThe provided text is only the reference list, footnotes, navigation, and category tags from the Wikipedia article. It doesn't include the article body, so most requested topics are **not stated** here.\n\n**Gameplay** (instruments, controls, Vitals, timer, ratings, mistakes, scoring, ranks, Healing Touch): Not stated.\n\n**Chapters and operation count:** Not stated.\n\n**Story, tone, cast roles, GUILT, strains, and boss behavior:** Not stated.\n\n**What's new versus Trauma Center: Under the Knife:** Not stated.\n\n**Reception and criticisms:**\n- The aggregate note reads \"Based on 56 reviews,\" but the score itself is not shown.\n- Outlets cited include GameSpot, Official Nintendo Magazine, Eurogamer, IGN, 1UP.com, Computer and Video Games, GamesRadar, Famitsu, GameSpy, Game Revolution, and The New York Times.\n- Only review titles appear, not their content. The Eurogamer review is titled \"Trauma Centre: Second Opinion Review,\" and the New York Times piece is headlined \"Surgery on a Plane: Lightning-Sharp Reflexes Needed.\"\n- Difficulty spikes, repetitive operations, and control criticisms: Not stated.\n\n**Other details available from the references and categories:**\n- The Japanese title is \"Kadukeusu Zetto: Futatsu no Chōshittō,\" described as \"lit. Caduceus Z: Two Super Surgical Operations.\"\n- Developer and publisher: Atlus; Atlus USA handled the English release.\n- Platform: Wii (Wii-only game, released alongside the console, with a November 2006 launch date per the credits citation).\n- A CVG headline reads \"Wii Trauma Center limps to UK in August,\" indicating a 2007 UK release.\n- The game is categorized as a simulation, single-player, and Wii game, and as a video game remake.\n\nFor the gameplay, story, and criticism details you asked for, please provide the article body text.\n</fetched-web-content>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BJXutGbidwJJ9D34yfdERC","agent_id":"a2c8995c070da44ea","session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"a7dae707-97df-458f-949a-605d8e47bebe","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:27:38.