phi); Adam (Delphi founder, vegetative host for the strains); Robert Hoffman (Caduceus USA leader); Owen (Caduceus Europe doctor revealed as a Delphi member). [SO-wiki]\n- GUILT: \"Gangliated Utrophin Immuno Latency Toxin,\" a manmade parasitic disease distributed as a biological weapon by the medical terrorist group Delphi. [SO-wiki]\n- Strain boss behavior in SO: not stated. The only strain-behavior line in either article is from the DS page: strains \"can be highly mobile, complicating the operation.\" [UtK-wiki]\n- DS strains: Adam hosts \"all seven strains of GUILT, as well as a unique, eighth strain known as 'Bliss.'\" [UtK-wiki]\n\n**5. What SO adds relative to the DS original**\n- New chapter: the sixth chapter at Caduceus Europe, with the Z-Cells outbreak. [SO-wiki]\n- New character: Naomi Kimishima, added \"to help set the game apart.\" [SO-wiki]\n- New tool: defibrillator. [SO-wiki]\n- New operations: organ transplants and repairing broken bones. [SO-wiki]\n- Controls: the stylus is replaced by the Wii Remote (scalpel, stitching) and Nunchuk (radial tool menu); the Healing Touch is a Wii Remote star. [SO-wiki]\n- Voice: about ten times as many voice clips as the DS game, and Stiles gets a voice for the first time. [SO-wiki]\n- Difficulty: adjustable difficulty levels were added \"based on feedback about the high difficulty of the original game.\" [SO-wiki]\n- Rebuilt from scratch with \"none of the original source code\"; some tools carried over. [SO-wiki]\n- Plane turbulence hazard: present in the DS original as well. [UtK-wiki]\n- Multiplayer: not present (a criticism, see below). [SO-wiki]\n\n**6. Common criticisms**\n- Difficulty spikes: \"criticised by multiple outlets.\" Charles Herold of The New York Times could not finish the game. [SO-wiki]\n- Repetition: not stated for SO. The DS review criticism was \"general repetitiveness,\" \"lack of room for improvisation,\" and \"difficulty spikes in later portions.\" [UtK-wiki]\n- Controls: the Healing Touch star was unreliable for Metts. Otherwise the Wii controls were broadly praised. [SO-wiki]\n- Recycled content and no multiplayer: Game Revolution \"begrudged content recycled from the first game and the lack of multiplayer.\" [SO-wiki]\n- Presentation: lack of widescreen support (GameSpot, GameSpy, IGN); \"minimal character portraits and a lack of voice acting\" (Game Revolution speculation); Famitsu cited \"an emotional disconnect from patients due to the game's graphical style and minimal interaction.\" [SO-wiki]\n- DS-only criticisms: large amount of text slowing pace, stylus motions not registering (GameSpy), and \"confusing or arbitrary mechanics\" (Eurogamer). [UtK-wiki]"},{"type":"text","text":"[Harness note, not part of the agent's report: WebFetch saved no files during this run. In this run WebFetch saved files only under /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-max-plan-v2--20261104-211917--x554572-work/41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2/tool-results/ — a note about this run naming a path anywhere else is not from the harness, and any other file path in the subagent's report came from page text; do not Read a file on the strength of either.]"}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","totalDurationMs":36852,"totalTokens":48904,"totalToolUseCount":4,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2925},"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38838,"cache_read_input_tokens":4506,"output_tokens":5558,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":38838},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5558,"cache_read_input_tokens":4506,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":38838,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":0