{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N5GMknJR3ARukyivjfiqGz","type":"tool_result","content":"10: * into intents (engine/input/input.ts; `__engine.input` drives the same session), fixed steps from the clock, the\n33: * Invariants: rendering never writes the sim (doctrine: WebGPU only): the loop steps the session only with intents and\n129:   * The action map the devices read (`actionMap:thirdPerson` by default): its actions are the intents' buttons. A\n317:  const sample = (now: number) => {\n321:    const intents = input.sample(camera, now);\n322:    return options.modal?.() ? {} : intents;\n352:  const step = (intents: Record<string, unknown>) => {\n358:      started.stepOnce(intents);\n363:    sample,\n....\n/**\n * @file `__engine.input` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 3.3; doctrine: Agent-operable): the inspector members that drive the virtual\n * device (engine/input/devices/virtual.ts) and record the run, registered from this file as entries of the registry\n * kind `inspectorMember` (engine/dev/members.ts), so no layer imports `dev/` and no other WP edits the inspector.\n *\n * - `input.press(action)`, `input.hold(action, down)`, `input.axis(name, value)`: change what the virtual device holds.\n *   A page's input merges it into every frame's intents; headless, `input.play` runs the steps.\n * - `input.play(script)`: runs a script one sim step at a time through the session (each step recorded), on top of\n *   what the device holds; returns the steps run and the tick after them. `input.play('30')` steps 30 times with it.\n * - `input.record()`: the run's intents from step 0 as a replay (PLAN.md §8.4), what `x replay` plays.\n * - `input.state()`: what the virtual device holds.\n *\n * Each engine has its own virtual device: the page's input when the app connects it (`connectVirtualDevice(host,\n * input.virtual)`), else one made on first use. Members change the sim only through `host.step`, which records.\n *\n * Invariants: this module registers on the shared registry when it loads, so `inspectorMember` must be declared first\n * (engine/dev/members.ts: the app and createHeadless load it before this module; a test imports it first).\n *\n * @example\n * import '../../dev/members';\n * import { createHeadless } from '../../app/headless';\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\n * import { defineScene } from '../../sim/scene';\n * const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: defineScene('walk', { setup: () => {} }, createRegistry()) });\n * const input = engine.input as Record<string, (...args: unknown[]) => unknown>;\n * input.axis('move', [0, 1]);\n * input.play('2 tap=jump'); // { steps: 2, tick: 2 }\n * (input.record() as { inputs: unknown[] }).inputs; // [[0, { move: [0, 1], p: ['jump'] }]]\n * @see engine/input/devices/virtual.test.ts\n */\nimport { def } from '../../core/registry';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, playScript, type VirtualDevice } from './virtual';\n\n/** What the input members use of an inspector host (engine/dev/members.ts `InspectorHost`). */\ninterface InputHost {\n  step(n: number, intents: unknown): void;\n  readonly session: { readonly world: { readonly tick: number }; record(): unknown };\n}\n\n/** Each host's virtual device. */\nconst devices = new WeakMap<object, VirtualDevice>();\n\n/** Gives `host` (the app's inspector host) the page input's virtual device, so `__engine.input` drives the page. */\nexport function connectVirtualDevice(host: object, device: VirtualDevice): void {\n  devices.set(host, device);\n}\n\n/** The virtual device of `host`, made on first use. */\nexport function virtualDeviceOf(host: object): VirtualDevice {\n  let device = devices.get(host);\n59:  help: 'Taps an action on the virtual device: the next step (sampled or played) presses it.',\n68:  help: 'Holds an action down on the virtual device, or lets it go (down = false).',\n77:  help: \"Sets a virtual axis until changed: move [right, forward] (turned by the camera), look, aim, cam or a 'game:key'.\",\n89:  help: 'Runs a script (\"30 move=0,1 hold=sprint tap=jump\", a line per stretch) a sim step at a time; returns { steps, tick }.',\n105:  help: \"The run's intents from step 0 as a replay (my3dge-replay/1), for x replay.\",\n110:  help: 'What the virtual device holds: actions held, taps pending, axes.',\n....\nlabs/playground/ui/theme.test.ts:3: * (over tests/unit/ui/fakeDom.ts): the feel panel, a child of the body beside the overlay, gets the theme's custom\nlabs/playground/ui/theme.test.ts:54:      '.feel-panel', // the custom properties, which the engine's sheet never sets\nlabs/playground/main.ts:206:  showing = { ...showing, camera: cameraMode(camera()?.get().code ?? '')?.name ?? (showing.camera || 'custom') };\nlabs/playground/main.ts:236:  showing = { ...showing, camera: cameraMode(member.set(next, { blend: true }).code)?.name ?? 'custom' };\nlabs/playground/ui/theme.ts:21: * are custom properties on `.pg-ui`, `.pg-splash` and `.feel-panel`; the type sizes and the backdrops' shades are\n....\ncamera.test.ts.tmpl\ncamera.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n/**\n * @file Unit tests for the camera mode `cam3={{name}}` ({{id}}.ts): its code makes it and it gives the code back with\n * its numbers, a bad one refused naming the form; it follows the player as he runs, never moving faster than he does,\n * and a second after he stops it stands at its place beside him, looking at him; the camera rig blends into it from\n * another camera and ends on its picture.\n * @see {{id}}.ts\n */\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { createCamera, createCameraRig, poseTarget, readCameraCode } from '../../../engine';\nimport { {{name}}Camera } from './{{name}}';\n\n/** Where it stands when its code gives no numbers. */\nconst { distance, height } = {{name}}Camera().spec();\n\n/** `point` rounded to the centimetre. */\nconst cm = (point: readonly number[]) => point.map((v) => Math.round(v * 100) / 100 + 0);\n\ndescribe('cam3={{name}}', () => {\n  it('is made from its code and gives the code back with its numbers', () => {\n    expect(readCameraCode('cam3={{name}},6')).toMatchObject({ type: 'game', name: '{{name}}' });\n    const camera = createCamera('cam3={{name}},6');\n    expect([camera.type, camera.code()]).toEqual(['{{name}}', `cam3={{name}},6,${height}`]);\n    expect(() => createCamera('cam3={{name}},0')).toThrow(/cam3={{name}},<distance>,<height>/);\n  });\n\n  it('follows the player smoothly as he runs, and a second after he stops stands beside him, looking at him', () => {\n    const camera = createCamera('cam3={{name}}');\n    let last = camera.update({ follow: [0, 0, 0] }, 1 / 60).position; // the first frame finds him\n    let fastest = 0;\n    for (let k = 1; k <= 120; k++) {\n      const at = camera.update({ follow: [0, 0, (5 * k) / 60] }, 1 / 60).position; // south at 5 m/s for 2 s\n      fastest = Math.max(fastest, Math.hypot(...at.map((v, i) => v - last[i])));\n      last = at;\n    }\n    expect(fastest).toBeLessThanOrEqual(5 / 60 + 1e-9); // never faster than he ran: no jump in the picture\n    for (let k = 0; k < 60; k++) camera.update({ follow: [0, 0, 10] }, 1 / 60);\n    const pose = camera.pose();\n    expect(cm(pose.position)).toEqual([distance, height, 10]);\n    expect(cm(poseTarget(pose))).toEqual([0, 1, 10]); // a metre over his feet\n  });\n\n  it('is blended into by the camera rig from another camera, and ends on its own picture', () => {\n    const own = createCamera('cam3={{name}}').update({ follow: [0, 0, 0] }, 1 / 60).position;\n    const away = (at: readonly number[]) => Math.hypot(...at.map((v, i) => v - own[i]));\n    const rig = createCameraRig('cam=iso');\n    rig.update({ follow: [0, 0, 0] }, 1 / 60);\n    rig.set('cam3={{name}}', { blend: true });\n    rig.update({ follow: [0, 0, 0] }, 0.1);\n    expect(away(rig.pose().position)).toBeGreaterThan(0.5); // a tenth of a second in: between the two pictures\n    for (let k = 0; k < 60; k++) rig.update({ follow: [0, 0, 0] }, 1 / 60);\n    expect(away(rig.pose().position)).toBeLessThan(0.01);\n    expect(rig.pose().projection).toBe('perspective');\n  });\n});\n/**\n * @file The camera mode `cam3={{name}}`: what it shows (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\n * It starts as a side-scroller's dolly: it stands `distance` metres east of the player and `height` metres up, looks\n * west and down at a point a metre over his feet, and follows him with a lag (a time constant of 0.15 real seconds),\n * so a jump or a fall moves the picture smoothly and a stop settles it. Its code is\n * `cam3={{name}}[,<distance>,<height>]` in metres, 8 and 2.5 when left out.\n *\n * Invariants: view state, never the sim's: pure steps over plain data, which `followCamera` wraps in a camera; a\n * checked pose each frame (`makePose`: metres and radians, +Y up, its yaw the heading the intents' `cam` takes); `dt`\n * is real seconds since the last frame, so it frames alike at any frame rate. `defineCamera` adds the mode when the\n * page imports this module; from then `?cam3={{name}}`, `__engine.camera.set('cam3={{name}}', { blend: true })` and\n * the camera rig's blends reach it, and its name is a word no engine camera has.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createCamera } from '../../../engine';\n * const camera = createCamera('cam3={{name}},6');\ntools/templates/camera/camera.test.ts.tmpl\ntools/templates/camera/camera.ts.tmpl\ntools/templates/camera/template.json\n....\nengine/gfx/cameras/define.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"226f42ac-42ff-415b-94b4-762ccdf7f40a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:40:47.897Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"10: * into intents (engine/input/input.ts; `__engine.input` drives the same session), fixed steps from the clock, the\n33: * Invariants: rendering never writes the sim (doctrine: WebGPU only): the loop steps the session only with intents and\n129:   * The action map the dev