{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SMTFS2HAD96BCRFCzAVmAN","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file Resolution modes (PLAN.md WP 2.1): how many pixels the renderer draws for the canvas's size on screen, from\n * the view setting `gfx.resolution`. `pixels` draws the engine's own chunky pixels, at most 330 lines and a whole\n * number of screen pixels each (2 at 540 screen lines, 3 at 720, 4 at 1080), so the picture is crisp and cheap;\n * `balanced` draws half the screen's resolution; `full` all of it. Both reduced modes are shown with\n * `image-rendering: pixelated`, so the browser enlarges them without blurring. `auto`, the default (WP 13.30), draws\n * the mode the page's look asks for (its `resolution`, engine/gfx/post/looks.ts), given by `prefer(mode)`\n * (engine/app/look.ts), and `pixels` while the look names none; the other three hold whatever the look asks.\n *\n * `fitResolution` is the arithmetic, pure and tested in Node; `createResolution` applies it to a renderer and its\n * canvas: `update()` measures the canvas's CSS size and the device pixel ratio (capped at `MAX_PIXEL_RATIO`) and,\n * when the size, the ratio or the mode changed since the last call, sets the drawing buffer (`setPixelRatio(1)`, then\n * `setSize(width, height, false)`). The page sizes the canvas with CSS; this module never writes its CSS size. The\n * frame calls `update()` first (engine/gfx/renderer.ts), so a resize or a mode change takes effect on the next frame.\n *\n * The picture's glide (WP 13.24): `shift(x, y)` moves the whole picture by a fraction of a pixel (CSS `transform`), the\n * remainder a camera snapped to the pixel grid took off (engine/gfx/post/snap.ts `snapGrid`), so a snapped picture\n * still glides as the camera does; the CSS variable `--my3dge-pixel`, one drawn pixel's size in CSS pixels, lets the\n * page give its canvas a margin of two drawn pixels so the glide never shows an edge (labs/playground/index.html).\n *\n * Phones (WP 3.12, built, not tested): `cap(budget)` caps the buffer's pixels and the pixel ratio by the quality tier\n * (engine/gfx/quality.ts; `pixels` mode by a coarser whole scale), and `keepWidth` widens a portrait picture's\n * vertical field of view so the horizontal one is kept (`2·atan(tan(fov/2)/aspect)`, at most 150°).\n *\n * Invariants: the drawing buffer is at least 1 × 1; in `pixels` mode its height is at most `PIXEL_LINES`, and,\n * uncapped, at least 200 whenever the screen has that many lines and a whole-pixel scale allows it (all but 331 to\n * 399). Changing the size never builds a pipeline (measured, WP 2.1). The setting is a view setting: never in the hash.\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/50-frame.js:18-28` (`fit()`, its modes and numbers), and the caps and the\n * portrait lens from `shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/quality.rs:73-84` and `shardfall:crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs:168-173`.\n *\n * @example\n * fitResolution({ width: 1280, height: 720 }, 1, 'pixels'); // { width: 427, height: 240, scale: 3, … }\n * fitResolution({ width: 1280, height: 720 }, 1, 'balanced').width; // 640\n * fitResolution({ width: 1280, height: 720 }, 2, 'full').height; // 1440\n....\n58:export type TouchSetting = 'auto' | 'on' | 'off';\n64:    enum: ['auto', 'on', 'off'],\n68:      \"Touch mode, which shows the touch controls and the phone defaults: 'auto' follows the screen (a coarse pointer or a first touch on, the mouse off), 'on' and 'of\n30: * page's chrome, the touch layer from `touchLayout` and swiping (engine/ui/), the quality budget's pixel caps\n69:import { createTouchLayer, getTouchLayout, type TouchLayout } from '../ui/touch';\n127:  touchLayout?: string;\n285:    if (options.touchLayout !== undefined) layout = getTouchLayout(options.touchLayout, registry);\n327:  parts.layer = createTouchLayer(document, layout);\n342:    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\n373:    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\n....\n11: * (`padStyle` reads it from `Gamepad.id`: Xbox by default, PlayStation, Nintendo).\n31: * codeLabel('PadSouth', { pad: padStyle('DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c)') }); // 'Cross'\n55:export type PadStyle = 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo';\n148:const PAD_LABELS: Record<PadStyle, readonly string[]> = {\n174:export function padStyle(id: string): PadStyle {\n185:  pad?: PadStyle;\nengine/input/codes.ts:6: * mapping by position (`PadSouth` is index 0: A on Xbox, Cross on PlayStation), and each stick has four direction codes\nengine/input/codes.ts:11: * (`padStyle` reads it from `Gamepad.id`: Xbox by default, PlayStation, Nintendo).\nengine/input/codes.ts:31: * codeLabel('PadSouth', { pad: padStyle('DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c)') }); // 'Cross'\nengine/input/codes.ts:55:export type PadStyle = 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo';\nengine/input/codes.ts:149:  xbox: ['A', 'B', 'X', 'Y', 'LB', 'RB', 'LT', 'RT', 'View', 'Menu', 'LS', 'RS', 'D-pad Up', 'D-pad Down', 'D-pad Left', 'D-pad Right', 'Guide']\nengine/input/codes.ts:150:  playstation: ['Cross', 'Circle', 'Square', 'Triangle', 'L1', 'R1', 'L2', 'R2', 'Create', 'Options', 'L3', 'R3', 'D-pad Up', 'D-pad Down', 'D-p\nengine/input/codes.ts:175:  if (/054c|playstation|dualsense|dualshock|sony/i.test(id)) return 'playstation';\nengine/input/codes.ts:177:  return 'xbox';\nengine/input/codes.ts:184:  /** The pad family (Xbox by default). */\nengine/input/codes.ts:188:/** What a prompt shows for `code`: `W`, `Space`, `LMB`, `A` / `Cross`, `L Stick Up`, `Hold X`. */\nengine/input/codes.ts:193:  if (button >= 0) return PAD_LABELS[options.pad ?? 'xbox'][button];\nengine/input/intents.ts:20: * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n....\n/**\n * @file The audio runtime (PLAN.md WP 9.3, §6.4, I-23; doctrines: Assets, Common ground): a page's sound. It plays\n * the effects and songs the DSP renders (engine/audio/data) through Web Audio: mixed on buses with ducking and voice\n * limits (mixer.ts, voices.ts), placed in 3D and muffled behind walls (spatial.ts), in a room's reverb (reverb.ts),\n * with music in layers that change on the beat (music.ts). `createAudio()` makes it; the frame loop calls\n * `update(cameraPose, queries)` once per rendered frame, after the render.\n *\n * The context: a page's runtime starts `locked`, with no `AudioContext`, and makes one inside the first user gesture\n * (gesture.ts: a key, a click, the end of a touch), so the browser lets it run and prints no warning; a later gesture\n * resumes it when the browser suspended it. Its `state` is then the context's (`running`, `suspended`, `closed`).\n * Without Web Audio it is `off` and says so once (`AUDIO_OFF`); the game plays on in silence. A test passes its own\n * context (`OfflineAudioContext`), which needs no gesture.\n *\n * Playing: `play(id, { vol, pitch, variant, bus, position, when, loop, duck })` plays an `sfx` entry on its bus (the\n * entry's `bus` by default), its variants in turn unless one is named, placed at `position` when given; it returns\n * the `Sound` (move it, stop it), or null when the voice limits drop it or there is no running context yet (sounds\n * asked for while locked are dropped, music is remembered). `duck` ducks the music and ambience for the sound's\n * length. `footstep(surface, position)` plays the effect `footsteps` maps the level's surface tag to (WP 4.2's\n * `surfaceAt`), `'*'` for any other, `sfx:step` without one. `event(type, payload)` plays a sim event: a sound event\n * (`{ sfx, vol?, variant?, position? }`, as `x audio --replay` reads them) plays its effect, and a type bound with\n * `bind(type, id)` plays its stinger on the beat.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here changes the sim, and the QueryView only answers occlusion rays. An\n * unknown id throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest, when it is asked for, locked or not. Renders are cached per\n * effect and variant at the context's rate (played looped, an effect with a `loop` pass is its render folded onto it:\n * buffers.ts `foldLoop`, so it has no seam); a voice disconnects its nodes when it ends.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3708-3786` (`ChipAudio`: the lazy context, resume on a gesture, the\n * buses and their levels, `sfx` with its per-sound rule, `music`), on pre-rendered buffers.\n *\n * @example\n * // browser: Web Audio plays only in a page (tests/e2e/examples.spec.ts runs it; tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts the rest)\n * const audio = createAudio({ footsteps: { iron: 'sfx:stomp', '*': 'sfx:step' } });\n * audio.music('song:dungeon', { intensity: 0 }); // starts on the first gesture\n * audio.bind('bossSeen', 'sfx:secret');\n * // each frame, after the render: audio.update(camera.pose, queryViewOf(world));\n * audio.event('hit', { sfx: 'sfx:hit', position: [2, 1, 5] });\n * @see tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts\n */\nimport { defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../../core/log';\n100:  readonly state: AudioState;\n102:  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\n103:  play(id: string, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\n104:  footstep(surface: string, position?: Vec3, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\n105:  event(type: string, payload?: unknown): Sound | null;\n106:  bind(type: string, id: string | null): void;\n108:  music(id: string | null, options?: MusicChange & { intensity?: number }): void;\n110:  intensity(value: number, options?: MusicChange): void;\n112:  stinger(id: string, options?: MusicChange & { vol?: number }): void;\n114:  update(pose?: ListenerPose, queries?: QueryView): void;\n115:  volume(bus: AudioBus | 'master', value?: number): number;\n116:  mute(on?: boolean): boolean;\n118:  duck(on: boolean | number): void;\n119:  room(room: RoomName | RoomSpec): void;\n120:  info(): AudioInfo;\n122:  close(): Promise<void>;\n129:  sfxKind(registry);\n130:  songKind(registry);\n33:    doc: 'Raised by `audio.play` and `Sound.move` (engine/audio/runtime/sound.ts) for a volume, pitch, variant or position out of range.',\n44:  /** Playback rate (pitch and speed together), 0.1 to 10; 1 by default. */\n45:  pitch?: number;\n107:  checkRange('pitch', options.pitch, 0.1, 10);\n131:  const source = new AudioBufferSourceNode(c, { buffer, loop, playbackRate: options.pitch ?? 1 });\n....\n/**\n * @file The effect `sfx:{{name}}`: what it is the sound of (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\n *\n * Invariants: voices in the chip synth's words (wave, freq, to, dur, vol, arp, vib, filter…; node x describe sfx lists\n * the kind's fields, engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts a voice's); `layers` mix other effects in ({ sfx, at, vol, pitch });\n * `variants` versions spread ±`vary` in pitch, for a sound heard often; `bus` is effects, ui or ambience.\n *\n * @example\n * {{name}}.id; // 'sfx:{{name}}'\n * @see {{id}}.test.ts\n */\nimport { defineSfx } from '../../../engine';\n\n/** The effect `sfx:{{name}}`: replace this sentence with what it is the sound of. */\nexport const {{name}} = defineSfx('sfx:{{name}}', {\n  voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 440, to: 880, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.25 },\n  variants: 4,\n});\n/**\n * @file The song `song:{{name}}`: where it plays and its mood (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\n *\n * Invariants: tracker notation, one token per step: a note (C4, F#3, Bb2), - holding the note before it, . a rest,\n * and | a bar line, which takes no step; a drums track writes the kit's tokens (k kick, s snare, h hat, o open hat,\n * c crash, t tom). At `steps` per beat and `beats` per bar, every track fills whole bars or divides one (node x\n * describe song lists the fields; engine/audio/data/song.ts gives the rules). `intensity` makes a track join only\n * when the music's intensity reaches it.\n *\n * @example\n * import { songTiming } from '../../../engine';\n * songTiming({{name}}).seconds; // 4: two bars of 4/4 at 120 bpm\n * @see {{id}}.test.ts\n */\nimport { defineSong } from '../../../engine';\n\n/** The song `song:{{name}}`: replace this sentence with where it plays. */\nexport const {{name}} = defineSong('song:{{name}}', {\n  bpm: 120,\n  tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: 0.12, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - E5 - D5 - F5 - A5 - G5 - | E5 - - - D5 - - - C5 - - - - - . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.25, notes: 'C3 - - - G2 - - - C3 - - - G2 - - - | C3 - - - G2 - - - C3 - - - . . . .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: 0.12, intensity: 0.25, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h . s . h h' },\n  ],\n});\n....\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:2: * @file The look `look:playground-pixel`, the playground as pixel art (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.2, PLAN.md WP 13.24): a\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:18: * look.id; // 'look:playground-pixel'\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:23:import { defineLook } from '../../../engine';\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:26:/** The look `look:playground-pixel`: a low-resolution picture, ramps dithered on the world, snapped and gliding. */\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:27:export const look = defineLook('look:playground-pixel', {\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:34:  perspective: 'look:playground-pixel-perspective',\nlabs/playground/looks/pixelPerspective.ts:2: * @file The look `look:playground-pixel-perspective`, the pixel look's variant for the perspective cameras (first\nlabs/playground/looks/pixelPerspective.ts:4: * toon numbers in place of `look:playground-pixel`'s while the camera is a perspective one (the look's `perspective`,\n/**\n * @file The look `look:playground-clean`, the playground's default (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.2; the owner's direction of\n * 2026-11-03, ADR-0025 amendment 46): the picture as the scene draws it, unstyled: every material in the set's own\n * lit style (`style` left `''`), lit by the hour's sky (`sky:daylight`, engine/gfx/daylight.ts: the sun, the moon,\n * the ambient and the streetlights at dusk, as the other two looks have them), its dome as the day draws it (no\n * gradient), and edges smoothed (the `aa` filter: the engine's edge smoothing, FXAA unless the view setting `post.aa`\n * names another, engine/gfx/post/aa.ts), with no bands, ink, outline shells, pixels or grade. The engine's own\n * `look:clean` would keep the stage's own lights (a hemisphere and one sun under a plain background,\n * engine/gfx/stageSky.ts), which the hour and the lamps never reach, and smooth nothing.\n *\n * Drawn at the screen's full resolution (`resolution: 'full'`, while `gfx.resolution` is `auto`) with every texture\n * blended (`textures: 'smooth'`: linear filtering, so a floor up close is not a grid of 6 cm squares), the owner's\n * direction of 2026-11-03 (WP 13.30, ADR-0025 amendment 47): the engine's own `pixels` resolution and crisp texels\n * are the pixel look's.\n *\n * Invariants: data only, the kind's fields (`node x describe look`); the sky `sky:daylight`; the scene's own style;\n * every filter it leaves out off. The page draws it by default (labs/playground/main.ts); P steps on to the cel look,\n * then the pixel look.\n *\n * @example\n * look.id; // 'look:playground-clean'\n * look.filters.aa.scope; // 'all': its edges smoothed\n * [look.resolution, look.textures]; // ['full', 'smooth']\n * @see labs/playground/looks/looks.test.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"28fc05a6-d4da-4a69-b35d-e7b7f2dc81cb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:42:10.064Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file Resolution modes (PLAN.md WP 2.1): how many pixels the renderer draws for the canvas's size on screen, from\n * the view setting `gfx.resolution`. `pixels` draws the engine's own chunky pixels, at most 330 lines and a whole\n * number of screen pixels each (2 at 540 screen lines, 3 at 720, 4 at 1080), so the picture is crisp and cheap;\n * `balanced` draws half the screen's resolution; `full` all of it. Both reduced modes are shown with\n * `image-rendering: pixelated`, so the browser enlarges them without blurring. `auto`, the default (WP 13.30), draws\n * the mode the page's look asks for (its `resolution`, engine/gfx/post/looks.ts), given by `prefer(mode)`\n * (engine/app/look.ts), and `pixels` while the look names none; the other three hold whatever the look asks.\n *\n * `fitResolution` is the arithmetic, pure and tested in Node; `createResolution` applies it to a renderer and its\n * canvas: `update()` measures the canvas's CSS size and the device pixel ratio (capped at `MAX_PIXEL_RATIO`) and,\n * when the size, the ratio or the mode changed since the last call, sets the drawing buffer (`setPixelRatio(1)`, then\n * `setSize(width, height, false)`). The page sizes the canvas with CSS; this module never writes its CSS size. The\n * frame calls `update()` first (engine/gfx/renderer.ts), so a resize or a mode change takes effect on the next frame.\n *\n * The picture's glide (WP 13.24): `shift(x, y)` moves the whole picture by a fraction of a pixel (CSS `transform`), the\n * remainder a camera snapped to the pixel grid took off (engine/gfx/post/snap.ts `snapGrid`), so a snapped picture\n * still glides as the camera does; the CSS variable `--my3dge-pixel`, one drawn pixel's size in CSS pixels, lets the\n * page give its canvas a margin of two drawn pixels so the glide never shows an edge (labs/playground/index.html).\n *\n * Phones (WP 3.12, built, not tested): `cap(budget)` caps the buffer's pixels and the pixel ratio by the quality tier\n * (engine/gfx/quality.ts; `pixels` mode by a coarser whole scale), and `keepWidth` widens a portrait picture's\n * vertical field of view so the horizontal one is kept (`2·atan(tan(fov/2)/aspect)`, at most 150°).\n *\n * Invariants: the drawing buffer is at least 1 × 1; in `pixels` mode its height is at most `PIXEL_LINES`, and,\n * uncapped, at least 200 whenever the screen has that many lines and a whole-pixel scale allows it (all but 331 to\n * 399). Changing the size never builds a pipeline (measured, WP 2.1). The setting is a view setting: never in the hash.\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/50-frame.js:18-28` (`fit()`, its modes and numbers), and the caps and the\n * portrait lens from `shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/quality.rs:73-84` and `shardfall:crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs:168-173`.\n *\n * @example\n * fitResolution({ width: 1280, height: 720 }, 1, 'pixels'); // { width: 427, height: 240, scale: 3, … }\n * fitResolution({ width: 1280, height: 720 }, 1, 'balanced').width; // 640\n * fitResolution({ width: 1280, height: 720 }, 2, 'full').height; // 1440\n....\n58:export type TouchSetting = 'auto' | 'on' | 'off';\n64:    enum: ['auto', 'on', 'off'],\n68:      \"Touch mode, which shows the touch controls and the phone defaults: 'auto' follows the screen (a coarse pointer or a first touch on, the mouse off), 'on' and 'of\n30: * page's chrome, the touch layer from `touchLayout` and swiping (engine/ui/), the quality budget's pixel caps\n69:import { createTouchLayer, getTouchLayout, type TouchLayout } from '../ui/touch';\n127:  touchLayout?: string;\n285:    if (options.touchLayout !== undefined) layout = getTouchLayout(options.touchLayout, registry);\n327:  parts.layer = createTouchLayer(document, layout);\n342:    const budget = () => parts.governor!.budget(settingsNow.get<QualitySetting>('quality'), input.touch?.active ?? false); // prettier-ignore\n373:    cap: () => input.touch?.active ?? false,\n....\n11: * (`padStyle` reads it from `Gamepad.id`: Xbox by default, PlayStation, Nintendo).\n31: * codeLabel('PadSouth', { pad: padStyle('DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c)') }); // 'Cross'\n55:export type PadStyle = 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo';\n148:const PAD_LABELS: Record<PadStyle, readonly string[]> = {\n174:export function padStyle(id: string): PadStyle {\n185:  pad?: PadStyle;\nengine/input/codes.ts:6: * mapping by position (`PadSouth` is index 0: A on Xbox, Cross on PlayStation), and each stick has four direction codes\nengine/input/codes.ts:11: * (`padStyle` reads it from `Gamepad.id`: Xbox by default, PlayStation, Nintendo).\nengine/input/codes.ts:31: * codeLabel('PadSouth', { pad: padStyle('DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c)') }); // 'Cross'\nengine/input/codes.ts:55:export type PadStyle = 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo';\nengine/input/codes.ts:149:  xbox: ['A', 'B', 'X', 'Y', 'LB', 'RB', 'LT', 'RT', 'View', 'Menu', 'LS', 'RS', 'D-pad Up', 'D-pad Down', 'D-pad Left', 'D-pad Right', 'Guide']\nengine/input/codes.ts:150:  playstation: ['Cross', 'Circle', 'Square', 'Triangle', 'L1', 'R1', 'L2', 'R2', 'Create', 'Options', 'L3', 'R3', 'D-pad Up', 'D-pad Down', 'D-p\nengine/input/codes.ts:175:  if (/054c|playstation|dualsense|dualshock|sony/i.test(id)) return 'playstation';\nengine/input/codes.ts:177:  return 'xbox';\nengine/input/codes.ts:184:  /** The pad family (Xbox by default). */\nengine/input/codes.ts:188:/** What a prompt shows for `code`: `W`, `Space`, `LMB`, `A` / `Cross`, `L Stick Up`, `Hold X`. */\nengine/input/codes.ts:193:  if (button >= 0) return PAD_LABELS[options.pad ?? 'xbox'][button];\nengine/input/intents.ts:20: * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n....\n/**\n * @file The audio runtime (PLAN.md WP 9.3, §6.4, I-23; doctrines: Assets, Common ground): a page's sound. It plays\n * the effects and songs the DSP renders (engine/audio/data) through Web Audio: mixed on buses with ducking and voice\n * limits (mixer.ts, voices.ts), placed in 3D and muffled behind walls (spatial.ts), in a room's reverb (reverb.ts),\n * with music in layers that change on the beat (music.ts). `createAudio()` makes it; the frame loop calls\n * `update(cameraPose, queries)` once per rendered frame, after the render.\n *\n * The context: a page's runtime starts `locked`, with no `AudioContext`, and makes one inside the first user gesture\n * (gesture.ts: a key, a click, the end of a touch), so the browser lets it run and prints no warning; a later gesture\n * resumes it when the browser suspended it. Its `state` is then the context's (`running`, `suspended`, `closed`).\n * Without Web Audio it is `off` and says so once (`AUDIO_OFF`); the game plays on in silence. A test passes its own\n * context (`OfflineAudioContext`), which needs no gesture.\n *\n * Playing: `play(id, { vol, pitch, variant, bus, position, when, loop, duck })` plays an `sfx` entry on its bus (the\n * entry's `bus` by default), its variants in turn unless one is named, placed at `position` when given; it returns\n * the `Sound` (move it, stop it), or null when the voice limits drop it or there is no running context yet (sounds\n * asked for while locked are dropped, music is remembered). `duck` ducks the music and ambience for the sound's\n * length. `footstep(surface, position)` plays the effect `footsteps` maps the level's surface tag to (WP 4.2's\n * `surfaceAt`), `'*'` for any other, `sfx:step` without one. `event(type, payload)` plays a sim event: a sound event\n * (`{ sfx, vol?, variant?, position? }`, as `x audio --replay` reads them) plays its effect, and a type bound with\n * `bind(type, id)` plays its stinger on the beat.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here changes the sim, and the QueryView only answers occlusion rays. An\n * unknown id throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest, when it is asked for, locked or not. Renders are cached per\n * effect and variant at the context's rate (played looped, an effect with a `loop` pass is its render folded onto it:\n * buffers.ts `foldLoop`, so it has no seam); a voice disconnects its nodes when it ends.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3708-3786` (`ChipAudio`: the lazy context, resume on a gesture, the\n * buses and their levels, `sfx` with its per-sound rule, `music`), on pre-rendered buffers.\n *\n * @example\n * // browser: Web Audio plays only in a page (tests/e2e/examples.spec.ts runs it; tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts the rest)\n * const audio = createAudio({ footsteps: { iron: 'sfx:stomp', '*': 'sfx:step' } });\n * audio.music('song:dungeon', { intensity: 0 }); // starts on the first gesture\n * audio.bind('bossSeen', 'sfx:secret');\n * // each frame, after the render: audio.update(camera.pose, queryViewOf(world));\n * audio.event('hit', { sfx: 'sfx:hit', position: [2, 1, 5] });\n * @see tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts\n */\nimport { defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../../core/log';\n100:  readonly state: AudioState;\n102:  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\n103:  play(id: string, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\n104:  footstep(surface: string, position?: Vec3, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\n105:  event(type: string, payload?: unknown): Sound | null;\n106:  bind(type: string, id: string | null): void;\n108:  music(id: string | null, options?: MusicChange & { intensity?: number }): void;\n110:  intensity(value: number, options?: MusicChange): void;\n112:  stinger(id: string, options?: MusicChange & { vol?: number }): void;\n114:  update(pose?: ListenerPose, queries?: QueryView): void;\n115:  volume(bus: AudioBus | 'master', value?: number): number;\n116:  mute(on?: boolean): boolean;\n118:  duck(on: boolean | number): void;\n119:  room(room: RoomName | RoomSpec): void;\n120:  info(): AudioInfo;\n122:  close(): Promise<void>;\n129:  sfxKind(registry);\n130:  songKind(registry);\n33:    doc: 'Raised by `audio.play` and `Sound.move` (engine/audio/runtime/sound.ts) for a volume, pitch, variant or position out of range.',\n44:  /** Playback rate (pitch and speed together), 0.1 to 10; 1 by default. */\n45:  pitch?: number;\n107:  checkRange('pitch', options.pitch, 0.1, 10);\n131:  const source = new AudioBufferSourceNode(c, { buffer, loop, playbackRate: options.pitch ?? 1 });\n....\n/**\n * @file The effect `sfx:{{name}}`: what it is the sound of (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\n *\n * Invariants: voices in the chip synth's words (wave, freq, to, dur, vol, arp, vib, filter…; node x describe sfx lists\n * the kind's fields, engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts a voice's); `layers` mix other effects in ({ sfx, at, vol, pitch });\n * `variants` versions spread ±`vary` in pitch, for a sound heard often; `bus` is effects, ui or ambience.\n *\n * @example\n * {{name}}.id; // 'sfx:{{name}}'\n * @see {{id}}.test.ts\n */\nimport { defineSfx } from '../../../engine';\n\n/** The effect `sfx:{{name}}`: replace this sentence with what it is the sound of. */\nexport const {{name}} = defineSfx('sfx:{{name}}', {\n  voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 440, to: 880, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.25 },\n  variants: 4,\n});\n/**\n * @file The song `song:{{name}}`: where it plays and its mood (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\n *\n * Invariants: tracker notation, one token per step: a note (C4, F#3, Bb2), - holding the note before it, . a rest,\n * and | a bar line, which takes no step; a drums track writes the kit's tokens (k kick, s snare, h hat, o open hat,\n * c crash, t tom). At `steps` per beat and `beats` per bar, every track fills whole bars or divides one (node x\n * describe song lists the fields; engine/audio/data/song.ts gives the rules). `intensity` makes a track join only\n * when the music's intensity reaches it.\n *\n * @example\n * import { songTiming } from '../../../engine';\n * songTiming({{name}}).seconds; // 4: two bars of 4/4 at 120 bpm\n * @see {{id}}.test.ts\n */\nimport { defineSong } from '../../../engine';\n\n/** The song `song:{{name}}`: replace this sentence with where it plays. */\nexport const {{name}} = defineSong('song:{{name}}', {\n  bpm: 120,\n  tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: 0.12, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - E5 - D5 - F5 - A5 - G5 - | E5 - - - D5 - - - C5 - - - - - . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.25, notes: 'C3 - - - G2 - - - C3 - - - G2 - - - | C3 - - - G2 - - - C3 - - - . . . .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: 0.12, intensity: 0.25, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h . s . h h' },\n  ],\n});\n....\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:2: * @file The look `look:playground-pixel`, the playground as pixel art (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.2, PLAN.md WP 13.24): a\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:18: * look.id; // 'look:playground-pixel'\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:23:import { defineLook } from '../../../engine';\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:26:/** The look `look:playground-pixel`: a low-resolution picture, ramps dithered on the world, snapped and gliding. */\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:27:export const look = defineLook('look:playground-pixel', {\nlabs/playground/looks/pixel.ts:34:  perspective: 'look:playground-pixel-perspective',\nlabs/playground/looks/pixelPerspective.ts:2: * @file The look `look:playground-pixel-perspective`, the pixel look's variant for the perspective cameras (first\nlabs/playground/looks/pixelPerspective.ts:4: * toon numbers in place of `look:playground-pixel`'s while the camera is a perspective one (the look's `perspective`,\n/**\n * @file The look `look:playground-clean`, the playground's default (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.2; the owner's direction of\n * 2026-11-03, ADR-0025 amendment 46): the picture as the scene draws it, unstyled: every material in the set's own\n * lit style (`style` left `''`), lit by the hour's sky (`sky:daylight`, engine/gfx/daylight.ts: the sun, the moon,\n * the ambient and the streetlights at dusk, as the other two looks have them), its dome as the day draws it (no\n * gradient), and edges smoothed (the `aa` filter: the engine's edge smoothing, FXAA unless the view setting `post.aa`\n * names another, engine/gfx/post/aa.ts), with no bands, ink, outline shells, pixels or grade. The engine's own\n * `look:clean` would keep the stage's own lights (a hemisphere and one sun under a plain background,\n * engine/gfx/stageSky.ts), which the hour and the lamps never reach, and smooth nothing.\n *\n * Drawn at the screen's full resolution (`resolution: 'full'`, while `gfx.resolution` is `auto`) with every texture\n * blended (`textures: 'smooth'`: linear filtering, so a floor up close is not a grid of 6 cm squares), the owner's\n * direction of 2026-11-03 (WP 13.30, ADR-0025 amendment 47): the engine's own `pixels` resolution and crisp texels\n * are the pixel look's.\n *\n * Invariants: data only, the kind's fields (`node x describe look`); the sky `sky:daylight`; the scene's own style;\n * every filter it leaves out off. The page draws it by default (labs/playground/main.ts); P steps on to the cel look,\n * then the pixel look.\n *\n * @example\n * look.id; // 'look:playground-clean'\n * look.filters.aa.scope; // 'all': its edges smoothed\n * [look.resolution, look.textures]; // ['full', 'smooth']\n * @see labs/playground/looks/looks.test.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SMTFS2HAD96BCRFCzAVmAN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
