.751s\nuser\t0m3.330s\nsys\t0m0.685s\nbot.replay.json\n# The 3D kit\n\nGames using the shared kit run on one foundation. Imported games that retain\ntheir own engine version use the separate shelf in `../vendor/README.md`.\n\n| Piece | Version | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| three.js | r186 (0.186.1), `WebGPURenderer` from `three/webgpu`, WebGL2 fallback | `/lib/three/` |\n| Rapier | 0.20.0 (SIMD build where wasm SIMD exists, plain build otherwise) | `/lib/rapier/` |\n| The kit | boot, renderer, quality tiers, settings menu, input, touch, physics, post, points | `/lib/kit/` |\n\nThe rule of thumb: **share the foundation, not the gameplay.** Hosting, startup,\nrenderer setup, quality tiers, the settings panel, input plumbing and physics\nsetup come from here. Every game keeps its own mechanics, feel and art. Games\nstay comparable because they follow the same conventions (versions, units,\naction names), not because they share gameplay code.\n\n`example.html` in this folder is a complete small game that uses every piece.\nRead it before migrating anything.\n\nREADME.md\nboot.js\nexample.html\ninput.js\ninstancing.js\nloop.js\nphysics.js\npoints.js\npost.js\nrenderer.js","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"9193f087-a4a3-43dc-be2f-8a49511dfa56","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:47:42.209Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"engine/audio/runtime/mixer.ts:36:export type AudioBus = (typeof BUSES)[number];\n117:  readonly lastDevice: DeviceKind;\n293:    get lastDevice() {\n57:  yaw(): number;\n107:  use(map: string | Bindings): Bindings;\n109:  bindingsFor(map: string): Bindings;\n126:  sample(camera?: CameraLike, now?: number): Record<string, unknown>;\n128:  held(action: string): boolean;\n130:  pressed(action: string): boolean;\n132:  strength(action: string): number;\n134:  camera(): CameraInputSample;\n136:  prompt(action: string): string;\n138:  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\n140: