{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01251EVs4QyL7gAVMSjPQ4eu","type":"tool_result","content":"4: * the layout, so WASD stays under the left hand on AZERTY; mouse buttons and the wheel are `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`,\n5: * `MouseMiddle`, `MouseBack`, `MouseForward`, `WheelUp` and `WheelDown`; gamepad buttons follow the W3C standard\n21: * for `Mouse…` and `Wheel…`, `touch` for `touch:…`, `keyboard` otherwise (a held binding its code's); `PAD_BUTTONS[i]`\n91:export const MOUSE_BUTTONS = ['MouseLeft', 'MouseMiddle', 'MouseRight', 'MouseBack', 'MouseForward'] as const;\n94:export const WHEEL_CODES = ['WheelUp', 'WheelDown'] as const;\n144:  return code.startsWith('Mouse') || code.startsWith('Wheel') ? 'mouse' : 'keyboard';\n156:  MouseLeft: 'LMB',\n157:  MouseMiddle: 'MMB',\n38:export type DeviceKind = 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch' | 'virtual';\n/**\n * @file The overlay's widgets (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 10.6, I-50; doctrine: Verifiable without a display): bars, hearts and\n * boxes as HTML/CSS elements, each marked `data-ui` so `ui.state()` (engine/ui/state.ts) and DOM queries read it as\n * text, a value and a box, never as pixels; and what the dialog and the menu share (engine/ui/{dialog,menu}.ts).\n *\n * - `createBar(parent, { id, value, max, label, color })`: a filled bar (a health, magic or boss bar): `data-ui=bar`,\n *   `data-value` its fill from 0 to 1, its text the label and the value (`HP 30/40`).\n * - `createHearts(parent, { id, hp, max })`: a row of `max` hearts (rounded up), each full, half or empty by `hp`\n *   (halves count): `data-ui=hearts`, `data-value` `hp/max`, a heart per `data-fill`.\n * - `createBox(parent, { id, title, text })`: a window frame, Final Fantasy's soft gradient in a light rim, a title and\n *   a body (`data-ui=box`); the dialog and the menu draw theirs alike.\n * Each returns its element, `set(…)` (the new numbers or text, changing the page only where they differ) and\n * `remove()`. Put a HUD widget in a HUD place with `overlay.attach(widget.el, at)` (engine/ui/overlay.ts).\n *\n8:94-  /** The root element (`.ui-overlay`), over the canvas. */\n9:95-  readonly root: HTMLElement;\n11:97-  label(text: string, options: LabelOptions): Label;\n13:99-  damage(value: number | string, options: DamageOptions): void;\n15:101-  hud(id: string, text: string | null, options?: HudOptions): void;\n18:104-  /** Shows or hides the crosshair at the canvas's centre. */\n19:105-  crosshair(on: boolean): void;\n/**\n * @file A Vite dev server through Vite's JavaScript API, for the `x` commands that open pages (PLAN.md §8.1). It\n * serves the repository with `vite.config.ts`, as `npm run dev` and Playwright's `webServer` do.\n *\n * Invariants: it listens on 127.0.0.1; on a free port chosen by the system unless one is asked for, so it never\n * collides with a lane's `$PORT`; `close()` stops it.\n *\n * @example\n * const server = await startVite();\n * const page = `${server.url}tests/pages/harness.html`;\n * await server.close();\n * @see tools/lib/vite.test.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"4ef08499-c81e-4a81-8383-1bcda29da21b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:43.313Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"4: * the layout, so WASD stays under the left hand on AZERTY; mouse buttons and the wheel are `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`,\n5: * `MouseMiddle`, `MouseBack`, `MouseForward`, `WheelUp` and `WheelDown`; gamepad buttons follow the W3C standard\n21: * for `Mouse…` and `Wheel…`, `touch` for `touch:…`, `keyboard` otherwise (a held binding its code's); `PAD_BUTTONS[i]`\n91:export const MOUSE_BUTTONS = ['MouseLeft', 'MouseMiddle', 'MouseRight', 'MouseBack', 'MouseForward'] as const;\n94:export const WHEEL_CODES = ['WheelUp', 'WheelDown'] as const;\n144:  return code.startsWith('Mouse') || code.startsWith('Wheel') ? 'mouse' : 'keyboard';\n156:  MouseLeft: 'LMB',\n157:  MouseMiddle: 'MMB',\n38:export type DeviceKind = 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch' | 'virtual';\n/**\n * @file The overlay's widgets (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 10.6, I-50; doctrine: Verifiable without a display): bars, hearts and\n * boxes as HTML/CSS elements, each marked `data-ui` so `ui.state()` (engine/ui/state.ts) and DOM queries read it as\n * text, a value and a box, never as pixels; and what the dialog and the menu share (engine/ui/{dialog,menu}.ts).\n *\n * - `createBar(parent, { id, value, max, label, color })`: a filled bar (a health, magic or boss bar): `data-ui=bar`,\n *   `data-value` its fill from 0 to 1, its text the label and the value (`HP 30/40`).\n * - `createHearts(parent, { id, hp, max })`: a row of `max` hearts (rounded up), each full, half or empty by `hp`\n *   (halves count): `data-ui=hearts`, `data-value` `hp/max`, a heart per `data-fill`.\n * - `createBox(parent, { id, title, text })`: a window frame, Final Fantasy's soft gradient in a light rim, a title and\n *   a body (`data-ui=box`); the dialog and the menu draw theirs alike.\n * Each returns its element, `set(…)` (the new numbers or text, changing the page only where they differ) and\n * `remove()`. Put a HUD widget in a HUD place with `overlay.attach(widget.el, at)` (engine/ui/overlay.ts).\n *\n8:94-  /** The root element (`.ui-overlay`), over the canvas. */\n9:95-  readonly root: HTMLElement;\n11:97-  label(text: string, options: LabelOptions): Label;\n13:99-  damage(value: number | string, options: DamageOptions): void;\n15:101-  hud(id: string, text: string | null, options?: HudOptions): void;\n18:104-  /** Shows or hides the crosshair at the canvas's centre. */\n19:105-  crosshair(on: boolean): void;\n/**\n * @file A Vite dev server through Vite's JavaScript API, for the `x` commands that open pages (PLAN.md §8.1). It\n * serves the repository with `vite.config.ts`, as `npm run dev` and Playwright's `webServer` do.\n *\n * Invariants: it listens on 127.0.0.1; on a free port chosen by the system unless one is asked for, so it never\n * collides with a lane's `$PORT`; `close()` stops it.\n *\n * @example\n * const server = await startVite();\n * const page = `${server.url}tests/pages/harness.html`;\n * await server.close();\n * @see tools/lib/vite.test.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01251EVs4QyL7gAVMSjPQ4eu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
