{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBpdVgpejiBjA5SibSL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017hNZvhNJs8WV55TLhAafzz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b) if count==0 else s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# Originality: the source's subtitle is not a case title or a stinger.\nrep('''source's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks. Nothing else\ndoes.''','''source's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks; nothing else\ndoes. \"Second opinion\" appears only as the ordinary phrase, in dialogue.''')\nrep('| 5 | Second Opinion | Sabine, AI |','| 5 | Struck Off | Sabine, AI |')\nrep('5. **Second Opinion** (70).','5. **Struck Off** (70).')\nrep('with a big \"SECOND OPINION!\"\\n  stinger.','with a big \"CONSULT!\"\\n  stinger.')\n\n# Seats: who plays whom, and where the AI colleague appears.\nrep('''- **Solo:** seat 0. An **AI colleague** in seat 1 in Cases 5 to 7: the bot's policy (§17.6) limited to holding flaps, draining\n  and clearing small things, at reduced speed. It teaches co-op without a second human.''','''- **Solo:** seat 0. An **AI colleague** in seat 1 in Cases 5 to 8: the bot's policy (§17.6) limited to holding flaps, draining\n  and clearing small things, at reduced speed. It teaches co-op without a second human.\n- **Who plays whom:** seat 0 is the case's lead; seat 1 is the other surgeon where a case has both; any other seat is a resident\n  with no Gift.''')\nrep('''- **In Case 6**, a solo player also gets **Swap** (R3 or Tab): take over the other surgeon. The AI takes yours.''','''- **In Cases 6 to 8**, a solo player also gets **Swap** (R3 or Tab): take over the other surgeon. The AI takes yours.''')\nrep('| R3 | Swap surgeon (Case 6) |','| R3 | Swap surgeon (Cases 6 to 8) |')\n\n# Ranks are written by a tool, not by a test.\nrep('the bot scores on Resident, computed by a test and written into the case data.','the bot scores on Resident, computed by a tool and written into the case data; a test checks they are current.')\nrep('  ranks: [/* written by a test */],','  ranks: [/* written by the rank tool */],')\n\n# Mouse: things in the world.\nrep('''The tool bar is clickable. Shift: precision.''','''The tool bar, site tabs and Board cards are clickable, and hovering a valid target highlights it. Shift: precision.''')\n\n# Boot: no WebGPU.\nrep('''- **Boot/Loading:** dark, lighthouse beam, status text; the engine error text stays visible if startup fails.''','''- **Boot/Loading:** dark, lighthouse beam, status text; the engine error text stays visible if startup fails. With no WebGPU (the engine has no fallback), show a large plain message saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, with `AIHub.fail` in a session.''')\n\n# Dialog in play.\nrep('(`createDialog` with `modal: false`)','(`createDialog` with `modal: false` and `auto`)')\n\n# Performance.\nrep('''**Palette.** Harbor Light:''','''**Detail.** TASK.md's performance budget is unlimited, and FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope. Add as much geometry, effects, lights and shadows as a scene needs.\n\n**Palette.** Harbor Light:''')\n\n# Animation: how story actors are made.\nrep('''**New actions** (`labs/game/cast/actions/`),''','''**Story actors** are `spawnActor` with their `body` and `anim: { build }`, not player-controlled; they play actions with `actOn` and clips with `playClip`.\n\n**New actions** (`labs/game/cast/actions/`),''')\n\n# The /tmp exception, stated plainly.\nrep('''1. **A long `TMPDIR` breaks tools silently.** The run's `TMPDIR` is too long for a Unix socket path. Chromium dies with `Socket path too long` and `node x shot` then hung for over 4 minutes; `npx tsx` fails with `EINVAL`. Use the short private directory above in every shell (shell state does not persist between tool calls, so put it in your commands or a script), and remove it when you finish.''','''1. **A long `TMPDIR` breaks tools silently.** The run's `TMPDIR` is too long for a Unix socket path. Chromium dies with `Socket path too long` and `node x shot` then hung for over 4 minutes; `npx tsx` fails with `EINVAL`. Use the short private directory above in every shell (shell state may not persist between tool calls, so put it in your commands or a script), and remove it when you finish. This is the one exception to TASK.md's rule against `/tmp`: no path inside your folder is short enough for the sockets. Keep your real files in your folder.''')\nrep('''9. Golden replays break whenever play changes on purpose: `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`.''','''9. Golden replays break whenever play changes on purpose: `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`.\n10. You share this machine. Stay in your own folder, keep one or two browsers open, and stop only processes you started, by PID. The `x` commands pick a free port by themselves.''')\n\n# Session: seed and a lone player.\nrep('''Run `case:gala-shift` with seed `info.seed`, seats = players.''','''Run `case:gala-shift` with seed `info.seed` (the same on every copy), seats = players. A lone player gets the AI colleague, added by the host.''')\n\n# Tests.\nrep('''- Touch profile: exact message, settings button works, no touch stick, attract runs.''','''- Touch profile: exact message, settings button works, no touch stick, attract runs.\n- No WebGPU: Firefox and WebKit here have WebGL only, so open the file there and expect the plain message, with no crash.''')\n\n# Coverage table.\nrep('| Performance unlimited, FPS out of scope | §11 sheet density, §12 |','| Performance unlimited, FPS out of scope | §11 |')\nrep('| This computer: stand-ins for pad, touch, audio, second player, TV | §17.1, §19 |','| This computer: stand-ins for pad, touch, audio, second player, TV; shared machine | §10, §16, §17.1, §19 |')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\n\nimport re\nprint('words',len(s.split()),'bytes',len(s.encode()))\nfor bad in ['exit-interview','GameTitle','.scratch','Second Opinion |','SECOND OPINION','claude-opus']:\n    print(bad, s.count(bad))\nheads=re.findall(r'^#+ .*$',s,flags=re.M)\nprint('\\n'.join(heads))\nEOF","description":"Apply review fixes to PLAN.md and check for names it must leave out"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30741,"cache_read_input_tokens":422352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30741},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"2b919c50-cd85-4ad7-b878-8dff32a30cf1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:58:11.559Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBpd8MqFDcmGq4sB3Gp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017hNZvhNJs8WV55TLhAafzz":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b) if count==0 else s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# Originality: the source's subtitle is not a case title or a stinger.\nrep('''source's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks. Nothing else\ndoes.''','''source's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks; nothing else\ndoes. \"Second opinion\" appears only as the ordinary phrase, in dialogue.''')\nrep('| 5 | Second 