ils. With no WebGPU (the engine has no fallback), show a large plain message saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, with `AIHub.fail` in a session.''')\n\n# Dialog in play.\nrep('(`createDialog` with `modal: false`)','(`createDialog` with `modal: false` and `auto`)')\n\n# Performance.\nrep('''**Palette.** Harbor Light:''','''**Detail.** TASK.md's performance budget is unlimited, and FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope. Add as much geometry, effects, lights and shadows as a scene needs.\n\n**Palette.** Harbor Light:''')\n\n# Animation: how story actors are made.\nrep('''**New actions** (`labs/game/cast/actions/`),''','''**Story actors** are `spawnActor` with their `body` and `anim: { build }`, not player-controlled; they play actions with `actOn` and clips with `playClip`.\n\n**New actions** (`labs/game/cast/actions/`),''')\n\n# The /tmp exception, stated plainly.\nrep('''1. **A long `TMPDIR` breaks tools silently.** The run's `TMPDIR` is too long for a Unix socket path. Chromium dies with `Socket path too long` and `node x shot` then hung for over 4 minutes; `npx tsx` fails with `EINVAL`. Use the short private directory above in every shell (shell state does not persist between tool calls, so put it in your commands or a script), and remove it when you finish.''','''1. **A long `TMPDIR` breaks tools silently.** The run's `TMPDIR` is too long for a Unix socket path. Chromium dies with `Socket path too long` and `node x shot` then hung for over 4 minutes; `npx tsx` fails with `EINVAL`. Use the short private directory above in every shell (shell state may not persist between tool calls, so put it in your commands or a script), and remove it when you finish. This is the one exception to TASK.md's rule against `/tmp`: no path inside your folder is short enough for the sockets. Keep your real files in your folder.''')\nrep('''9. Golden replays break whenever play changes on purpose: `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`.''','''9. Golden replays break whenever play changes on purpose: `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`.\n10. You share this machine. Stay in your own folder, keep one or two browsers open, and stop only processes you started, by PID. The `x` commands pick a free port by themselves.''')\n\n# Session: seed and a lone player.\nrep('''Run `case:gala-shift` with seed `info.seed`, seats = players.''','''Run `case:gala-shift` with seed `info.seed` (the same on every copy), seats = players. A lone player gets the AI colleague, added by the host.''')\n\n# Tests.\nrep('''- Touch profile: exact message, settings button works, no touch stick, attract runs.''','''- Touch profile: exact message, settings button works, no touch stick, attract runs.\n- No WebGPU: Firefox and WebKit here have WebGL only, so open the file there and expect the plain message, with no crash.''')\n\n# Coverage table.\nrep('| Performance unlimited, FPS out of scope | §11 sheet density, §12 |','| Performance unlimited, FPS out of scope | §11 |')\nrep('| This computer: stand-ins for pad, touch, audio, second player, TV | §17.1, §19 |','| This computer: stand-ins for pad, touch, audio, second player, TV; shared machine | §10, §16, §17.1, §19 |')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\n\nimport re\nprint('words',len(s.split()),'bytes',len(s.encode()))\nfor bad in ['exit-interview','GameTitle','.scratch','Second Opinion |','SECOND OPINION','claude-opus']:\n    print(bad, s.count(bad))\nheads=re.findall(r'^#+ .*$',s,flags=re.M)\nprint('\\n'.join(heads))\nEOF","description":"Apply review fixes to PLAN.md and check for names it must leave out"}}}
