{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCbPByAV6WmZ9MGsXXC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both checks passed, and the camera fix works. I'm now writing the hub testing results, including the working boot order, into the plan as a code skeleton.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1776,"cache_read_input_tokens":484797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1776},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"874e5a3c-35fc-4398-8d75-103d54585d78","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:07:12.971Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCbNtrpmy6Nt6itAoQ3","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCbPByAV6WmZ9MGsXXC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UqL7M2cx5PufmGKDixgNMN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:80]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n\n# §16: the tested boot order and netcode.\nrep('''- No title or menus. `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`; on `null`, run as on its own.\n''','''- No title or menus. Boot in the order below; on `connect` giving `null`, run as on its own.\n''')\nrep('''- `AIHub.ready()` once when the engine is ready, with no press. `AIHub.fail(msg)` if WebGPU is missing.\n''','''- `AIHub.ready()` once, with no press, as soon as the sim can run (below). `AIHub.fail(msg)` if WebGPU is missing.\n''')\nrep('''**Netcode: host-sequenced lockstep.** The engine promises''','''**Boot order, tested against the real harness. Each line here fixes a failure seen there.**\n\n```ts\n// labs/game/main.ts, at the very top: nothing heavy before connect, or the hub's 10 s hello window closes\nconst hub = window.AIHub;\nconst info = hub?.active ? await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\n// The hub opens the page with ?aihub=1&aihub-seed=…; the engine reads every query key as a setting and REFUSES TO START (CORE_BAD_SETTING).\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key);\nif (info) { search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); search.set('gfx.warmUp', 'asked'); search.set('game.run', 'op:gala-shift'); }\nif (info) void runSession(info);                // beside createEngine, not after it: its warm-up can take 20 s here\nengine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:main'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\n\nasync function runSession(info) {\n  while (typeof window.__engine?.step !== 'function') await sleep(25);   // about 1 s; long before the warm-up ends\n  const e = window.__engine;\n  e.pause();\n  hub.ready();                                  // the harness waits only 20 s; a four-copy software warm-up reached 21 s on the starter\n  setInterval(() => (info.isHost ? hostTick(e) : clientTick(e)), 16);   // keeps running in a hidden tab, throttled\n}\n```\n\nKeep the card up until `engine.ready`; on real GPUs that is about a second.\n\n**Netcode: host-sequenced lockstep.** The engine promises''')\nrep('''- **Host:** `inspector.pause()`, then its own accumulator: each 1/60 s of hub time, build the tick's `game:hands` and call `inspector.step(1, { 'game:hands': hands })`, then queue it to send.\n- **Client:** `inspector.pause()`, then release buffered ticks with `inspector.step(n, list)`, keeping about 100 ms behind the newest; when more than 500 ms behind, run ×2 to catch up.\n''','''- **Host tick:** `due = floor(AIHub.time() * 60 / 1000)`; while `next < due`, build the tick's hands, `e.step(1, { 'game:hands': hands })`, and queue it. Flush every 66 ms.\n- **Client tick:** step one buffered tick each timer pass; two when more than 6 are queued, eight when more than 30. After `end`, a client may drain what it has, sending nothing.\n''')\nrep('''- Hidden tab: use a timer fallback so a hidden host keeps the world moving and a hidden client catches up on return.\n''','')\nrep('''- If software rendering makes the harness too slow with several frames, reduce sheet density when the adapter is SwiftShader (`__engine.info()`), in a session only.\n''','''- **Tested:** a 70-line prototype of exactly this, on the starter with a 40,000-vertex live mesh and no card, passed all four harness runs below. Every client's hash matched the host's at every check (about one a second), including at `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`.\n- If software rendering makes the harness too slow with your full scenes, reduce sheet density when the adapter is SwiftShader (`__engine.info()`), in a session only.\n''')\nrep('''- `AIHub.server`: the host's copy has no player. It runs the world with `createHeadless` and no rendering, no card input, nothing drawn.\n''','''- `AIHub.server`: the host's copy has no player, camera or input, and draws nothing. The same host code runs the world. Prefer `createHeadless` there, or stop drawing; the prototype passed with the full engine, so this is not a blocker.\n''')\nrep('''Use `&limit=` to shorten rounds. Also open''','''Use `&limit=` to shorten rounds; expose your hash checks on a debug object so the test can read them from each frame and require zero mismatches. Also open''')\n\n# §10: touch tested.\nrep('''No touch controls: start the page with `touch=off` (a view setting, `?touch=off`, or the\nengine shows a touch stick).''','''No touch controls: put `touch=off` in the `search` you give `createEngine`, always, or the engine shows its touch layer (tested on a phone profile: `touch=off` removes it all).''')\n\n# §17.1: traps and the tested list.\nrep('''4. A running page **cannot switch scenes**; the guide's page reload is not allowed in a hub session. Use §17.2.''','''4. A running page **cannot switch scenes**; the guide's page reload is not allowed in a hub session. Use §17.2. **Every query key is read as a setting**: an unknown one stops the engine, which is why §16 strips the hub's.''')\nrep('''Tested and working, so build on these: the live mesh of §17.3, one-file build and boot from `file://`, frames still drawing while paused, `step(n, intents)` with custom keys, restart with new settings keeping the page, custom intents recorded in a replay. **Not tested:** custom camera in play, transparent live meshes, the hub harness on a WebGPU build, the netcode of §16, vertex counts past 40,000. Prove these early.''','''Tested and working, so build on these: the live mesh of §17.3; one-file build and boot from `file://`; frames still drawing while paused; `step(n, intents)` with custom keys; restart with new settings keeping the page; custom intents recorded in a replay; `cam3=fixed` cuts with `{ blend: true }`; `touch=off`; the boot order and netcode of §16 in all four harness runs. **Not tested:** the game's own card in the harness, a `defineCamera` mode in play, transparent live meshes, the light pool's focus (§17.2), vertex counts past 40,000. Prove these early.''')\n\n# §18: client bytes.\nrep('''- A classic inline script in the head stays before the module script after the build (tested). **Test that the pasted `session.js` matches the original byte for byte** and is the first script.''','''- Paste `session.js` into `labs/game/index.html` as the first inline script. Through this build it came out byte-identical and first, and the harness accepted it (tested). Keep a test that says so.''')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint(len(s.split()),'words',len(s.encode()),'bytes')\nEOF\nsed -n '/^## 16/,/^## 17/p' PLAN.md | cut -c1-170 | head -70","description":"Update PLAN.md with tested hub boot order and netcode, then reread the multiplayer section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1776,"cache_read_input_tokens":484797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1776},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"daf2da46-92e4-410c-9612-19bda1976951","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:07:34.285Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCbNtrpmy6Nt6itAoQ3","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UqL7M2cx5PufmGKDixgNMN":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211