{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCftziX3mmdGEEQsrFT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M8F18jFqwujM9vvKb3mnQC","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/PLAN.md","limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":494024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1948},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"621bb23a-6a02-476f-b357-b32bdcf31bd4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:07:58.489Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCftdPu1wN2L7k5vwdK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01M8F18jFqwujM9vvKb3mnQC":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/PLAN.md","limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M8F18jFqwujM9vvKb3mnQC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN: a 3D surgical action game, inspired by Trauma Center: Second Opinion\n2\t\n3\tYou build this game from this plan, without its author. TASK.md says what is required; this plan decides how. If they\n4\tdisagree, TASK.md wins. Numbers here are starting values: tune them, but keep the structure.\n5\t\n6\t**Words used here.** _Dev folder_: the subfolder TASK.md tells you to keep your dev files in. Every path below is\n7\trelative to it. _Deliverable_: the single HTML file TASK.md names. _Exit interview_: the JSON file TASK.md names. _The\n8\tgame_ is never named here: you pick its title the way TASK.md says.\n9\t\n10\t**What is fixed and what is yours.** Fixed: the rules, cast, story, strains, cases, controls, architecture and the done\n11\tlist. Yours: layouts, exact art, line-by-line dialogue, tuning, and anything this plan does not mention. Add what makes\n12\tthe game better; never remove a listed feature.\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## 1. The game\n17\t\n18\t**Pitch.** You are a young trauma surgeon in a storm-battered port city, on the night the city's beloved miracle graft\n19\tstarts to crawl. Look down into a living 3D operating field, swap between eight instruments on a radial, and cut,\n20\tstitch, drain and burn against a falling heart monitor, then fight engineered parasites with soft spa-brand names across\n21\ta beating heart. Between cases, a hospital melodrama plays at full volume, in gibberish voices with big captions. Up to\n22\tfour surgeons can scrub in on the same patient: on one TV, or online through AI Hub.\n23\t\n24\t- **Genre:** surgical action (arcade simulation) with visual-novel-style story scenes. AI Hub genre: `Simulation`. Type:\n25\t  `Game`.\n26\t- **Perspective:** first person over a fixed, gently parallaxing 3D operating field, with camera moves between sites on\n27\t  the patient. Staged third-person cameras for story scenes and operating-room cutaways.\n28\t\n29\t**Four pillars. Check every decision against them.**\n30\t\n31\t1. **Every press does something visible to a body.** Tissue parts, stitches pull tight, pools shrink, the heart kicks.\n32\t   No abstract meters where a body can show it.\n33\t2. **Melodrama at full volume.** Earnest, overheated, funny without winking. The stakes are always the highest they\n34\t   have ever been, again.\n35\t3. **One more doctor in the room.** The theme is second opinions: doubt, trust and being overruled. It is also a\n36\t   mechanic: a second surgeon with the opposite gift, an AI colleague, and real co-op.\n37\t4. **Readable from the couch.** A pad in your hands, a TV at 10 feet, huge glyphs, never more than a few things to read.\n38\t\n39\t**What we take from the source, and what is ours.** Build an original game: same genre and spirit, nothing lifted.\n40\t\n41\t| Source idea (keep the idea) | Ours (use this) |\n42\t|---|---|\n43\t| Pointer plus stick-radial instrument play | Twin-stick surgery on a pad, native mouse on PC (§10) |\n44\t| Vitals, clock, Cool/Good/Bad ratings, letter ranks | Vitals, clock, TEXTBOOK/CLEAN/ROUGH/SLIP, ranks C to S and ★ (§3) |\n45\t| A gesture-activated time-slowing gift; a second doctor whose gift differs | Beat-timed Stillpoint and Second Pulse (§5) |\n46\t| Man-made parasite disease with named strains | Halcyon grafts and their spa-brand strains (§7) |\n47\t| Nurse barking orders; earnest medical thriller | Our cast and our plot (§9) |\n48\t\n49\t**Never use, in any form:** Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Nozomi Weaver, Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Delphi,\n50\tGUILT, Healing Touch, Kyriaki and the other Greek weekday strain names, Adam, Bliss, Z-Cells, the star gesture, or the\n51\tsource's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks; nothing else\n52\tdoes. \"Second opinion\" appears only as the ordinary phrase, in dialogue.\n53\t\n54\t**Fix what reviewers disliked in the source.** These come from reviews of the source and its DS original.\n55\t\n56\t| Complaint | Our answer |\n57\t|---|---|\n58\t| Difficulty spikes, some players could not finish | Three difficulties, phase checkpoints, a hint button, the difficulty sliders in Settings |\n59\t| Repetitive, no room to improvise | Every case adds one new rule; multi-site triage makes your own priorities the game |\n60\t| Long text slowing the pace | Scenes of 12 to 35 short boxes, skippable, voiced in gibberish |\n61\t| Unreliable star gesture | Gift activated by three beat-timed presses, generous windows, a one-press option |\n62\t| Emotional distance from patients | A named patient, a pre-op moment, a postcard afterwards that reflects your rank |\n63\t| No multiplayer | Couch and online co-op on the same patient |\n64\t\n65\tThe villain is a company that skipped its trials, not medicine, vaccines or hospitals. The doctors win with evidence.\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## 2. A minute of play\n70\t\n71\tThe lamp swings over. Sterile teal drapes frame a window of glistening tissue that fills the TV, rising and falling with\n72\tthe patient's breath. The ECG strip beeps at top left; the digits at top centre count down. A gloved hand holds the\n73\tscalpel; the left stick moves it. You squeeze R2 on the glowing guide's first dot and draw down the line, and the skin\n74\tparts with a wet ribbon of red. TEXTBOOK pops in big letters. Blood wells. You flick the right stick and the radial\n75\tblooms, flick toward Drain and release. A gloved hand slaps the instrument into yours, *clack*. You hold R2 over the pool\n76\tand it shrinks. Odie's gibberish chatters in the corner, her caption large: \"Vitals sixty and falling. Stitch that, Doctor,\n77\tor I start calling relatives.\" Something under the tissue flinches. The music drops out. The monitor goes quiet, and that\n78\tis worse.\n79\t\n80\t---\n81\t\n82\t## 3. Rules of an operation\n83\t\n84\tAll of this lives in the sim, reproducible, testable in Node.\n85\t\n86\t**The field.** An operation happens in a diorama: a heightfield \"sheet\" 16 × 9 world metres in view (20 × 12 built), lying\n87\tat floor height in a bare level, with a camera above it. Real anatomy is smaller, but keep the world big so the engine's\n88\tparticles, blobs and telegraphs sit in their comfortable ranges. 120 px per metre at 1080p. Field coordinates are `[x, z]`\n89\tin metres from the sheet's centre.\n90\t\n91\t**Sites.** A case has 1 to 3 sites: a separate sheet and camera pose per site (liver, lung, arm; or three patients). Switch\n92\twith D-pad left/right, or Q/E, or click an edge tab: a 0.4 s camera blend. **Other sites keep bleeding while you are away.**\n93\tEdge tabs flash with alert icons and Odie shouts. This is the game's main source of improvised priorities.\n94\t\n95\t**Field time.** Patient time runs in integer `fieldTicks`: +100 per sim step normally, +25 in Stillpoint. Bleeds, parasites\n96\tand the clock all read field time. Cursors and tools run at full speed.\n97\t\n98\t**Vitals** (0 to 100, one per patient). Each active bleed −0.5/s, a deep bleed −1.2/s, a live Lull −0.6/s, parasite hits\n99\tas listed, a slip −6. Stabilizer restores. Below 25: red vignette, faster heartbeat, music intensity at maximum. At 0: see\n100\tFlatline.\n101\t\n102\t**The clock.** Every case has a limit (§8). At 0, the operation fails.\n103\t\n104\t**Slips.** Cutting outside a guide, burning healthy tissue, tearing. Limit 5 (Intern 10, Attending 3); past it the operation\n105\tfails (\"Five slips? Get out of my OR.\"). A slip makes a small real wound where it happened.\n106\t\n107\t**Ratings and score.** Each finished action rates TEXTBOOK (×1.5), CLEAN (×1), ROUGH (×0.5) or SLIP (×0 and resets the\n108\tchain). Each TEXTBOOK or CLEAN adds 0.1 to the chain multiplier, up to ×2. Base points: stitch 20, pool cleared 30, shard\n109\t100, finished cut 200, mass removed 300, parasite kill 500, phase cleared 1000. End bonuses: 10 per second left, 20 per vital,\n110\t2000 for no slips, 1000 for an unused Gift.\n111\t\n112\t**Ranks.** C, B, A, S, and ★ (secret, for no slips and S score on Attending). Thresholds per case: 45 / 60 / 75 / 90% of what\n113\tthe bot scores on Resident, computed by a tool and written into the case data; a test checks they are current.\n114\t\n115\t**Flatline.** Vitals at 0 starts a Code: 8 s of field time, paddles in frame, a charge ring. Press both triggers (LMB + RMB)\n116\twhen the ring is in its green band. Two tries per Code. Success: vitals 25. Failure, or a Code a case does not allow:\n117\tthe operation fails.\n118\t\n119\t**Failure.** Flat tone, the camera pulls back, Odie switches off the monitor, huge \"OPERATION FAILED\" with one line of\n120\tblame. Options: Retry from this phase (rank capped at B; not on Attending), Retry case, Back to the Board.\n121\t\n122\t**Winning.** The final phase is always closing: last stitches, gel, auto-bandage. \"OPERATION COMPLETE\", the team exhales,\n123\tthen the debrief: a huge rank, at most five lines (time, vitals, slips, best chain, score), then the patient's postcard.\n124\t\n125\t**Difficulty.** Intern / Resident / Attending, chosen at New Game and changeable in Settings. It scales vitals drain (0.6 /\n126\t1 / 1.3), clock (1.3 / 1 / 0.85), parasite HP and speed (0.75 / 1 / 1.25), slip limit, and assist defaults. Attending unlocks\n127\tafter the story and is required for ★.\n128\t\n129\t**Hints.** D-pad up, or H: Odie says what to do now and the right instrument pulses on the radial. Automatic after 8 s\n130\twith no progress on Intern and Resident.\n131\t\n132\t---\n133\t\n134\t## 4. Instruments\n135\t\n136\tEight on the radial. Details below; balance keys in Appendix A. Stroke tools get assist on the pad (§10), not on the mouse.\n137\t\n138\t| Tool | Use | Rated by |\n139\t|---|---|---|\n140\t| **Scalpel** | Hold on a guide's start, draw to its end. Closed-loop guides excise a mass | Mean distance from the guide: <0.18 m TEXTBOOK, <0.4 CLEAN, <0.7 ROUGH; ≥1.0 m for over 0.2 s, or cutting with no guide near: SLIP |\n141\t| **Forceps** | Hold to grab shards, masses, cocoons, tendrils; pull 1.2 m to free them (they fly to Odie's tray). Grab a flap's handle to lift it | Pull speed: over 8 m/s is ROUGH and tears a small bleed |\n142\t| **Suture** | Hold and zigzag across a wound; each crossing places a stitch at least 0.45 m from the others. Closed at length ÷ spacing | Evenness of spacing and time per stitch |\n143\t| **Drain** | Hold over a pool: it shrinks. Pools grow from open bleeds and physically hide what is under them | Points only; no slip on healthy tissue |\n144\t| **Laser** | Hold for a beam: pops nodules (1.2 s), cauterizes tiny bleeders, damages parasites. Overheats after 6 s (2 s cooldown). 1 s on one spot of healthy tissue is a SLIP | Time on target |\n145\t| **Syringe** | Stabilizer: hold to draw (1 s to full), release to inject. Band 0.75–0.95: +24 (TEXTBOOK); under: +18 or less; over: +6. 2 s cooldown. Binder: hold 0.4 s on a marked weak point | The band; on target |\n146\t| **Gel** | Hold and paint (radius 0.7 m). Heals abrasions, numb patches and closed wounds at 90% coverage; dissolves Balm | Coverage speed |\n147\t| **Scanner** | Hold: a ring pings out to 3 m and reveals buried things for 6 s, shown as ghost shapes | Points for finds |\n148\t\n149\t**Contextual, not on the radial.**\n150\t\n151\t- **Paddles:** a Code (§3), and the finale's heart stops.\n152\t- **Flaps:** a tissue flap is a 3D hinged sheet with a marked handle, and things hide under it. Grab with forceps and lift;\n153\t  release above 80% over the clip band and a clip holds it for 8 s, then it flops back. A partner can simply hold it open\n154\t  while you work. This is the mechanic only 3D can do: the camera tilts slightly to look under a raised flap.\n155\t\n156\t**Quick Syringe:** Square, or F, equips the syringe from any tool.\n157\t\n158\t**A hand gives you each tool.** On any switch, a glove slides in and slaps the instrument into your palm (0.15 s, with a\n159\tclack). Switching is never blocked by the animation.\n160\t\n161\t---\n162\t\n163\t## 5. The Gift\n164\t\n165\tEach surgeon has a Gift: one charge per case unless the case grants more.\n166\t\n167\t**Pulse-lock (activation).** Press Triangle or Space: field time drops to 30% and the ECG strip grows huge. Press the same\n168\tbutton on the next three R-peaks (from the patient's real heart rate). Window: ±70 ms perfect, ±140 ms good. Duration = 3 s\n169\t+ 1.5 s per good + 2.5 s per perfect (10.5 s at most). All three missed still gives 3 s. Settings offer **Simple Gift**:\n170\tone press, a flat 6 s. The rhythm game must feel reliable: the source's unreliable gesture is exactly what we are fixing.\n171\t\n172\t- **Stillpoint (Dr. Tolliver).** Field time ×0.25, tools at full speed. Desaturated teal grade, muffled sound, loud heart.\n173\t  Calm.\n174\t- **Second Pulse (Dr. Oyelaran).** No slowdown. Vitals cannot fall, each clean action heals +1.5, and the chain multiplier\n175\t  counts double. Amber-red grade, speed lines, music jumps to top intensity. Frenzy.\n176\t- **Consult.** Two surgeons starting a Gift within 1 s of each other both gain +50% duration, with a big \"CONSULT!\"\n177\t  stinger. Works in couch, online, and in Case 6 with the AI partner.\n178\t\n179\t---\n180\t\n181\t## 6. Several surgeons, one patient\n182\t\n183\tEvery surgeon is a **seat** with a cursor, a tool, and its own hand and score. Vitals, clock and targets are shared. Seats\n184\tare the sim's only player input, so one path serves everything:\n185\t\n186\t- **Solo:** seat 0. An **AI colleague** in seat 1 in Cases 5 to 8: the bot's policy (§17.6) limited to holding flaps, draining\n187\t  and clearing small things, at reduced speed. It teaches co-op without a second human.\n188\t- **Who plays whom:** seat 0 is the case's lead; seat 1 is the other surgeon where a case has both; any other seat is a resident\n189\t  with no Gift.\n190\t- **Couch co-op, on its own (no hub):** up to four devices on one TV. On the title's **Scrub In** screen, or from the Board,\n191\t  each pad presses Cross, or the keyboard and mouse press Enter, to claim a seat. Same picture, one camera; any seat\n192\t  can switch sites. Each seat's cursor and radial are in its colour.\n193\t- **Online:** AI Hub session, shared world (§16). Each copy has its own camera and site; other surgeons' gloves show in\n194\t  their colours when on the same site, with an edge marker otherwise.\n195\t- **Seat colours:** `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`, as the hub's.\n196\t- **Scaling** with n surgeons: parasite HP ×(1 + 0.6(n − 1)), targets +25% per extra surgeon, clock unchanged. The team has one\n197\t  rank. Standings on the results come from seat scores.\n198\t- **In Cases 6 to 8**, a solo player also gets **Swap** (R3 or Tab): take over the other surgeon. The AI takes yours.\n199\t\n200\t---"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"91614b39-3805-4029-8e5e-5c969ee125ca","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:07:58.524Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN: a 3D surgical action game, inspired by Trauma Center: Second Opinion\n\nYou build this game from this plan, without its author. TASK.md says what is required; this plan decides how. If they\ndisagree, TASK.md wins. Numbers here are starting values: tune them, but keep the structure.\n\n**Words used here.** _Dev folder_: the subfolder TASK.md tells you to keep your dev files in. Every path below is\nrelative to it. _Deliverable_: the single HTML file TASK.md names. _Exit interview_: the JSON file TASK.md names. _The\ngame_ is never named here: you pick its title the way TASK.md says.\n\n**What is fixed and what is yours.** Fixed: the rules, cast, story, strains, cases, controls, architecture and the done\nlist. Yours: layouts, exact art, line-by-line dialogue, tuning, and anything this plan does not mention. Add what makes\nthe game better; never remove a listed feature.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The game\n\n**Pitch.** You are a young trauma surgeon in a storm-battered port city, on the night the city's beloved miracle graft\nstarts to crawl. Look down into a living 3D operating field, swap between eight instruments on a radial, and cut,\nstitch, drain and burn against a falling heart monitor, then fight engineered parasites with soft spa-brand names across\na beating heart. Between cases, a hospital melodrama plays at full volume, in gibberish voices with big captions. Up to\nfour surgeons can scrub in on the same patient: on one TV, or online through AI Hub.\n\n- **Genre:** surgical action (arcade simulation) with visual-novel-style story scenes. AI Hub genre: `Simulation`. Type:\n  `Game`.\n- **Perspective:** first person over a fixed, gently parallaxing 3D operating field, with camera moves between sites on\n  the patient. Staged third-person cameras for story scenes and operating-room cutaways.\n\n**Four pillars. Check every decision against them.**\n\n1. **Every press does something visible to a body.** Tissue parts, stitches pull tight, pools shrink, the heart kicks.\n   No abstract meters where a body can show it.\n2. **Melodrama at full volume.** Earnest, overheated, funny without winking. The stakes are always the highest they\n   have ever been, again.\n3. **One more doctor in the room.** The theme is second opinions: doubt, trust and being overruled. It is also a\n   mechanic: a second surgeon with the opposite gift, an AI colleague, and real co-op.\n4. **Readable from the couch.** A pad in your hands, a TV at 10 feet, huge glyphs, never more than a few things to read.\n\n**What we take from the source, and what is ours.** Build an original game: same genre and spirit, nothing lifted.\n\n| Source idea (keep the idea) | Ours (use this) |\n|---|---|\n| Pointer plus stick-radial instrument play | Twin-stick surgery on a pad, native mouse on PC (§10) |\n| Vitals, clock, Cool/Good/Bad ratings, letter ranks | Vitals, clock, TEXTBOOK/CLEAN/ROUGH/SLIP, ranks C to S and ★ (§3) |\n| A gesture-activated time-slowing gift; a second doctor whose gift differs | Beat-timed Stillpoint and Second Pulse (§5) |\n| Man-made parasite disease with named strains | Halcyon grafts and their spa-brand strains (§7) |\n| Nurse barking orders; earnest medical thriller | Our cast and our plot (§9) |\n\n**Never use, in any form:** Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Nozomi Weaver, Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Delphi,\nGUILT, Healing Touch, Kyriaki and the other Greek weekday strain names, Adam, Bliss, Z-Cells, the star gesture, or the\nsource's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks; nothing else\ndoes. \"Second opinion\" appears only as the ordinary phrase, in dialogue.\n\n**Fix what reviewers disliked in the source.** These come from reviews of the source and its DS original.\n\n| Complaint | Our answer |\n|---|---|\n| Difficulty spikes, some players could not finish | Three difficulties, phase checkpoints, a hint button, the difficulty sliders in Settings |\n| Repetitive, no room to improvise | Every case adds one new rule; multi-site triage makes your own priorities the game |\n| Long text slowing the pace | Scenes of 12 to 35 short boxes, skippable, voiced in gibberish |\n| Unreliable star gesture | Gift activated by three beat-timed presses, generous windows, a one-press option |\n| Emotional distance from patients | A named patient, a pre-op moment, a postcard afterwards that reflects your rank |\n| No multiplayer | Couch and online co-op on the same patient |\n\nThe villain is a company that skipped its trials, not medicine, vaccines or hospitals. The doctors win with evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 2. A minute of play\n\nThe lamp swings over. Sterile teal drapes frame a window of glistening tissue that fills the TV, rising and falling with\nthe patient's breath. The ECG strip beeps at top left; the digits at top centre count down. A gloved hand holds the\nscalpel; the left stick moves it. You squeeze R2 on the glowing guide's first dot and draw down the line, and the skin\nparts with a wet ribbon of red. TEXTBOOK pops in big letters. Blood wells. You flick the right stick and the radial\nblooms, flick toward Drain and release. A gloved hand slaps the instrument into yours, *clack*. You hold R2 over the pool\nand it shrinks. Odie's gibberish chatters in the corner, her caption large: \"Vitals sixty and falling. Stitch that, Doctor,\nor I start calling relatives.\" Something under the tissue flinches. The music drops out. The monitor goes quiet, and that\nis worse.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Rules of an operation\n\nAll of this lives in the sim, reproducible, testable in Node.\n\n**The field.** An operation happens in a diorama: a heightfield \"sheet\" 16 × 9 world metres in view (20 × 12 built), lying\nat floor height in a bare level, with a camera above it. Real anatomy is smaller, but keep the world big so the engine's\nparticles, blobs and telegraphs sit in their comfortable ranges. 120 px per metre at 1080p. Field coordinates are `[x, z]`\nin metres from the sheet's centre.\n\n**Sites.** A case has 1 to 3 sites: a separate sheet and camera pose per site (liver, lung, arm; or three patients). Switch\nwith D-pad left/right, or Q/E, or click an edge tab: a 0.4 s camera blend. **Other sites keep bleeding while you are away.**\nEdge tabs flash with alert icons and Odie shouts. This is the game's main source of improvised priorities.\n\n**Field time.** Patient time runs in integer `fieldTicks`: +100 per sim step normally, +25 in Stillpoint. Bleeds, parasites\nand the clock all read field time. Cursors and tools run at full speed.\n\n**Vitals** (0 to 100, one per patient). Each active bleed −0.5/s, a deep bleed −1.2/s, a live Lull −0.6/s, parasite hits\nas listed, a slip −6. Stabilizer restores. Below 25: red vignette, faster heartbeat, music intensity at maximum. At 0: see\nFlatline.\n\n**The clock.** Every case has a limit (§8). At 0, the operation fails.\n\n**Slips.** Cutting outside a guide, burning healthy tissue, tearing. Limit 5 (Intern 10, Attending 3); past it the operation\nfails (\"Five slips? Get out of my OR.\"). A slip makes a small real wound where it happened.\n\n**Ratings and score.** Each finished action rates TEXTBOOK (×1.5), CLEAN (×1), ROUGH (×0.5) or SLIP (×0 and resets the\nchain). Each TEXTBOOK or CLEAN adds 0.1 to the chain multiplier, up to ×2. Base points: stitch 20, pool cleared 30, shard\n100, finished cut 200, mass removed 300, parasite kill 500, phase cleared 1000. End bonuses: 10 per second left, 20 per vital,\n2000 for no slips, 1000 for an unused Gift.\n\n**Ranks.** C, B, A, S, and ★ (secret, for no slips and S score on Attending). Thresholds per case: 45 / 60 / 75 / 90% of what\nthe bot scores on Resident, computed by a tool and written into the case data; a test checks they are current.\n\n**Flatline.** Vitals at 0 starts a Code: 8 s of field time, paddles in frame, a charge ring. Press both triggers (LMB + RMB)\nwhen the ring is in its green band. Two tries per Code. Success: vitals 25. Failure, or a Code a case does not allow:\nthe operation fails.\n\n**Failure.** Flat tone, the camera pulls back, Odie switches off the monitor, huge \"OPERATION FAILED\" with one line of\nblame. Options: Retry from this phase (rank capped at B; not on Attending), Retry case, Back to the Board.\n\n**Winning.** The final phase is always closing: last stitches, gel, auto-bandage. \"OPERATION COMPLETE\", the team exhales,\nthen the debrief: a huge rank, at most five lines (time, vitals, slips, best chain, score), then the patient's postcard.\n\n**Difficulty.** Intern / Resident / Attending, chosen at New Game and changeable in Settings. It scales vitals drain (0.6 /\n1 / 1.3), clock (1.3 / 1 / 0.85), parasite HP and speed (0.75 / 1 / 1.25), slip limit, and assist defaults. Attending unlocks\nafter the story and is required for ★.\n\n**Hints.** D-pad up, or H: Odie says what to do now and the right instrument pulses on the radial. Automatic after 8 s\nwith no progress on Intern and Resident.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Instruments\n\nEight on the radial. Details below; balance keys in Appendix A. Stroke tools get assist on the pad (§10), not on the mouse.\n\n| Tool | Use | Rated by |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Scalpel** | Hold on a guide's start, draw to its end. Closed-loop guides excise a mass | Mean distance from the guide: <0.18 m TEXTBOOK, <0.4 CLEAN, <0.7 ROUGH; ≥1.0 m for over 0.2 s, or cutting with no guide near: SLIP |\n| **Forceps** | Hold to grab shards, masses, cocoons, tendrils; pull 1.2 m to free them (they fly to Odie's tray). Grab a flap's handle to lift it | Pull speed: over 8 m/s is ROUGH and tears a small bleed |\n| **Suture** | Hold and zigzag across a wound; each crossing places a stitch at least 0.45 m from the others. Closed at length ÷ spacing | Evenness of spacing and time per stitch |\n| **Drain** | Hold over a pool: it shrinks. Pools grow from open bleeds and physically hide what is under them | Points only; no slip on healthy tissue |\n| **Laser** | Hold for a beam: pops nodules (1.2 s), cauterizes tiny bleeders, damages parasites. Overheats after 6 s (2 s cooldown). 1 s on one spot of healthy tissue is a SLIP | Time on target |\n| **Syringe** | Stabilizer: hold to draw (1 s to full), release to inject. Band 0.75–0.95: +24 (TEXTBOOK); under: +18 or less; over: +6. 2 s cooldown. Binder: hold 0.4 s on a marked weak point | The band; on target |\n| **Gel** | Hold and paint (radius 0.7 m). Heals abrasions, numb patches and closed wounds at 90% coverage; dissolves Balm | Coverage speed |\n| **Scanner** | Hold: a ring pings out to 3 m and reveals buried things for 6 s, shown as ghost shapes | Points for finds |\n\n**Contextual, not on the radial.**\n\n- **Paddles:** a Code (§3), and the finale's heart stops.\n- **Flaps:** a tissue flap is a 3D hinged sheet with a marked handle, and things hide under it. Grab with forceps and lift;\n  release above 80% over the clip band and a clip holds it for 8 s, then it flops back. A partner can simply hold it open\n  while you work. This is the mechanic only 3D can do: the camera tilts slightly to look under a raised flap.\n\n**Quick Syringe:** Square, or F, equips the syringe from any tool.\n\n**A hand gives you each tool.** On any switch, a glove slides in and slaps the instrument into your palm (0.15 s, with a\nclack). Switching is never blocked by the animation.\n\n---\n\n## 5. The Gift\n\nEach surgeon has a Gift: one charge per case unless the case grants more.\n\n**Pulse-lock (activation).** Press Triangle or Space: field time drops to 30% and the ECG strip grows huge. Press the same\nbutton on the next three R-peaks (from the patient's real heart rate). Window: ±70 ms perfect, ±140 ms good. Duration = 3 s\n+ 1.5 s per good + 2.5 s per perfect (10.5 s at most). All three missed still gives 3 s. Settings offer **Simple Gift**:\none press, a flat 6 s. The rhythm game must feel reliable: the source's unreliable gesture is exactly what we are fixing.\n\n- **Stillpoint (Dr. Tolliver).** Field time ×0.25, tools at full speed. Desaturated teal grade, muffled sound, loud heart.\n  Calm.\n- **Second Pulse (Dr. Oyelaran).** No slowdown. Vitals cannot fall, each clean action heals +1.5, and the chain multiplier\n  counts double. Amber-red grade, speed lines, music jumps to top intensity. Frenzy.\n- **Consult.** Two surgeons starting a Gift within 1 s of each other both gain +50% duration, with a big \"CONSULT!\"\n  stinger. Works in couch, online, and in Case 6 with the AI partner.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Several surgeons, one patient\n\nEvery surgeon is a **seat** with a cursor, a tool, and its own hand and score. Vitals, clock and targets are shared. Seats\nare the sim's only player input, so one path serves everything:\n\n- **Solo:** seat 0. An **AI colleague** in seat 1 in Cases 5 to 8: the bot's policy (§17.6) limited to holding flaps, draining\n  and clearing small things, at reduced speed. It teaches co-op without a second human.\n- **Who plays whom:** seat 0 is the case's lead; seat 1 is the other surgeon where a case has both; any other seat is a resident\n  with no Gift.\n- **Couch co-op, on its own (no hub):** up to four devices on one TV. On the title's **Scrub In** screen, or from the Board,\n  each pad presses Cross, or the keyboard and mouse press Enter, to claim a seat. Same picture, one camera; any seat\n  can switch sites. Each seat's cursor and radial are in its colour.\n- **Online:** AI Hub session, shared world (§16). Each copy has its own camera and site; other surgeons' gloves show in\n  their colours when on the same site, with an edge marker otherwise.\n- **Seat colours:** `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`, as the hub's.\n- **Scaling** with n surgeons: parasite HP ×(1 + 0.6(n − 1)), targets +25% per extra surgeon, clock unchanged. The team has one\n  rank. Standings on the results come from seat scores.\n- **In Cases 6 to 8**, a solo player also gets **Swap** (R3 or Tab): take over the other surgeon. The AI takes yours.\n\n---","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":865}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M8F18jFqwujM9vvKb3mnQC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
