{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCgKPR7GHAgCJycfMwM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018a1RwqCeYP1WiEfRFhSs6m","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/PLAN.md","offset":200,"limit":180},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6489,"cache_read_input_tokens":495972,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6489},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"3127904c-8e0e-408f-9466-97e35c35a2b5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:08:03.222Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCgK643qiSz8B7ooyE7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018a1RwqCeYP1WiEfRFhSs6m":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/PLAN.md","offset":200,"limit":180}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018a1RwqCeYP1WiEfRFhSs6m","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t---\n201\t\n202\t## 7. The strains\n203\t\n204\tHalcyon Biosciences sold grafts under soothing brand names, so each deadly strain has a soft spa-brand name. Numbers are in\n205\tmetres and seconds of field time at ×1. Each strain is data in `labs/game/data/strains.ts` driving one state machine in\n206\t`labs/game/scenes/strains/`.\n207\t\n208\t**All strains share:** a telegraph before every hit (drawn following the sheet's heights; test it with the engine's\n209\t`inTelegraph`), a hit reaction, a colour unique on the tissue, and a 3-note musical signature when first seen.\n210\t\n211\t- **LULL** (Case 4). Blob rig, lilac, radius 0.45, crawls 1.2 m/s. Its aura silently drains vitals and **dims the ECG and its\n212\t  beep** while any Lull lives: the room gets quieter as things get worse. Every 6 s it nuzzles: ring telegraph r 1.2 for 1.5 s,\n213\t  then a numb patch (−2 vitals, −0.2/s until gelled). Laser 1.5 s kills it and leaves a cocoon for the forceps. **The\n214\t  Matron:** radius 1.2, armoured except when yawning (2.5 s every 8 s), when a Binder dose in its maw deals 50%; births one small\n215\t  Lull per 10 s.\n216\t- **SOLACE** (Case 5). Blob with wing-arms, amber, generations of radius 0.9 / 0.6 / 0.35. Hugs blood vessels. A scalpel stroke\n217\t  of at least 1.5 m through it splits it into two of the next generation; laser only works on generation 3 (1 s), and Odie\n218\t  notes \"it likes the warmth.\" After 5 s latched: line telegraph along the vessel for 2 s, then it constricts: a new bleed and −5\n219\t  vitals. Cap 12 alive. **Mother Solace** hides under a flap: someone must hold it open.\n220\t- **REVERIE** (Case 6). A raised ripple moving under the sheet at 3 m/s (real displacement), invisible until scanned. Scanned, it\n221\t  shows for 6 s; hit by laser, it surfaces for 3 s and can take damage (5 s of laser, three exposures). Lance: cone telegraph 1.2\n222\t  s, then a short laceration that turns deep after 20 s. **Decoys:** floaters that pop when scanned. The real one's pulse beats in\n223\t  time with the ECG, so you can hear which it is.\n224\t- **BALM** (Case 7, session case). A lacquer film spreading cell by cell (0.5 m grid) from a translucent Node. Lacquered wounds\n225\t  cannot be stitched or drained. Gel clears a 1 m radius per second. Laser clears faster and costs −0.5 vitals. Kill the Node\n226\t  with 2 Binder doses and its film fades over 6 s. Drains −0.1/s per 10 cells.\n227\t- **MERCY** (Case 8, finale). Floater rig with orbiting motes, white-gold, radius 1.4. She sings, a gibberish choir in the music.\n228\t  Three phases on the beating heart:\n229\t  1. **Anesthesia.** Six motes shield her; laser 0.6 s each, a new one every 8 s. Every 9 s a sleep ring (r 2, 1.5 s) leaves a\n230\t     numb patch that slows the heart until gelled. No motes: exposed for 5 s; three Binder doses move to phase 2.\n231\t  2. **The Kindness.** She stops the heart: a Code that does not cost a try if you land one of two shocks in 8 s. Then three arc\n232\t     rakes leave three lacerations to close in 30 s. Two rounds.\n233\t  3. **Last Rites.** She burrows into the ventricle. A scalpel guide moves with each heartbeat. Then forceps on five tendrils\n234\t     (each re-attaches after 10 s until all are out), then a Gift is granted free and three Binder points must land within it. A\n235\t     final Code restarts the heart, with every surgeon's paddles.\n236\t\n237\t---\n238\t\n239\t## 8. The cases\n240\t\n241\tEight cases, 35 to 50 minutes for a first run, then **Free Surgery**. Each adds one new rule, so the demo shows everything\n242\tthe game does. Phases are data (§17.5) and each phase is a checkpoint. \"AI\" means the AI colleague is present.\n243\t\n244\t| # | Title | Surgeon | Patient | Site(s) | Limit | New here |\n245\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n246\t| 1 | First Cut | Wren | Tomás Reyes, 52, harbor pilot; glass from a deck hatch | Chest | 4:00 | Cursor, radial, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Syringe, Gel |\n247\t| 2 | The Quiet Lump | Wren | Gwen Abara, 34, trumpet player; an old graft scar | Abdomen | 4:30 | Scalpel, Scanner, Laser |\n248\t| 3 | Crosstalk | Wren | Hal Minsky, 58, bus driver; crash on Breakwater Road | Liver, Lung, Arm | 5:00 | Sites, Code, Stillpoint |\n249\t| 4 | It Moves | Wren | Gwen again, in crisis | Abdomen | 5:30 | LULL, Binder |\n250\t| 5 | Struck Off | Sabine, AI | \"Big Ana\" Duarte, stevedore | Abdomen, on a ship | 5:30 | Flaps, SOLACE, Second Pulse, ship roll hazard |\n251\t| 6 | Reverie | Both, Swap | Chief Achterberg | Chest, Abdomen | 6:00 | REVERIE, decoys, Swap, Consult |\n252\t| 7 | Gala Night | Both, AI | Three donors, three tables | Tables A, B, C | 6:30 | BALM, one vitals bar per patient |\n253\t| 8 | Mercy | Both, AI | Dr. Lucan Voss | Heart | 8:00 | MERCY, every tool |\n254\t\n255\t**Phases.**\n256\t\n257\t1. **First Cut** (vitals start at 70; no Gift). Clear 3 pools, with Odie teaching cursor, use and the radial → pull 4 shards → scripted dip to 40,\n258\t   teach the Stabilizer → stitch 3 lacerations → gel and close.\n259\t2. **The Quiet Lump** (85). Curved 7 m incision → laser its tiny bleeders → scan to find a buried mass and 3 nodules, laser the\n260\t   nodules → loop-cut the mass, lift it with forceps. **It flinches.** Drama Cut. → stitch and gel.\n261\t3. **Crosstalk** (60). Each site has 2 wounds and a pool; triage while the others bleed → scripted flatline when the first site\n262\t   closes: teach the Code → 3 arterial bleeds at once, no time left: time slows, teach the pulse-lock, Wren discovers\n263\t   Stillpoint → close across all sites.\n264\t4. **It Moves** (75). Reopen → 3 Lulls in silence, numb patches, the Chief mocking from the gallery → cocoons, tears →\n265\t   the Matron → close.\n266\t5. **Struck Off** (70). Lift and clip a flap; Solace beneath → split and burn generation by generation → **the storm hits**: the\n267\t   ship rolls every 7 s (camera tilts up to 6°, cursor drifts, instruments slide); teach Second Pulse → Mother Solace under\n268\t   the flap, Wren holding it → close, still rolling.\n269\t6. **Reverie** (65). Two incisions, one on each site, swapping surgeons → hunt with the Scanner, 3 exposures → decoy storm, listen\n270\t   for the beat → the Reverie under the heart flap; Consult → close.\n271\t7. **Gala Night** (each table 80). Three bleeding patients while Balm spreads; a Code allowed once per patient; losing any patient fails\n272\t   the case → Nodes on every table → a final closing race. Voss's speech keeps playing on a big screen throughout.\n273\t8. **Mercy** (100). Open → the three-phase boss of §7 → close. Odie's moral line before it; see §9.\n274\t\n275\t**Session case, \"The Gala Shift\"** (`case:gala-shift`; §16). Not in the story. 4:30 limit. Two patients, wounds, shards, a Lull, a Balm\n276\tNode, one flap. Ends when both are closed (won) or one dies or time runs out (lost). Playable also from Free Surgery for couch play.\n277\t\n278\t**Free Surgery.** After a case is finished, it is on the Board for score attack on any unlocked difficulty, best rank kept, with\n279\tSecond Pulse or Stillpoint selectable. Attending and ★ unlock after the ending.\n280\t\n281\t---\n282\t\n283\t## 9. World, cast, story and writing\n284\t\n285\t**Port Verity**, a rain-lashed harbour city; **Harbor Light General**, its hospital, with a lighthouse for a logo. Near future.\n286\t**Halcyon Biosciences** sells \"Halcyon grafts\": a miracle patch that heals anything, adored by everyone, ads on every ward TV.\n287\tTagline: **\"Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing.\"** The ad has a jingle. The trials were skipped, and the grafts\n288\tare alive.\n289\t\n290\t| Who | Role, attitude | Look | Voice (§13) |\n291\t|---|---|---|---|\n292\t| **Dr. Wren Tolliver** (she/her), 27 | Second-year resident, player. Apologises to unconscious patients. Discovers Stillpoint | Short dark hair, oversized teal scrubs, reading glasses on a cord | Medium-high, quick, trailing off |\n293\t| **Odalys \"Odie\" Ferreira** (she/her), 41 | Charge nurse, voice of every operation. Sarcasm and steel; always two steps ahead | Grey streak, navy scrubs, pens in a bun | Low, dry, clipped |\n294\t| **Dr. Bram Achterberg** (he/him), 60 | Chief of Surgery. Thunder and a huge moustache. \"A surgeon does not feel. A surgeon *finishes*.\" Secretly has a graft | Huge frame, white coat, moustache | Deep, booming, slow |\n295\t| **Dr. Sabine Oyelaran** (she/her), 44 | Struck off for warning about the grafts. Runs a free clinic on a moored hospital ship. Second Pulse | Tall, long coat, close-cropped silver hair | Low-mid, musical |\n296\t| **Dr. Lucan Voss** (he/him), 50 | Founder and TV face of Halcyon. Teeth | Pale suit, immaculate hair, huge smile | High, smooth, sing-song |\n297\t| Patients | Each has a person's detail: Tomás's dog, Gwen's trumpet, Hal's route, Ana's crew | Variations by slots | Variations |\n298\t\n299\t**Outline.** Each scene is 12 to 35 boxes, in a set from §11.\n300\t\n301\t- **Before Case 1.** Storm, night shift, the Halcyon ad on the ward TV. Odie: \"Congratulations, Doctor. You're the only surgeon in the\n302\t  building.\"\n303\t- **After 2.** The mass flinched. Odie saw it. Nobody else will believe it. It is filed as a cyst.\n304\t- **Before 3.** Bus crash; the ER overflows; the Chief throws Wren in.\n305\t- **After 3.** Wren: what happened in there? Odie: \"You were fast. Don't make it weird.\"\n306\t- **Before 4.** Gwen is back, in agony; her scar is moving. The Chief watches from the gallery.\n307\t- **After 4.** The sample vanishes. Halcyon lawyers appear. The Chief suspends Wren. \"You saw a *twitch*, Doctor, at hour nineteen of a\n308\t  shift. Get a second opinion. If you can find a fool to give one.\"\n309\t- **Before 5.** Wren finds Sabine on the ship. Sabine: \"Everyone agreed I was wrong. That is what consensus feels like from the inside.\"\n310\t  A stevedore collapses on deck.\n311\t- **After 5.** The two compare samples. Sabine: \"I'm not a doctor anymore, Dr. Tolliver. I am a second opinion.\"\n312\t- **Before 6.** The Chief collapses at a board meeting and pulls his collar open: his own graft scar.\n313\t- **After 6.** His confession, from the bed: \"I signed the trial. I signed them all.\" He gives them the trial files, and access to the Gala.\n314\t- **Before 7.** Halcyon's gala in the new wing, paid for by Halcyon. Voss on the big screen. Donors begin to fall.\n315\t- **Before 8.** Voss himself is wheeled in: his own product. Odie, quietly: \"We could be slow, Doctor. Nobody would know.\" Wren: \"I\n316\t  would.\"\n317\t- **After 8.** Voss wakes in handcuffs. \"You saved me. That's the one thing I could never have sold.\" Montage of postcards.\n318\t  Then a last beat: a shipping manifest, a crate of grafts already at sea. **\"CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN.\"** Credits. Free Surgery unlocks.\n319\t\n320\t**Writing style.** Earnest, overheated medical thriller. Short, punchy lines; jargon always explained at once; big speeches about duty;\n321\tdramatic reversals; a nurse who is always right. Comedy comes from everyone taking this completely seriously. Two lines per box at\n322\tmost. In operations, lines are one short sentence and never pause play.\n323\t\n324\tLines to set the voice:\n325\t\n326\t> ODIE: \"Scalpel. No, the other end, Doctor.\"\n327\t> WREN: \"I think I've got it.\" CHIEF: \"In my operating room, 'I think' is a cause of death!\"\n328\t> ODIE: \"Vitals sixty and falling. Stitch that, or I start calling relatives.\"\n329\t> VOSS, on TV: \"Pain is just a feeling you haven't paid to remove yet.\"\n330\t> SABINE: \"Your hands are shaking.\" WREN: \"They've never shaken.\" SABINE: \"Then that's new. Use it.\"\n331\t> WREN, to a patient under anaesthetic: \"Sorry. Sorry. Nearly done. Sorry.\"\n332\t> ODIE, at a TEXTBOOK chain: \"Careful, Doctor. People will start to expect it.\"\n333\t\n334\t**Drama Cut.** The game's visual signature, used 6 to 10 times in the story, on reveals. 0.8 s: the camera snaps to a face with a Dutch\n335\ttilt, `post.combine` lays on `look:anime-action` speed lines and cel, the screen shakes, a stinger hits, and a huge caption slams in\n336\t(\"IT MOVED.\"). Then it snaps back.\n337\t\n338\t**Postcards.** After each debrief, a card from the patient, with a line chosen by rank. S: \"Back on the trumpet. Played your name badly on\n339\tpurpose.\" C: \"They say I'll walk fine. They say you looked very worried.\" They collect in the Board's Postcards gallery.\n340\t\n341\t---\n342\t\n343\t## 10. Controls and screens\n344\t\n345\t**Pad (DualSense, or any pad in the standard mapping). This is the design target.**\n346\t\n347\t| Input | Action | Engine code |\n348\t|---|---|---|\n349\t| Left stick | Cursor | read directly (§17.4) |\n350\t| R2 or Cross | Use tool (hold) | `PadRightTrigger`, `PadSouth` |\n351\t| Right stick | Radial: push to open, aim at a tool, release to equip. Field time ×0.6 while open | `PadRightStick*` |\n352\t| L1 / R1 | Previous / next tool | `PadLeftShoulder`, `PadRightShoulder` |\n353\t| L2 | Precision: cursor ×0.4, stronger magnet, slight dolly-in | `PadLeftTrigger` |\n354\t| Triangle | Gift (and the pulse-lock beats) | `PadNorth` |\n355\t| Square | Quick Syringe | `PadWest` |\n356\t| Circle | Drop what forceps hold; cancel the radial | `PadEast` |\n357\t| D-pad left/right | Switch site | `PadLeft`, `PadRight` |\n358\t| D-pad up | Hint | `PadUp` |\n359\t| R3 | Swap surgeon (Cases 6 to 8) | `PadRightStick` |\n360\t| Options | Pause | `PadStart` |\n361\t| L2 + R2 | Paddles, in a Code | triggers |\n362\t\n363\tMenus: D-pad or left stick, Cross accepts, Circle goes back. Both sticks and triggers are analog; use dead zones. In a hub session, ignore\n364\tOptions while Create is held (that chord belongs to the hub).\n365\t\n366\t**Mouse and keyboard. The same game and screens, but native.**\n367\t\n368\t- **Mouse** moves the cursor absolutely, 1:1, no pointer lock, with the OS cursor hidden over the field. LMB uses the tool. **Hold RMB** for the\n369\t  radial at the cursor, flick and release. Wheel cycles tools. Keys **1–8** pick tools directly. The tool bar, site tabs and Board cards are clickable, and hovering a valid target highlights it. Shift: precision. Space:\n370\t  Gift. F: quick Syringe. R: drop. Q/E: sites. H: hint. Tab: swap. Esc: pause. LMB + RMB: paddles.\n371\t- **Keyboard-only** still works: WASD or arrows move the cursor, Enter uses the tool.\n372\t- Every menu: hover moves focus, click picks (`createMenu` already does this; do the same in custom panels). Rebinding in Settings → Controls.\n373\t\n374\t**Cursor feel on a pad (page-side, tune these).** Speed = `cursorSpeed × lean^2.2`. Within 0.6 m of a valid target for the current tool: velocity ×0.55 and a\n375\tgentle pull (the magnet). On a scalpel guide while cutting: the across-line part of stick input ×0.4 (rail assist). Suturing on a wound: a soft clamp\n376\tto ±0.8 m of the wound (sew assist), so you just weave. Mouse gets a light version only, at 0.2 of these strengths.\n377\t\n378\t**Prompts** follow the device used last (`input.lastDevice`). Draw your own glyph set in code (SVG/CSS): PlayStation shapes by default for **any** pad; **Settings →\n379\tControls → Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox** swaps to A B X Y and LB RB LT RT. Don't use `input.prompt()` text directly, as it reads Xbox for unknown pads. Keyboard"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"744ca16b-101d-4da5-9493-240f32bc43d3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:08:03.264Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/PLAN.md","content":"---\n\n## 7. The strains\n\nHalcyon Biosciences sold grafts under soothing brand names, so each deadly strain has a soft spa-brand name. Numbers are in\nmetres and seconds of field time at ×1. Each strain is data in `labs/game/data/strains.ts` driving one state machine in\n`labs/game/scenes/strains/`.\n\n**All strains share:** a telegraph before every hit (drawn following the sheet's heights; test it with the engine's\n`inTelegraph`), a hit reaction, a colour unique on the tissue, and a 3-note musical signature when first seen.\n\n- **LULL** (Case 4). Blob rig, lilac, radius 0.45, crawls 1.2 m/s. Its aura silently drains vitals and **dims the ECG and its\n  beep** while any Lull lives: the room gets quieter as things get worse. Every 6 s it nuzzles: ring telegraph r 1.2 for 1.5 s,\n  then a numb patch (−2 vitals, −0.2/s until gelled). Laser 1.5 s kills it and leaves a cocoon for the forceps. **The\n  Matron:** radius 1.2, armoured except when yawning (2.5 s every 8 s), when a Binder dose in its maw deals 50%; births one small\n  Lull per 10 s.\n- **SOLACE** (Case 5). Blob with wing-arms, amber, generations of radius 0.9 / 0.6 / 0.35. Hugs blood vessels. A scalpel stroke\n  of at least 1.5 m through it splits it into two of the next generation; laser only works on generation 3 (1 s), and Odie\n  notes \"it likes the warmth.\" After 5 s latched: line telegraph along the vessel for 2 s, then it constricts: a new bleed and −5\n  vitals. Cap 12 alive. **Mother Solace** hides under a flap: someone must hold it open.\n- **REVERIE** (Case 6). A raised ripple moving under the sheet at 3 m/s (real displacement), invisible until scanned. Scanned, it\n  shows for 6 s; hit by laser, it surfaces for 3 s and can take damage (5 s of laser, three exposures). Lance: cone telegraph 1.2\n  s, then a short laceration that turns deep after 20 s. **Decoys:** floaters that pop when scanned. The real one's pulse beats in\n  time with the ECG, so you can hear which it is.\n- **BALM** (Case 7, session case). A lacquer film spreading cell by cell (0.5 m grid) from a translucent Node. Lacquered wounds\n  cannot be stitched or drained. Gel clears a 1 m radius per second. Laser clears faster and costs −0.5 vitals. Kill the Node\n  with 2 Binder doses and its film fades over 6 s. Drains −0.1/s per 10 cells.\n- **MERCY** (Case 8, finale). Floater rig with orbiting motes, white-gold, radius 1.4. She sings, a gibberish choir in the music.\n  Three phases on the beating heart:\n  1. **Anesthesia.** Six motes shield her; laser 0.6 s each, a new one every 8 s. Every 9 s a sleep ring (r 2, 1.5 s) leaves a\n     numb patch that slows the heart until gelled. No motes: exposed for 5 s; three Binder doses move to phase 2.\n  2. **The Kindness.** She stops the heart: a Code that does not cost a try if you land one of two shocks in 8 s. Then three arc\n     rakes leave three lacerations to close in 30 s. Two rounds.\n  3. **Last Rites.** She burrows into the ventricle. A scalpel guide moves with each heartbeat. Then forceps on five tendrils\n     (each re-attaches after 10 s until all are out), then a Gift is granted free and three Binder points must land within it. A\n     final Code restarts the heart, with every surgeon's paddles.\n\n---\n\n## 8. The cases\n\nEight cases, 35 to 50 minutes for a first run, then **Free Surgery**. Each adds one new rule, so the demo shows everything\nthe game does. Phases are data (§17.5) and each phase is a checkpoint. \"AI\" means the AI colleague is present.\n\n| # | Title | Surgeon | Patient | Site(s) | Limit | New here |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | First Cut | Wren | Tomás Reyes, 52, harbor pilot; glass from a deck hatch | Chest | 4:00 | Cursor, radial, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Syringe, Gel |\n| 2 | The Quiet Lump | Wren | Gwen Abara, 34, trumpet player; an old graft scar | Abdomen | 4:30 | Scalpel, Scanner, Laser |\n| 3 | Crosstalk | Wren | Hal Minsky, 58, bus driver; crash on Breakwater Road | Liver, Lung, Arm | 5:00 | Sites, Code, Stillpoint |\n| 4 | It Moves | Wren | Gwen again, in crisis | Abdomen | 5:30 | LULL, Binder |\n| 5 | Struck Off | Sabine, AI | \"Big Ana\" Duarte, stevedore | Abdomen, on a ship | 5:30 | Flaps, SOLACE, Second Pulse, ship roll hazard |\n| 6 | Reverie | Both, Swap | Chief Achterberg | Chest, Abdomen | 6:00 | REVERIE, decoys, Swap, Consult |\n| 7 | Gala Night | Both, AI | Three donors, three tables | Tables A, B, C | 6:30 | BALM, one vitals bar per patient |\n| 8 | Mercy | Both, AI | Dr. Lucan Voss | Heart | 8:00 | MERCY, every tool |\n\n**Phases.**\n\n1. **First Cut** (vitals start at 70; no Gift). Clear 3 pools, with Odie teaching cursor, use and the radial → pull 4 shards → scripted dip to 40,\n   teach the Stabilizer → stitch 3 lacerations → gel and close.\n2. **The Quiet Lump** (85). Curved 7 m incision → laser its tiny bleeders → scan to find a buried mass and 3 nodules, laser the\n   nodules → loop-cut the mass, lift it with forceps. **It flinches.** Drama Cut. → stitch and gel.\n3. **Crosstalk** (60). Each site has 2 wounds and a pool; triage while the others bleed → scripted flatline when the first site\n   closes: teach the Code → 3 arterial bleeds at once, no time left: time slows, teach the pulse-lock, Wren discovers\n   Stillpoint → close across all sites.\n4. **It Moves** (75). Reopen → 3 Lulls in silence, numb patches, the Chief mocking from the gallery → cocoons, tears →\n   the Matron → close.\n5. **Struck Off** (70). Lift and clip a flap; Solace beneath → split and burn generation by generation → **the storm hits**: the\n   ship rolls every 7 s (camera tilts up to 6°, cursor drifts, instruments slide); teach Second Pulse → Mother Solace under\n   the flap, Wren holding it → close, still rolling.\n6. **Reverie** (65). Two incisions, one on each site, swapping surgeons → hunt with the Scanner, 3 exposures → decoy storm, listen\n   for the beat → the Reverie under the heart flap; Consult → close.\n7. **Gala Night** (each table 80). Three bleeding patients while Balm spreads; a Code allowed once per patient; losing any patient fails\n   the case → Nodes on every table → a final closing race. Voss's speech keeps playing on a big screen throughout.\n8. **Mercy** (100). Open → the three-phase boss of §7 → close. Odie's moral line before it; see §9.\n\n**Session case, \"The Gala Shift\"** (`case:gala-shift`; §16). Not in the story. 4:30 limit. Two patients, wounds, shards, a Lull, a Balm\nNode, one flap. Ends when both are closed (won) or one dies or time runs out (lost). Playable also from Free Surgery for couch play.\n\n**Free Surgery.** After a case is finished, it is on the Board for score attack on any unlocked difficulty, best rank kept, with\nSecond Pulse or Stillpoint selectable. Attending and ★ unlock after the ending.\n\n---\n\n## 9. World, cast, story and writing\n\n**Port Verity**, a rain-lashed harbour city; **Harbor Light General**, its hospital, with a lighthouse for a logo. Near future.\n**Halcyon Biosciences** sells \"Halcyon grafts\": a miracle patch that heals anything, adored by everyone, ads on every ward TV.\nTagline: **\"Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing.\"** The ad has a jingle. The trials were skipped, and the grafts\nare alive.\n\n| Who | Role, attitude | Look | Voice (§13) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Dr. Wren Tolliver** (she/her), 27 | Second-year resident, player. Apologises to unconscious patients. Discovers Stillpoint | Short dark hair, oversized teal scrubs, reading glasses on a cord | Medium-high, quick, trailing off |\n| **Odalys \"Odie\" Ferreira** (she/her), 41 | Charge nurse, voice of every operation. Sarcasm and steel; always two steps ahead | Grey streak, navy scrubs, pens in a bun | Low, dry, clipped |\n| **Dr. Bram Achterberg** (he/him), 60 | Chief of Surgery. Thunder and a huge moustache. \"A surgeon does not feel. A surgeon *finishes*.\" Secretly has a graft | Huge frame, white coat, moustache | Deep, booming, slow |\n| **Dr. Sabine Oyelaran** (she/her), 44 | Struck off for warning about the grafts. Runs a free clinic on a moored hospital ship. Second Pulse | Tall, long coat, close-cropped silver hair | Low-mid, musical |\n| **Dr. Lucan Voss** (he/him), 50 | Founder and TV face of Halcyon. Teeth | Pale suit, immaculate hair, huge smile | High, smooth, sing-song |\n| Patients | Each has a person's detail: Tomás's dog, Gwen's trumpet, Hal's route, Ana's crew | Variations by slots | Variations |\n\n**Outline.** Each scene is 12 to 35 boxes, in a set from §11.\n\n- **Before Case 1.** Storm, night shift, the Halcyon ad on the ward TV. Odie: \"Congratulations, Doctor. You're the only surgeon in the\n  building.\"\n- **After 2.** The mass flinched. Odie saw it. Nobody else will believe it. It is filed as a cyst.\n- **Before 3.** Bus crash; the ER overflows; the Chief throws Wren in.\n- **After 3.** Wren: what happened in there? Odie: \"You were fast. Don't make it weird.\"\n- **Before 4.** Gwen is back, in agony; her scar is moving. The Chief watches from the gallery.\n- **After 4.** The sample vanishes. Halcyon lawyers appear. The Chief suspends Wren. \"You saw a *twitch*, Doctor, at hour nineteen of a\n  shift. Get a second opinion. If you can find a fool to give one.\"\n- **Before 5.** Wren finds Sabine on the ship. Sabine: \"Everyone agreed I was wrong. That is what consensus feels like from the inside.\"\n  A stevedore collapses on deck.\n- **After 5.** The two compare samples. Sabine: \"I'm not a doctor anymore, Dr. Tolliver. I am a second opinion.\"\n- **Before 6.** The Chief collapses at a board meeting and pulls his collar open: his own graft scar.\n- **After 6.** His confession, from the bed: \"I signed the trial. I signed them all.\" He gives them the trial files, and access to the Gala.\n- **Before 7.** Halcyon's gala in the new wing, paid for by Halcyon. Voss on the big screen. Donors begin to fall.\n- **Before 8.** Voss himself is wheeled in: his own product. Odie, quietly: \"We could be slow, Doctor. Nobody would know.\" Wren: \"I\n  would.\"\n- **After 8.** Voss wakes in handcuffs. \"You saved me. That's the one thing I could never have sold.\" Montage of postcards.\n  Then a last beat: a shipping manifest, a crate of grafts already at sea. **\"CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN.\"** Credits. Free Surgery unlocks.\n\n**Writing style.** Earnest, overheated medical thriller. Short, punchy lines; jargon always explained at once; big speeches about duty;\ndramatic reversals; a nurse who is always right. Comedy comes from everyone taking this completely seriously. Two lines per box at\nmost. In operations, lines are one short sentence and never pause play.\n\nLines to set the voice:\n\n> ODIE: \"Scalpel. No, the other end, Doctor.\"\n> WREN: \"I think I've got it.\" CHIEF: \"In my operating room, 'I think' is a cause of death!\"\n> ODIE: \"Vitals sixty and falling. Stitch that, or I start calling relatives.\"\n> VOSS, on TV: \"Pain is just a feeling you haven't paid to remove yet.\"\n> SABINE: \"Your hands are shaking.\" WREN: \"They've never shaken.\" SABINE: \"Then that's new. Use it.\"\n> WREN, to a patient under anaesthetic: \"Sorry. Sorry. Nearly done. Sorry.\"\n> ODIE, at a TEXTBOOK chain: \"Careful, Doctor. People will start to expect it.\"\n\n**Drama Cut.** The game's visual signature, used 6 to 10 times in the story, on reveals. 0.8 s: the camera snaps to a face with a Dutch\ntilt, `post.combine` lays on `look:anime-action` speed lines and cel, the screen shakes, a stinger hits, and a huge caption slams in\n(\"IT MOVED.\"). Then it snaps back.\n\n**Postcards.** After each debrief, a card from the patient, with a line chosen by rank. S: \"Back on the trumpet. Played your name badly on\npurpose.\" C: \"They say I'll walk fine. They say you looked very worried.\" They collect in the Board's Postcards gallery.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Controls and screens\n\n**Pad (DualSense, or any pad in the standard mapping). This is the design target.**\n\n| Input | Action | Engine code |\n|---|---|---|\n| Left stick | Cursor | read directly (§17.4) |\n| R2 or Cross | Use tool (hold) | `PadRightTrigger`, `PadSouth` |\n| Right stick | Radial: push to open, aim at a tool, release to equip. Field time ×0.6 while open | `PadRightStick*` |\n| L1 / R1 | Previous / next tool | `PadLeftShoulder`, `PadRightShoulder` |\n| L2 | Precision: cursor ×0.4, stronger magnet, slight dolly-in | `PadLeftTrigger` |\n| Triangle | Gift (and the pulse-lock beats) | `PadNorth` |\n| Square | Quick Syringe | `PadWest` |\n| Circle | Drop what forceps hold; cancel the radial | `PadEast` |\n| D-pad left/right | Switch site | `PadLeft`, `PadRight` |\n| D-pad up | Hint | `PadUp` |\n| R3 | Swap surgeon (Cases 6 to 8) | `PadRightStick` |\n| Options | Pause | `PadStart` |\n| L2 + R2 | Paddles, in a Code | triggers |\n\nMenus: D-pad or left stick, Cross accepts, Circle goes back. Both sticks and triggers are analog; use dead zones. In a hub session, ignore\nOptions while Create is held (that chord belongs to the hub).\n\n**Mouse and keyboard. The same game and screens, but native.**\n\n- **Mouse** moves the cursor absolutely, 1:1, no pointer lock, with the OS cursor hidden over the field. LMB uses the tool. **Hold RMB** for the\n  radial at the cursor, flick and release. Wheel cycles tools. Keys **1–8** pick tools directly. The tool bar, site tabs and Board cards are clickable, and hovering a valid target highlights it. Shift: precision. Space:\n  Gift. F: quick Syringe. R: drop. Q/E: sites. H: hint. Tab: swap. Esc: pause. LMB + RMB: paddles.\n- **Keyboard-only** still works: WASD or arrows move the cursor, Enter uses the tool.\n- Every menu: hover moves focus, click picks (`createMenu` already does this; do the same in custom panels). Rebinding in Settings → Controls.\n\n**Cursor feel on a pad (page-side, tune these).** Speed = `cursorSpeed × lean^2.2`. Within 0.6 m of a valid target for the current tool: velocity ×0.55 and a\ngentle pull (the magnet). On a scalpel guide while cutting: the across-line part of stick input ×0.4 (rail assist). Suturing on a wound: a soft clamp\nto ±0.8 m of the wound (sew assist), so you just weave. Mouse gets a light version only, at 0.2 of these strengths.\n\n**Prompts** follow the device used last (`input.lastDevice`). Draw your own glyph set in code (SVG/CSS): PlayStation shapes by default for **any** pad; **Settings →\nControls → Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox** swaps to A B X Y and LB RB LT RT. Don't use `input.prompt()` text directly, as it reads Xbox for unknown pads. Keyboard","numLines":180,"startLine":200,"totalLines":865}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018a1RwqCeYP1WiEfRFhSs6m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
