{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L3FgYVk6nzXDuuxbjwV9va","type":"tool_result","content":"380\tshows keycaps; mouse shows mouse icons.\n381\t\n382\t**10-foot rules.** Judge every screen at 1920×1080 from a screenshot. Body text at least 32 px; instruments and menu items at least 64 px tall; thick outlines on guides\n383\tand cursor; focus state huge. One idea per screen. No tables, scrolling lists of small rows, or web-style forms.\n384\t\n385\t**In-operation HUD (at most these).** Vitals and ECG, top left, big. Clock and phase name, top centre. Score and chain, top right. Tool bar, bottom centre: 8 icons\n386\tat 72–96 px, current raised. Odie's line, bottom left: name, big caption, no input needed (`createDialog` with `modal: false` and `auto`). Site tabs at the edges. World labels\n387\tfor ratings (`ui.label`), huge and brief.\n388\t\n389\t**Screens.**\n390\t\n391\t- **Boot/Loading:** dark, lighthouse beam, status text; the engine error text stays visible if startup fails. With no WebGPU (the engine has no fallback), show a large plain message saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, with `AIHub.fail` in a session.\n392\t- **Title:** 3D lamp-lit OR with the lighthouse beam through rain on the window; the title; Continue / New Shift / The Board / Scrub In / Settings / About. Attract after 10 s idle (§14).\n393\t- **The Board:** a corkboard wall. One big case card at a time, left/right to browse: patient, one line, rank, tools as icons. Postcards tab.\n394\t- **Story:** full 3D scene, dialogue box along the bottom third, name plate, gibberish voice; Cross advances; hold Circle to skip the scene; auto mode in Settings.\n395\t- **Briefing:** patient card and one sentence, tools needed, difficulty, Start.\n396\t- **Pause:** Resume, Retry phase, Retry case, Settings, Controls, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Board.\n397\t- **Settings:** pages with few big rows. Audio (Master 70%, **Music 10%**, Effects 100%, Voice 100%). Controls (glyphs, cursor speed, aim assist, rebinding, hold vs toggle for use). Gameplay\n398\t  (difficulty, Simple Gift, hints, text speed, auto-advance). Display (blood colour: red / teal / off, reduce flashes, text size).\n399\t- **Scrub In:** four big seat slots; each device claims one by pressing its accept; Start.\n400\t- **About/Credits:** see §21. Paged cards, one question per card.\n401\t\n402\t**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` false and no pad seen. No touch controls: put `touch=off` in the `search` you give `createEngine`, always, or the engine shows its touch layer (tested on a phone profile: `touch=off` removes it all). Show exactly **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a large settings button that opens Settings, which accepts taps. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad or\n403\tkey arriving on such a device clears the message.\n404\t\n405\t---\n406\t\n407\t## 11. Art direction\n408\t\n409\t**Base: the engine's native style.** Everything is procedural shapes from the geometry kit, materials and textures as data, puppet bodies from the body grammar. Draw like the engine's clean playground look\n410\t(see `labs/playground/looks/clean.ts`): full resolution, smooth textures, edge smoothing. Do **not** use the chunky default `pixels` resolution: thin surgical lines must read at 10 feet. Set `resolution: 'full'` and\n411\t`textures: 'smooth'` in your looks.\n412\t\n413\t**Looks** (`defineLook`, in `labs/game/view/looks.ts`).\n414\t\n415\t- `look:harbor` for story: clean, soft `ao`, `aa`, a thin `outline` on characters only, warm-teal `grade`, gentle `bloom`.\n416\t- `look:field` for operations: `style: 'pbr'` for wet highlights, `ao`, `bloom`, `aa`; performance is unlimited, so add `ssr` if it helps the wetness.\n417\t- Transient overlays through `post.combine`: Stillpoint (teal, desaturated, vignette), Second Pulse (amber, `speedlines`), low vitals (red vignette), Drama Cut.\n418\t\n419\t**Detail.** TASK.md's performance budget is unlimited, and FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope. Add as much geometry, effects, lights and shadows as a scene needs.\n420\t\n421\t**Palette.** Harbor Light: sea-glass teal walls, brass fittings, amber lamps, rain-blue windows. The field: cherry, salmon, ochre and plum tissue, deliberately stylised and glossy; deep teal drapes around it.\n422\tEach strain has its own colour that never collides with tissue: lilac, amber, ink-blue, pearl, white-gold. Guides and the cursor: bright cyan with a dark outline. Keep blood dark cherry; the option recolours it.\n423\t\n424\t**The operating field (the showpiece).** Built as live meshes the page rewrites each frame, tested as described in §17.3.\n425\t\n426\t- **Sheet:** a dense grid (start at 320 × 192; performance is out of scope) per site. Height = breath + heartbeat + organ bulges (ellipses from data) + raised vessels (polylines) + wound lips + Reverie's ripple. Vertex colours: organ regions, veins, bruising, numb patches, burns, Balm.\n427\t- **Thin-things buffers,** one live mesh per material: wet red (incision interiors, pools with wobbling edges), thread, steel and glove (hands and tools, transformed in software from templates), transparent gel and lacquer. Each has a fixed capacity.\n428\t- **Texture:** one `defineTexture` wet-cell pattern with a height channel, for the normal map on the sheet.\n429\t- **Around it:** drapes and clamps as ordinary props, framing the window; the surgical lamp's warm white light; visible shadow of your own hand on the tissue.\n430\t- **Hands:** a gloved right hand with the tool, following the cursor with spring lag and a tremble that grows as vitals fall. In co-op, gloves tinted by seat.\n431\t\n432\t**Parasites:** engine rigs where they fit (`crowdBody` blob with its features, and floater with its motes), so they squash, look and hop natively. Reverie and Balm live in the sheet.\n433\t\n434\t**Characters** (`labs/game/view/bodies/`, `defineBody` on the humanoid skeleton). A custom build, `build:drama`, on `build:adult` proportions with heads about 25% larger for readable faces at 10 feet. Hair from several parts for a strong silhouette per character. Mask, cap and gown variants for the OR. Faces through `Blink`, `LookAt` and glow eye parts.\n435\t\n436\t**Sets as prop lists** (`labs/game/data/sets/`): OR (real scale), ward, Chief's office, ship's clinic, gala hall, corridor. Walls and floors are large box props with generated tiles. The engine's library is fine for generic props; make new props for what sells the hospital: operating table, surgical lamp, IV stand, heart monitor (with a live ECG), instrument tray, gurney, corkboard, TV (playing the Halcyon ad), trumpet.\n437\t\n438\t**Effects** (`defineEmitter`): blood squirt, goo, laser smoke and sparks, gel shine, stitch snap, rain on windows, sleepy motes.\n439\t\n440\t---\n441\t\n442\t## 12. Animation\n443\t\n444\t**Base:** the engine's animator, actions and clip library. `node x anim find <words>` searches 1,218 readable clips; `node x new action` writes a multi-beat action from a template; bundle only the clip sets you use (see `labs/box/library.ts`).\n445\t\n446\t**Story actors** are `spawnActor` with their `body` and `anim: { build }`, not player-controlled; they play actions with `actOn` and clips with `playClip`.\n447\t\n448\t**New actions** (`labs/game/cast/actions/`), each checked with `actionCheck`: scrub hands, mask up, hand over instrument, clipboard slam, point accusingly, hands on desk (loom), collar open (reveal), collapse, despair on knees, adjust glasses, moustache rage, TV-host smile and gesture, trumpet raise, salute with scalpel, exhale in relief, double fist on the operating table.\n449\t\n450\t**Field animation (page-side, springs from the API):** tool swings, needle arcs, stitch pull-tight, heart beats locked to the ECG, breathing, flap hinge, hand tremble, the slap of a tool handed over, tissue parting with lips along an incision, ripple under the sheet.\n451\t\n452\t**Camera moves:** lamp-to-field descent at operation start, pull-back on failure, site blends, parallax ±3° with the cursor, precision dolly-in, roll hazard tilt, Drama Cut, tilt under a raised flap.\n453\t\n454\t---\n455\t\n456\t## 13. Audio\n457\t\n458\t**Everything is written in code; no audio files, no `<audio>` tags, no data URLs of sound.** Effects and songs are `defineSfx` and `defineSong` data; the runtime is `createAudio`. Music defaults to 10%: `audio.volume('music', 0.10)` at start, and the Settings slider shows 10%. The engine's buses are `effects`, `music`, `ui`, `ambience`; there is no voice bus, so make your own `GainNode` from `audio.context` for voices.\n459\t\n460\t**Voices are gibberish**, Animalese/Simlish style, in `labs/game/audio/voice.ts`. At startup, render syllable buffers per character with an `OfflineAudioContext`: 16 syllables from a sawtooth through 2–3 formant filters plus a little noise. For each spoken character, play a syllable chosen by hashing the letter (the same line always sounds the same). Per character: base pitch, formant set, speed, breathiness. `?` rises, `!` is louder and higher, CAPS are louder, commas pause. Mercy's choir and Voss's jingle use the same engine, sung to notes.\n461\t\n462\t**Effects.** Every tool has a signature (cut: wet zip; stitch: tug-snip; drain: gurgling suction with pitch following pool size; laser: sizzle hum; syringe: glass tick; gel: squelch; scanner: sonar ping; forceps: click and pull; tool handover: clack). Monitor beep at the real heart rate, pitch falling with vitals; flat tone; alarm. Ratings have rising stingers. Each strain has its 3-note signature. Rain and ship creak as ambience.\n463\t\n464\t**Music (`defineSong`, with `intensity` layers driven by vitals and danger).** OR calm → OR tension → strain; Mercy's hymn (finale); story soft theme; title theme; Halcyon jingle (comic, played on TVs); success fanfare; failed motif. Energetic, operatic and synth-orchestral, original. Duck music under voices and key alarms.\n465\t\n466\t**Check by numbers.** Render effects with `node x audio sfx:<id>`; in a page, read levels from an `AnalyserNode` and confirm music is on at default volume but quiet.\n467\t\n468\t---\n469\t\n470\t## 14. Attract mode\n471\t\n472\tAfter **10 s with no input** on the title or any front-end menu (not in a rebind prompt): fade out and start the looping demo. **Any** input (key, mouse move or click, pad button, or stick past its dead zone) exits at once back to the title. Timer resets on any input.\n473\t\n474\tThe loop shows as much of the game as it can, about 3 minutes, each clip a real run driven by the bot with `game.attract=true` (cheats on: no failure, infinite Gift, the clock frozen when needed):\n475\t\n476\tTitle logo 6 s → Case 1 stitching → Case 3 site triage and Stillpoint → a story scene with a Drama Cut → Case 5 Solace splits under Second Pulse with the ship rolling → Case 6 Scanner and flap, with the AI colleague → Case 7 three tables → Case 8 Mercy's Code → postcards → loop.\n477\t\n478\tA \"DEMO\" banner and a large prompt to press a button. Save nothing during attract (`createStore` mode `demo`). On touch-only devices it just keeps running behind the message. Never in a hub session.\n479\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"97cc5d20-7bd1-4c7a-9b88-e2f2303c21ee","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:08:10.156Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work/PLAN.md","content":"shows keycaps; mouse shows mouse icons.\n\n**10-foot rules.** Judge every screen at 1920×1080 from a screenshot. Body text at least 32 px; instruments and menu items at least 64 px tall; thick outlines on guides\nand cursor; focus state huge. One idea per screen. No tables, scrolling lists of small rows, or web-style forms.\n\n**In-operation HUD (at most these).** Vitals and ECG, top left, big. Clock and phase name, top centre. Score and chain, top right. Tool bar, bottom centre: 8 icons\nat 72–96 px, current raised. Odie's line, bottom left: name, big caption, no input needed (`createDialog` with `modal: false` and `auto`). Site tabs at the edges. World labels\nfor ratings (`ui.label`), huge and brief.\n\n**Screens.**\n\n- **Boot/Loading:** dark, lighthouse beam, status text; the engine error text stays visible if startup fails. With no WebGPU (the engine has no fallback), show a large plain message saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, with `AIHub.fail` in a session.\n- **Title:** 3D lamp-lit OR with the lighthouse beam through rain on the window; the title; Continue / New Shift / The Board / Scrub In / Settings / About. Attract after 10 s idle (§14).\n- **The Board:** a corkboard wall. One big case card at a time, left/right to browse: patient, one line, rank, tools as icons. Postcards tab.\n- **Story:** full 3D scene, dialogue box along the bottom third, name plate, gibberish voice; Cross advances; hold Circle to skip the scene; auto mode in Settings.\n- **Briefing:** patient card and one sentence, tools needed, difficulty, Start.\n- **Pause:** Resume, Retry phase, Retry case, Settings, Controls, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Board.\n- **Settings:** pages with few big rows. Audio (Master 70%, **Music 10%**, Effects 100%, Voice 100%). Controls (glyphs, cursor speed, aim assist, rebinding, hold vs toggle for use). Gameplay\n  (difficulty, Simple Gift, hints, text speed, auto-advance). Display (blood colour: red / teal / off, reduce flashes, text size).\n- **Scrub In:** four big seat slots; each device claims one by pressing its accept; Start.\n- **About/Credits:** see §21. Paged cards, one question per card.\n\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` false and no pad seen. No touch controls: put `touch=off` in the `search` you give `createEngine`, always, or the engine shows its touch layer (tested on a phone profile: `touch=off` removes it all). Show exactly **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a large settings button that opens Settings, which accepts taps. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad or\nkey arriving on such a device clears the message.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Art direction\n\n**Base: the engine's native style.** Everything is procedural shapes from the geometry kit, materials and textures as data, puppet bodies from the body grammar. Draw like the engine's clean playground look\n(see `labs/playground/looks/clean.ts`): full resolution, smooth textures, edge smoothing. Do **not** use the chunky default `pixels` resolution: thin surgical lines must read at 10 feet. Set `resolution: 'full'` and\n`textures: 'smooth'` in your looks.\n\n**Looks** (`defineLook`, in `labs/game/view/looks.ts`).\n\n- `look:harbor` for story: clean, soft `ao`, `aa`, a thin `outline` on characters only, warm-teal `grade`, gentle `bloom`.\n- `look:field` for operations: `style: 'pbr'` for wet highlights, `ao`, `bloom`, `aa`; performance is unlimited, so add `ssr` if it helps the wetness.\n- Transient overlays through `post.combine`: Stillpoint (teal, desaturated, vignette), Second Pulse (amber, `speedlines`), low vitals (red vignette), Drama Cut.\n\n**Detail.** TASK.md's performance budget is unlimited, and FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope. Add as much geometry, effects, lights and shadows as a scene needs.\n\n**Palette.** Harbor Light: sea-glass teal walls, brass fittings, amber lamps, rain-blue windows. The field: cherry, salmon, ochre and plum tissue, deliberately stylised and glossy; deep teal drapes around it.\nEach strain has its own colour that never collides with tissue: lilac, amber, ink-blue, pearl, white-gold. Guides and the cursor: bright cyan with a dark outline. Keep blood dark cherry; the option recolours it.\n\n**The operating field (the showpiece).** Built as live meshes the page rewrites each frame, tested as described in §17.3.\n\n- **Sheet:** a dense grid (start at 320 × 192; performance is out of scope) per site. Height = breath + heartbeat + organ bulges (ellipses from data) + raised vessels (polylines) + wound lips + Reverie's ripple. Vertex colours: organ regions, veins, bruising, numb patches, burns, Balm.\n- **Thin-things buffers,** one live mesh per material: wet red (incision interiors, pools with wobbling edges), thread, steel and glove (hands and tools, transformed in software from templates), transparent gel and lacquer. Each has a fixed capacity.\n- **Texture:** one `defineTexture` wet-cell pattern with a height channel, for the normal map on the sheet.\n- **Around it:** drapes and clamps as ordinary props, framing the window; the surgical lamp's warm white light; visible shadow of your own hand on the tissue.\n- **Hands:** a gloved right hand with the tool, following the cursor with spring lag and a tremble that grows as vitals fall. In co-op, gloves tinted by seat.\n\n**Parasites:** engine rigs where they fit (`crowdBody` blob with its features, and floater with its motes), so they squash, look and hop natively. Reverie and Balm live in the sheet.\n\n**Characters** (`labs/game/view/bodies/`, `defineBody` on the humanoid skeleton). A custom build, `build:drama`, on `build:adult` proportions with heads about 25% larger for readable faces at 10 feet. Hair from several parts for a strong silhouette per character. Mask, cap and gown variants for the OR. Faces through `Blink`, `LookAt` and glow eye parts.\n\n**Sets as prop lists** (`labs/game/data/sets/`): OR (real scale), ward, Chief's office, ship's clinic, gala hall, corridor. Walls and floors are large box props with generated tiles. The engine's library is fine for generic props; make new props for what sells the hospital: operating table, surgical lamp, IV stand, heart monitor (with a live ECG), instrument tray, gurney, corkboard, TV (playing the Halcyon ad), trumpet.\n\n**Effects** (`defineEmitter`): blood squirt, goo, laser smoke and sparks, gel shine, stitch snap, rain on windows, sleepy motes.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Animation\n\n**Base:** the engine's animator, actions and clip library. `node x anim find <words>` searches 1,218 readable clips; `node x new action` writes a multi-beat action from a template; bundle only the clip sets you use (see `labs/box/library.ts`).\n\n**Story actors** are `spawnActor` with their `body` and `anim: { build }`, not player-controlled; they play actions with `actOn` and clips with `playClip`.\n\n**New actions** (`labs/game/cast/actions/`), each checked with `actionCheck`: scrub hands, mask up, hand over instrument, clipboard slam, point accusingly, hands on desk (loom), collar open (reveal), collapse, despair on knees, adjust glasses, moustache rage, TV-host smile and gesture, trumpet raise, salute with scalpel, exhale in relief, double fist on the operating table.\n\n**Field animation (page-side, springs from the API):** tool swings, needle arcs, stitch pull-tight, heart beats locked to the ECG, breathing, flap hinge, hand tremble, the slap of a tool handed over, tissue parting with lips along an incision, ripple under the sheet.\n\n**Camera moves:** lamp-to-field descent at operation start, pull-back on failure, site blends, parallax ±3° with the cursor, precision dolly-in, roll hazard tilt, Drama Cut, tilt under a raised flap.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Audio\n\n**Everything is written in code; no audio files, no `<audio>` tags, no data URLs of sound.** Effects and songs are `defineSfx` and `defineSong` data; the runtime is `createAudio`. Music defaults to 10%: `audio.volume('music', 0.10)` at start, and the Settings slider shows 10%. The engine's buses are `effects`, `music`, `ui`, `ambience`; there is no voice bus, so make your own `GainNode` from `audio.context` for voices.\n\n**Voices are gibberish**, Animalese/Simlish style, in `labs/game/audio/voice.ts`. At startup, render syllable buffers per character with an `OfflineAudioContext`: 16 syllables from a sawtooth through 2–3 formant filters plus a little noise. For each spoken character, play a syllable chosen by hashing the letter (the same line always sounds the same). Per character: base pitch, formant set, speed, breathiness. `?` rises, `!` is louder and higher, CAPS are louder, commas pause. Mercy's choir and Voss's jingle use the same engine, sung to notes.\n\n**Effects.** Every tool has a signature (cut: wet zip; stitch: tug-snip; drain: gurgling suction with pitch following pool size; laser: sizzle hum; syringe: glass tick; gel: squelch; scanner: sonar ping; forceps: click and pull; tool handover: clack). Monitor beep at the real heart rate, pitch falling with vitals; flat tone; alarm. Ratings have rising stingers. Each strain has its 3-note signature. Rain and ship creak as ambience.\n\n**Music (`defineSong`, with `intensity` layers driven by vitals and danger).** OR calm → OR tension → strain; Mercy's hymn (finale); story soft theme; title theme; Halcyon jingle (comic, played on TVs); success fanfare; failed motif. Energetic, operatic and synth-orchestral, original. Duck music under voices and key alarms.\n\n**Check by numbers.** Render effects with `node x audio sfx:<id>`; in a page, read levels from an `AnalyserNode` and confirm music is on at default volume but quiet.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 s with no input** on the title or any front-end menu (not in a rebind prompt): fade out and start the looping demo. **Any** input (key, mouse move or click, pad button, or stick past its dead zone) exits at once back to the title. Timer resets on any input.\n\nThe loop shows as much of the game as it can, about 3 minutes, each clip a real run driven by the bot with `game.attract=true` (cheats on: no failure, infinite Gift, the clock frozen when needed):\n\nTitle logo 6 s → Case 1 stitching → Case 3 site triage and Stillpoint → a story scene with a Drama Cut → Case 5 Solace splits under Second Pulse with the ship rolling → Case 6 Scanner and flap, with the AI colleague → Case 7 three tables → Case 8 Mercy's Code → postcards → loop.\n\nA \"DEMO\" banner and a large prompt to press a button. Save nothing during attract (`createStore` mode `demo`). On touch-only devices it just keeps running behind the message. Never in a hub session.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":380,"totalLines":865}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L3FgYVk6nzXDuuxbjwV9va","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
