{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCmYijY31eMpUY1KNjK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` and `planner-exit-interview.json` are both written, and the plan covers everything in TASK.md, with a table at the end mapping each requirement to its section. The exit interview parses as valid JSON with all four questions, and nothing is committed.\n\n## The game in the plan\nIt's a 3D surgical action game with story scenes told like a visual novel. The camera looks down from first person at live, deforming tissue, and story scenes use staged cameras.\n\n- **Story:** in a storm-battered port city, a beloved miracle graft turns out to be alive. The parasites have soft spa-brand names: Lull, Solace, Reverie, Balm and Mercy.\n- **Play:** there are eight instruments, two surgeons with opposite gifts, and eight cases that each add a new rule, plus Free Surgery.\n- **Original content:** cast, plot and strains are all new, with a list of source names builders must never use. The title is left to each builder.\n- **Multiplayer:** up to four surgeons can work on one patient through AI Hub, or on one TV as couch co-op. I read \"on its own\" as \"runs normally, plus couch co-op\"; the plan says so, because TASK.md's sentence is ambiguous.\n\nThe plan also covers controls, attract mode, dev mode with live sliders, audio, testing, build order and a done list.\n\n## What I tested\nI built a throwaway game on the real engine (`my-3dge@e7a1243`) to check the riskiest parts, then deleted it.\n\n**Worked:**\n- Tissue that deforms live, using only the engine's public API (40,000 vertices rewritten every frame).\n- A one-file 6.7 MB build that runs from `file://`.\n- Switching cases without reloading the page.\n- `touch=off`, which removes all touch controls on a phone profile.\n- A small netcode prototype in the real hub harness. All four harness runs passed, and client hashes always matched the host's, including with 4 players at 150 ms latency and 5% loss.\n\n**Not tested** (the plan tells builders to prove these early):\n- The game's own pre-round card in the harness\n- A custom camera mode in play\n- Transparent live meshes\n- More than 40,000 vertices\n- Whether the lighting follows the current set the way the plan assumes\n\n## Problems builders would have hit\nThe plan warns about all of these, but they're also worth fixing on your side:\n- **Long `TMPDIR`:** the run's path is too long for a Unix socket. Chromium dies with \"Socket path too long\", `tsx` fails with `EINVAL`, and `node x shot` hung until a 4m40s timeout killed it. The only fix I found is a short folder under `/tmp`, which breaks TASK.md's rule against `/tmp`, so the plan states it as an exception.\n- **Hub query keys:** the hub opens games with `?aihub=1…`, and the engine treats unknown query keys as settings and won't start.\n- **Hub timing:** the hub allows 10 s for hello, and the harness waits only 20 s for ready, while GPU warm-up in software reached 21 s. The plan includes a boot order that passed.\n- **Setup instructions:** `scripts/setup.sh` downloads Chrome and Node, but TASK.md says the browsers are already there. `CHROMIUM_PATH` plus `npm ci` is enough.\n- **Missing folder:** the engine guide cites `labs/playground/`, which games don't receive.\n\nI also removed the 5.7 GB of scratch clones and the temp files from my runs, and stopped my test server.\n\nSources:\n- [Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion)\n- [Trauma Center: Under the Knife (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Under_the_Knife)\n- [my-3dge engine](https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge)\n- [AI Hub Session Protocol](https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":521164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962},"output_tokens":706,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"1323bfb8-b1df-4c5c-820c-79bde9818678","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:22.169Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCmYQtDy9LkRunhJfBY"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for.]: STAGE.md asks for PLAN.md to cover everything TASK.md asks for, including the Testing section, which requires one command that prints only failures and a count, and the Source Information/feedback/About screen. The transcript shows PLAN.md was written and has a mapping table, but the plan's own verify command (npm run verify) was never implemented or run, and the requirement list in the mapping is self-asserted rather than checked. The exit-interview file was written, but the stop condition is about PLAN.md. Whether PLAN.md fully meets TASK.md is a judgment, and the transcript contains claims of coverage without independent verification of each item."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"412a1fbc-8c7e-43c4-a747-f9cba17d1e88","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:33.055Z","isSynthetic":true}
