{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QR2oEmsXtLoXDt6KBCtr3P","type":"tool_result","content":"=== A. the run's real long TMPDIR, full\nverify: 8 passed, 0 failed\nexit 0\n=== B. failing test, lint error, failing browser check, long TMPDIR\nFAIL npm run check: x check: ok: 3 plugins: all pass | assets: ok, 2159 files, 0 binary (0 approved, 0 fonts) | engine: ok, my-3dge@e7a1243, 2135 files | evals: ok, 0 tasks | report: out/check/all/report.json | check: FAIL (eslint, prettier)\nFAIL a rule that is broken on purpose: AssertionError: expected 2 to be 3 // Object.is equality\nFAIL e2e: a failing browser check: expected the title screen, saw nothing\nverify: 9 passed, 3 failed\nexit 1\n=== C. the one-file build with a stripped note, and how no-WebGPU browsers behave\n6721164 bytes; external: [] note gone: true\nwebkit iPhone 14 {'gpu': False, 'ready': False, 'step': 'function', 'text': 'GFX_NO_WEBGPU: WebGPU is unavailable: this browser has no navigator.gpu\\nFix: open the page in a browser with WebGPU and hardware acceleration on (Chrome or Edge 113+, Safari 26+); headless, launch Chr', 'errs': ['GFX_NO_WEBGPU'], 'anyFine': False} pageerrors []\nfirefox  {'gpu': False, 'ready': False, 'step': 'undefined', 'text': 'APP_START: the page failed to start: TypeError: can\\'t access property \"VERTEX\", Js is undefined\\nFix: the console names the cause; node x shot labs/game reports it headless', 'errs': ['APP_START'], 'anyFine': True} pageerrors ['can\\'t access property \"VERTEX\", Js is undefined']","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41ecbf1a-95aa-45b3-a227-3833f8bfa7e2","uuid":"bf77ed80-e45e-45fa-ba8b-94d0636092f4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:03.955Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== A. the run's real long TMPDIR, full\nverify: 8 passed, 0 failed\nexit 0\n=== B. failing test, lint error, failing browser check, long TMPDIR\nFAIL npm run check: x check: ok: 3 plugins: all pass | assets: ok, 2159 files, 0 binary (0 approved, 0 fonts) | engine: ok, my-3dge@e7a1243, 2135 files | evals: ok, 0 tasks | report: out/check/all/report.json | check: FAIL (eslint, prettier)\nFAIL a rule that is broken on purpose: AssertionError: expected 2 to be 3 // Object.is equality\nFAIL e2e: a failing browser check: expected the title screen, saw nothing\nverify: 9 passed, 3 failed\nexit 1\n=== C. the one-file build with a stripped note, and how no-WebGPU browsers behave\n6721164 bytes; external: [] note gone: true\nwebkit iPhone 14 {'gpu': False, 'ready': False, 'step': 'function', 'text': 'GFX_NO_WEBGPU: WebGPU is unavailable: this browser has no navigator.gpu\\nFix: open the page in a browser with WebGPU and hardware acceleration on (Chrome or Edge 113+, Safari 26+); headless, launch Chr', 'errs': ['GFX_NO_WEBGPU'], 'anyFine': False} pageerrors []\nfirefox  {'gpu': False, 'ready': False, 'step': 'undefined', 'text': 'APP_START: the page failed to start: TypeError: can\\'t access property \"VERTEX\", Js is undefined\\nFix: the console names the cause; node x shot labs/game reports it headless', 'errs': ['APP_START'], 'anyFine': True} pageerrors ['can\\'t access property \"VERTEX\", Js is undefined']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QR2oEmsXtLoXDt6KBCtr3P","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
