{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDKDp5YL3nmhuSAraMf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YP5oHtaEcADC1xTe6Umqho","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211917__x554572/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:80]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"Details beyond that were not confirmed; this plan does not depend on them.\",\"Details beyond that were not confirmed; this plan does not depend on them. Any more research is your choice.\")\nrep(\"Use the engine's **full workspace, not the lean** single page: you want its headless tests, replays and `node x` tools.\",\"Use the engine's **full workspace, not the lean** single page: you want its headless tests, replays and `node x` tools. The engine stays read-only: add every system, art asset and animation on top of it, in `labs/game/`.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\n\np='planner-exit-interview.json'\nd=json.load(open(p,encoding='utf-8'))\nd[2]['answer']+=\" Checking coverage honestly was hard too. My first requirements table was only my own claim, and when I audited every TASK.md line against the plan, with that table excluded, it found 29 unmet items. Three were real design gaps: nothing showed players what they cannot do, there was no issue log to answer the Testing Feedback counts, and the catalogue suggestions were incomplete. Testing also showed my no-WebGPU message could never have appeared in Firefox.\"\nd[3]['answer']+=\" Numbering TASK.md's requirements would also help: they are mixed in with machine facts over about 110 lines, so neither a planner nor a builder can easily prove nothing was missed.\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nopen(p,'a').write('\\n')\nd=json.load(open(p,encoding='utf-8'))\nassert [x['question'] for x in d]==['What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','What would you change in this prompt?']\nassert all(set(x)=={'question','answer'} and x['answer'].strip() for x in d)\nprint('exit interview: valid JSON,',len(d),'questions in the order STAGE.md lists')\n\nplan=open('PLAN.md',encoding='utf-8').read()\nnever=plan[plan.index('**Never use, in any form:**'):plan.index('**Fix what reviewers disliked')]\nrest=plan.replace(never,'')\nterms=['Derek','Stiles','Angie','Thompson','Naomi','Kimishima','Nozomi','Weaver','Hope Hospital','Caduceus','Delphi','GUILT','Healing Touch','Kyriaki','Deftera','Triti','Tetarti','Pempti','Paraskevi','Savato','Bliss','Z-Cells','Blackwell','Hoffman']\nhits={t:len(re.findall(r'\\b'+re.escape(t)+r'\\b',rest)) for t in terms}\nprint('banned names outside the never-use list:',{k:v for k,v in hits.items() if v} or 'none')\nprint('TODO-like text in plan:',re.findall(r'\\b(TODO|TBD|FIXME|XXX)\\b',plan.replace('No TODOs','').replace('\"TODO\"','')) or 'none')\nblocks=plan.count('```')\nprint('code fences balanced:',blocks%2==0,'; verify skeleton present:', 'The one command, `npm run verify`' in plan,'; words:',len(plan.split()))\nEOF\ncd .scratch && python3 audit.py | grep -v '^ok ' ; echo \"audit exit: ${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"; python3 audit.py | grep -c '^ok '; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ns=open('audit.py',encoding='utf-8').read()\ninfo=re.search(r'INFO = \\{(.*?)\\n\\}',s,re.S).group(1)\ntask=open('../TASK.md',encoding='utf-8').read().split('\\n')\nprint('--- lines marked info, for reading:')\nfor m in re.finditer(r\"(\\d+):'([^']*)'\",info):\n    n=int(m.group(1))\n    if task[n-1].strip(): print(f'T{n:<3} [{m.group(2)[:34]:<34}] {task[n-1][:88]}')\nEOF","description":"Make the last fixes, rerun the audit, scan banned names, and list lines marked as info"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"c